{"id": "21", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Magellan of Virginia is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services. They administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. The site is also for providers, offering them resources like weekly Q&A sessions each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. where they can address their questions and issues. Additionally, they offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses, approved by organizations like the American Psychological Association and the Association of Social Work Boards.", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to administer behavioral health services for Medicaid and FAMIS program members. It ensures quality behavioral health services for Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partners with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve healthcare delivery quality and satisfaction, and hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. for providers to address questions and issues.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to administer behavioral health services for Medicaid and FAMIS program members. It ensures quality behavioral health services for Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partners with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve healthcare delivery quality and satisfaction, and hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. for providers to address questions and issues.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to administer behavioral health services for Medicaid and FAMIS program members. It ensures quality behavioral health services for Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partners with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve healthcare delivery quality and satisfaction, and hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. for providers to address questions and issues.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia provides provider Q&A sessions on Fridays, hosting a weekly call each Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. that is open to all providers to address their questions and issues.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia provides a weekly Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues, and continues until further notice.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider that administers services for Medicaid and FAMIS program members in Virginia. It ensures quality behavioral health services for Medicaid enrollees, partners with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve healthcare delivery and overall health and well-being of Virginians, and hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. to address provider questions and issues.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to administer behavioral health services for Medicaid and FAMIS program enrollees. It ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which are open to all providers.\"]", "time_sec": 30.505, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.42, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "22", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They ensure the delivery of quality behavioral health services to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and work towards improving the overall health and well-being of Virginians. They also offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses and host weekly Q&A sessions for providers to address their questions and issues.", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia provides a weekly Provider Q&A Session for all providers, held every Friday from 1:00 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. This call is open to address providers' questions and issues, and it will continue until further notice. The organization administers behavioral health services for Virginia Medicaid and FAMIS program enrollees, with a mission to ensure quality care and improve the health and well-being of Virginians through partnerships with members, providers, and stakeholders.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Magellan of Virginia provides a weekly Provider Q&A Session for all providers, held every Friday from 1:00 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. This call is open to address providers' questions and issues, and it will continue until further notice. The organization administers behavioral health services for Virginia Medicaid and FAMIS program enrollees, with a mission to ensure quality care and improve the health and well-being of Virginians through partnerships with members, providers, and stakeholders.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Magellan of Virginia provides a weekly Provider Q&A Session for all providers, held every Friday from 1:00 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. This call is open to address providers' questions and issues, and it will continue until further notice. The organization administers behavioral health services for Virginia Medicaid and FAMIS program enrollees, with a mission to ensure quality care and improve the health and well-being of Virginians through partnerships with members, providers, and stakeholders.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider administering services for Medicaid and FAMIS program members in Virginia, hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions every Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m., and is approved to offer CE clock hours/credits through the American Psychological Association (APA) and Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB) when indicated on course promotional material.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia provides provider Q&A Sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m., which are open to all providers to address their questions and issues.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues. This session is part of their ongoing support for behavioral health service providers in Virginia.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia is a Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve Virginia Medicaid enrollees. It hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., open to all providers to address questions and issues, continuing until further notice.\"]", "time_sec": 29.988, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "24", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nMagellan of Virginia does offer continuing education clock hours/credits for their e-learning courses. According to passage 1, Magellan is approved to offer CE clock hours/credits by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB).\n\nAdditionally, Magellan of Virginia has been selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. This is mentioned in passage 2.\n\nFinally, Magellan of Virginia offers a Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. for providers to address their questions and issues. This is mentioned in passage 3.", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly Provider Q&A Session on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly Provider Q&A Session on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly Provider Q&A Session on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia provides provider Q&A sessions every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which are open to all providers to address their questions and issues, and continues these weekly calls until further notice.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia is a Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve Medicaid and FAMIS program members. It administers behavioral health services for Virginia Medicaid enrollees, hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions (Fridays 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m.), and ensures quality behavioral health services for Virginians through partnerships with members, providers, and stakeholders.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia provides a weekly Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to administer behavioral health services for Medicaid and FAMIS program enrollees in Virginia. It ensures quality behavioral health services for Medicaid enrollees, partners with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve healthcare delivery, and hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. to address provider questions and issues.\"]", "time_sec": 27.494, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "26", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not mention anything about Magellan of Virginia's status as a provider or its relationship with other providers. Passage 1 discusses Magellan's ability to offer continuing education credits, while Passage 2 explains its role as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Passage 3 mentions a weekly call for providers to ask questions and address issues, but it does not provide information about Magellan's status as a provider. Therefore, I cannot answer the question based on the given passages.", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia provides a weekly Provider Q&A Session for all providers, held every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to address providers' questions and issues.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia is a Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve Medicaid and FAMIS program members. It ensures quality behavioral health services for Virginia Medicaid enrollees and hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. for all providers.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues.\"]", "time_sec": 22.056, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.39, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "27", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try to align the door latch with the hole in the strike plate. If the latch is misaligned, you can perform a lipstick test to see where the latch contacts the strike plate. If it contacts too high or too low, tighten all the door's hinge screws. You may also need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate. If this doesn't work, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it up until it comes loose and remove it. Replace the door stop back on the jamb, set back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "pred": "To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps based on the provided passages:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If the door won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n2. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well, then place it back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Use the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish to align the door stop.\n3. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\n\nAdditionally, if the door latch won't catch, tighten the hinges first, enlarge the strike plate hole, and move the strike plate. You can also perform a \"lipstick test\" to check for misalignment between the latch and the strike plate hole.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps based on the provided passages:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If the door won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n2. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well, then place it back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Use the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish to align the door stop.\\n3. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\\n\\nAdditionally, if the door latch won't catch, tighten the hinges first, enlarge the strike plate hole, and move the strike plate. You can also perform a \\\"lipstick test\\\" to check for misalignment between the latch and the strike plate hole.\", \"Answer: To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it up until it comes loose. Remove the chisel and the door stop on top, then place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Use the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where the door stop came off to align it. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. This should allow the door to shut and lock normally.\", \"Answer: To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and attempt to lock it. If the door won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it loose, then remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location, using the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish as a guide for alignment. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. This should allow the door to shut and lock normally. Additionally, check if the latch aligns with the strike plate hole; if not, tighten the door hinges, enlarge the strike plate hole, or move the strike plate to ensure proper alignment.\", \"Answer: To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it loose. Remove the door stop, set it back 1/4 inch from its original location, and nail it back on to ensure proper alignment. Additionally, check for misalignment of the latch and strike plate by performing a lipstick test or observing the latch's position. If the latch is too high or too low, tighten the door's hinge screws, enlarge the latch hole in the jamb, enlarge the strike plate hole, or move the strike plate to achieve proper alignment.\", \"Answer: To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry up until it comes loose, and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Place the door stop back on the jamb, set it back 1/4 inch from its original location, and nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. This should allow the door to shut and lock normally.\"]", "time_sec": 59.642, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.69, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "28", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps based on the given passages:\n1. Close the door and attempt to lock it.\n2. If it doesn't lock, open the door and use a chisel to tap and pry off the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Remove the top door stop as well.\n3. Place the door stop back on the jamb, aligning it 1/4 inch from its original location using the distinct line left behind.\n4. Nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on.\n5. If the latch still doesn't catch, tighten the hinges first.\n6. Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb if necessary.\n7. Enlarge the strike plate hole or move the strike plate if the latch doesn't align with it.\n8. Ensure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\nFollowing these steps should help fix the door lock issue.", "pred": "Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry up until it comes loose. Remove the chisel and use it to remove the door stop on top as well. Place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry up until it comes loose. Remove the chisel and use it to remove the door stop on top as well. Place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and 