{"id": "30", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to fix a door that won't lock:\n\nPassage 1 provides tips on how to repair stuck or frozen door locks, keys that don’t work, and latches that don’t latch. However, it does not specifically address the issue of a door that won't lock.\n\nPassage 2 provides instructions on how to fix a door that won't shut or lock properly by removing the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and aligning it back on. This method might work for doors that won't lock due to a misaligned door stop.\n\nPassage 3 provides additional troubleshooting steps for when a door latch won't catch due to misalignment with the strike plate. This passage suggests enlarging the latch hole in the jamb, tightening the hinges, and moving the strike plate to align with the latch.\n\nIn summary, there is no definitive solution in the provided passages to fix a door that won't lock directly. However, these passages provide general tips and troubleshooting steps that may help identify and resolve related issues such as misaligned door stops or latches. If the problem persists after trying these methods, it may be best to consult a professional locksmith or carpenter.", "pred": "To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps from the passages:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it loose, and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Place the door stop back on the jamb, set it back 1/4 inch from its original location, and nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. This should allow the door to shut and lock normally.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it loose, and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Place the door stop back on the jamb, set it back 1/4 inch from its original location, and nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. This should allow the door to shut and lock normally.\", \"Answer: Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it up until it comes loose, and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Place the door stop back on the jamb, set it back 1/4 inch from its original location, and nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. This should allow the door to shut and lock normally.\", \"Answer: To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps from the passages:  \\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won’t lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it loose. Remove the door stop, then replace it back on the jamb set 1/4 inch from its original location (using the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish as alignment).  \\n2. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. This adjustment should allow the door to shut and lock normally.  \\n3. If the door still won’t lock, check for latch misalignment with the strike plate hole. Tighten all hinge screws, then enlarge the latch hole in the jamb, enlarge the strike plate hole, or move the strike plate to align with the latch.  \\n\\nAnswer: Shut the door, remove and reset the door stop 1/4 inch from its original location, and adjust the strike plate or latch hole if misalignment persists.\", \"Answer: To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps from the passages:  \\n1. Shut the door and attempt to lock it. If it fails to lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.  \\n2. Pry up on the chisel until the door stop loosens and remove it.  \\n3. Use the chisel to remove the door stop from the top of the jamb.  \\n4. Reattach the door stop, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location (visible as a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish).  \\n5. Nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on. This adjustment should allow the door to shut and lock normally.  \\n\\nThe passage specifies this procedure for resolving lock issues related to misaligned door stops, which prevents proper locking.\", \"Answer: To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and attempt to lock it. If it still won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it loose. Remove the door stop, then set it back 1/4 inch from its original location on the jamb, aligning it with the distinct line left in the paint, stain, or varnish. Nail the door stop back on and test if the door now shuts and locks normally. If the issue persists, consider tightening the hinges, enlarging the latch hole in the jamb, or adjusting the strike plate position, as misalignment between the latch and strike plate hole can prevent the door from locking properly.\"]", "time_sec": 59.454, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 8.63, "GAVIE-Rel": 6.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
