{"id": "35", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "To cook pollock, first, preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Then, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Next, place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish flakes easily. If desired, you can also add cheese on top of the pollock fillets and bake for an additional 3 minutes to melt the cheese.", "pred": "To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the fillets with paprika and black pepper, place them on a baking sheet sprayed with butter flavored cooking spray, layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, and bake for about 15 minutes until the fish flakes easily. After baking, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return the fish to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the fillets with paprika and black pepper, place them on a baking sheet sprayed with butter flavored cooking spray, layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, and bake for about 15 minutes until the fish flakes easily. After baking, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return the fish to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the fillets with paprika and black pepper, place them on a baking sheet sprayed with butter flavored cooking spray, layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, and bake for about 15 minutes until the fish flakes easily. After baking, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return the fish to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt f