{"id": "50", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "gt": "A water pick, also known as a Waterpik, is a beneficial tool for oral care. It is designed to shoot a strong stream of water at the gum line to help eliminate germs and plaque that are tough to get rid of with a toothbrush. It can also help maintain overall body health. In comparison to flossing, using a water pick can be easier and leave your mouth feeling cleaner. It can also massage and stimulate soft tissue in the mouth, reducing the risk of gingivitis. It is especially useful in cleaning around the teeth and gums, removing food from areas that brushing cannot reach.", "pred": "A water pick helps maintain good oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque that are tough to remove with a toothbrush. It massages and stimulates soft tissue, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and cleans better around teeth and gums, reaching areas that brushing cannot access.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: A water pick helps maintain good oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque that are tough to remove with a toothbrush. It massages and stimulates soft tissue, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and cleans better around teeth and gums, reaching areas that brushing cannot access.", "cot": "[\"Answer: A water pick helps maintain good oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque that are tough to remove with a toothbrush. It massages and stimulates soft tissue, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and cleans better around teeth and gums, reaching areas that brushing cannot access.\", \"Answer: Benefits of a water pick include helping to keep teeth, gums, mouth, and overall body healthier by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque that are tough to remove with a toothbrush; it can massage and stimulate soft tissue to reduce the risk of gingivitis; and it cleans better around teeth and gums, removing food from areas brushing cannot access.\", \"Answer: Water picks help maintain good oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque that are tough to remove with a toothbrush. They massage and stimulate soft tissue in the mouth, reducing the risk of gingivitis. They also clean better around teeth and gums, removing food from areas that brushing cannot access.\", \"Answer: Water picks help maintain oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque, especially in areas a toothbrush can't reach. They massage and stimulate soft tissue to reduce gingivitis risk, clean better around teeth and gums, and remove food from inaccessible areas.\", \"Answer: Water picks help maintain oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque, especially in areas a toothbrush cannot reach. They massage and stimulate soft tissue, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and clean better around teeth and gums by removing food particles.\"]", "time_sec": 28.854, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.49, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
