{"id": "55", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "You can prevent birds from building nests on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch and the top of the porch if it has open rafters. This will block the birds from reaching spaces they often choose to build their nests. If you have a light fixture, you can also install bird netting over it, but make sure the netting is nonflammable and safe to use around light bulbs and doesn't entangle birds. Another method is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch, as this can scare birds away. Remember to move the plastic hawk periodically to prevent the birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting for light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting for light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "cot": "[\"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting for light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.\", \"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover the top of light fixtures (ensuring it doesn't entangle birds), or mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch and moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.\", \"Answer: To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, you can attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, ensuring the netting is nonflammable and safe around light bulbs if used near fixtures. Additionally, you can mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch and move it periodically to deter birds, as their sight can scare birds away. These methods help prevent nests, which can block ventilation, are made from flammable materials, and can transmit disease through droppings.\", \"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, ensuring the netting is nonflammable and safe for light fixtures if used there, and by mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch and moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it; additionally, you can use other products designed to scare birds away from your property.\", \"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, or mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch and moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.\"]", "time_sec": 37.486, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_th