{"id": "57", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "To prevent birds from building a nest on your porch, you can attach bird netting to the eves and top of your porch with staples. Additionally, you can install bird netting over your light fixture to deter birds from accessing it. Another option is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away. It's important to note that any product used to deter birds should be nonflammable and safe to use.", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting for light fixtures to block access, or mounting a plastic hawk near your porch and moving it periodically to deter birds.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting for light fixtures to block access, or mounting a plastic hawk near your porch and moving it periodically to deter birds.", "cot": "[\"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting for light fixtures to block access, or mounting a plastic hawk near your porch and moving it periodically to deter birds.\", \"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while movin