ers, using a nonflammable and safe netting for light fixtures to block access, or mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch and moving it periodically to scare birds away.\", \"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, ensuring the netting is nonflammable and safe for light fixtures, and by mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.\"]", "time_sec": 35.421, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.64, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "59", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun (Passage 1:4). This will prevent birds from reaching the areas they often choose to build their nests.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it (Passage 2:1). Choose a non-flammable netting that is safe to use around light bulbs, and ensure that it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds from the area (Passage 3:1). Move the plastic hawk periodically to avoid the birds becoming accustomed to it.\n\nPlease note that the effectiveness of these methods may vary depending on the type of birds and the location of your porch. If the above methods do not work, you may need to consider other solutions or consult with a professional for assistance.", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, ensuring the netting is nonflammable and safe for light fixtures if used there, and by periodically moving a plastic hawk mounted on or near your porch to deter birds from inhabiting the area.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, ensuring the netting is nonflammable and safe for light fixtures if used there, and by periodically moving a plastic hawk mounted on or near your porch to deter birds from inhabiting the area.", "cot": "[\"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest o