ght fixtures, and by mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch and moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it; additionally, you can use other products designed to scare birds away from your property.\", \"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun, or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters; using nonflammable bird netting over the top of light fixtures (ensuring it doesn't entangle birds); or mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch and moving it periodically to deter birds.\", \"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable netting that is safe around light bulbs and ensuring it is installed to avoid entangling birds; alternatively, you can mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch and move it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it, as these methods are designed to scare birds away from your property.\", \"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun, or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters. Additionally, install bird netting over the top of light fixtures, ensuring it is nonflammable and safe around light bulbs, and is installed to avoid entangling birds. Another method is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch and move it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.\", \"Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable netting that is safe around light bulbs to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch whi