y parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems, including the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs. The systems are listed as skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous, with the urinary and respiratory systems specifically described as working closely with all other systems.\", \"Answer: The body systems work together in interconnected ways to maintain normal function. The urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.\"]", "time_sec": 43.561, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.56, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "107", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "The Windward and Leeward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea. The Windward Islands are in the southeast and are exposed to the northeast trade winds, hence they receive more rain and are wetter. On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are located in the northwest and are away from the wind, making them drier.", "pred": "The difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands get more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the leeward islands are farther from shore, drier, and still receive some rain.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands get more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the leeward islands are farther from shore, drier, and still receive some rain.", "cot": "[\"Answer: The difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands get more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the leeward islands are farther from shore, drier, and still receive some rain.\", \"Answer: The Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds, receive more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind, receive less rain, are drier, and are the farthest from shore.\", \"Answer: The difference is that windward islands get more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while leeward islands are farther from shore, drier, and still receive some rain.\", \"Answer: The windward islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds, receive more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain closest to