{"id": "118", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the process for transferring water shares includes the following steps:\n\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n5. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, if necessary.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how water shares are transferred is: By following the steps outlined above, which include the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate, the new owner providing proof of ownership, and paying the required fees.", "pred": "Water shares are transferred by returning the assigned Water Stock Certificate, signing the back of the certificate, providing proof of ownership by the new owner, and paying a $75.00 fee to process the transfer.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Water shares are transferred by returning the assigned Water Stock Certificate, signing the back of the certificate, providing proof of ownership by the new owner, and paying a $75.00 fee to process the transfer.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Water shares are transferred by returning the assigned Water Stock Certificate, signing the back of the certificate, providing proof of ownership by the new owner, and paying a $75.00 fee to process the transfer.\", \"Answer: Water shares are transferred by returning the assigned Water Stock Certificate, signing the back of the certificate, providing proof of ownership, and paying a $75.00 fee to process the transfer, as outlined in the passages.\", \"Answer: Water shares are transferred by having the seller return the Water Stock Certificate assigned to them, signing the back of the certificate, and the new owner providing proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record. Additionally, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form. The document must be furnished by the Company, signed, and notarized.\", \"Answer: Water shares are transferred by returning the assigned Water Stock Certificate, signing the back of the certificate, providing proof of ownership by the new owner, paying a $75.00 fee to process the transfer, and having the document signed and notarized as furnished by the Company.\", \"Answer: Water shares are transferred by having the seller return the assigned Water Stock Certificate, sign the back of it, and provide proof of ownership. A new owner must also pay a $75.00 fee to process the transfer, and a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued. Additionally, an additional $75.00 fee is required when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, and the document must be signed and notarized.\"]", "time_sec": 28.545, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "119", "question": "teresa name meaning", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek, American, Italian, and Spanish origin. In Greek and American, it means 'Reap; from Therasia.' In Italian, it is interpreted as 'Harvester.' In Spanish, the name is associated with two popular saints, 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux.' The name is also thought to originate from the Greek “therizein” meaning “to harvest, harvester” or from the Greek “theros” meaning “summer”.", "pred": "The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek and \"Harvester\" in Italian. In Spanish, it refers to the names of two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux. The etymology of Teresa is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or from the Greek \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek and \"Harvester\" in Italian. In Spanish, it refers to the names of two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux. The etymology of Teresa is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or from the Greek \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "cot": "[\"Answer: The name Teresa means \\\"Reap\\\" in Greek and \\\"Harvester\\\" in Italian. In Spanish, it refers to the names of two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux. The etymology of Teresa is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek \\\"therizein\\\" meaning \\\"to harvest, harvester\\\" or from the Greek \\\"theros\\\" meaning \\\"summer\\\".\", \"Answer: The name Teresa has multiple meanings depending on its linguistic and cultural context. In Greek, the name Teresa (or Theresa) means \\\"Reap\\\" or \\\"Reaper,\\\" derived from \\\"Therasia\\\" or the Greek word \\\"therizein,\\\" meaning \\\"to harvest.\\\" In Italian, Teresa means \\\"Harvester.\\\" In Spanish, it is associated with the names of two popular saints, \\\"Teresa of Avila\\\" and \\\"Therese of Lisieux.\\\" The etymology of Teresa is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek \\\"therizein\\\" (to harvest) or \\\"theros\\\" (summer).\", \"Answer: The name Teresa has multiple meanings depending on the cultural context. In Greek, it means \\\"Reap\\\" or \\\"Reaper\\\" (from \\\"Therasia\\\"). In Italian, it means \\\"Harvester\\\". In Spanish, it refers to \\\"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'\\\". The etymology suggests it may come from the Greek \\\"therizein\\\" meaning \\\"to harvest\\\" or \\\"theros\\\" meaning \\\"summer\\\".\", \"Answer: The name Teresa means \\\"Reap\\\" in Greek, \\\"Harvester\\\" in Italian, and refers to the names of two popular saints in Spanish.\", \"Answer: The name Teresa means \\\"Reap\\\" in Greek (from Therasia), \\\"Harvester\\\" in Italian, and refers to \\\"two popular saints\\\" in Spanish, while also being linked to the Greek root \\\"therizein\\\" meaning \\\"to harvest\\\" or \\\"summer\\\" in etymology.\"]", "time_sec": 33.729, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
