ociated with the names of two popular saints, \\\"Teresa of Avila\\\" and \\\"Therese of Lisieux,\\\" in Spanish.\", \"Answer: The name Teresa means \\\"Reap\\\" in Greek and American contexts, derived from \\\"Therasia,\\\" and \\\"Harvester\\\" in Italian. In Spanish, it refers to \\\"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'.\\\" Etymologically, Teresa may come from the Greek \\\"therizein\\\" meaning \\\"to harvest, harvester\\\" or \\\"theros\\\" meaning \\\"summer.\\\"\", \"Answer: The name Teresa means \\\"Reap\\\" in Greek, \\\"Harvester\\\" in Italian, and refers to \\\"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'\\\" in Spanish.\"]", "time_sec": 30.113, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "124", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "To build a lean-to shed, start by preparing the site with a 4\" layer of compacted gravel. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4\" and set and level them according to the shed building plans. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". Assemble the floor and place it on the skids as indicated in the floor framing section of the plans. Check for squareness and anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. Cut two more 4 x 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids and, when the frame is square, toenail the floor joists to the skids. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. The size of the shed can be adjusted as needed.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel, cutting 4 x 4 skids to 70 2/4″, setting and leveling the skids, cutting 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4″ and six joists to 44 3/4″, assembling the floor frame, checking for square, anchoring the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles, cutting pressure-treated 4 by 4s to 6 feet for the skids, positioning the frame on the skids, toenailing the floor joists to the skids when square, attaching 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, and constructing the walls separately before raising them onto the frame. The shed shown is 6 feet long by 4 feet wide and can be expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet, with the framing for the floor requiring cutting two pressure-treated 2 by 4s to 6 feet for the rim joists.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel, cutting and leveling 4 x 4 skids to 70 2/4″, assembling the floor frame with two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4″ and six joists at 44 3/4″, and anchoring the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. Alternatively, using pressure-treated 4 by 4s for skids at 6 feet and attaching 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring to the frame are also methods described. The shed dimensions can be 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the ability to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\"]", "time_sec": 33.444, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "125", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the process of building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with compacted gravel, cutting and setting the 4 x 4 skids, cutting and assembling the floor with 2 x 6 rim joists and joists, anchoring the frame to the skids, attaching tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, constructing the walls separately, and raising them onto the frame.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel, cutting 4 x 4 skids to 70 2/4″, and assembling the floor frame with two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4″ and six joists at 44 3/4″, then anchoring the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. Alternatively, using pressure-treated 4 by 4s cut to 6 feet for skids, positioning the frame square, toenailing floor joists to the skids, attaching 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, and constructing walls separately before raising them onto the frame. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the option to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel, cutting 4 x 4 skids to 70 2/4″, and assembling the floor frame with two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4″ and six joists at 44 3/4″, then anchoring the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. Alternatively, using pressure-treated 4 by 4s cut to 6 feet for skids, positioning the frame square, toenailing floor joists to the skids, attaching 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, and constructing walls separately before raising them onto the frame. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the option to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel, cutting and leveling 4 x 4 skids to 70 2/4″, and assembling the floor frame using two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4″ and six joists at 44 3/4″. The frame is anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. Alternatively, the skids can be made from two pressure-treated 4 by 4s cut to 6 feet, with the frame positioned on them and floor joists toenailed to the skids after squaring. The floor is then covered with 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood, and walls are constructed separately before being raised onto the frame. The shed dimensions can be 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with expansions possible in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\", \"Answer: Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel, cutting and setting 4 x 4 skids, and assembling the floor frame with 2 x 6 rim joists and 44 3/4″ joists, then anchoring with joist clip angles. Alternatively, using pressure-treated 4 by 4s for 6-foot skids and 2 by 4s for rim joists, attaching 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, and constructing walls separately before raising them onto the frame. The shed shown is 6 feet long by 4 feet wide and can be expanded in 2 or 4-foot increments.\"]", "time_sec": 42.692, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 13.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "126", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site, cutting and assembling the skids, flooring, and walls. To prepare the site, a 4\" layer of compacted gravel is recommended. The skids are cut to 70 2/4\" and set and leveled according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are cut at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". The floor is assembled and set on the skids, checked for square, and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. Pressure-treated 4 by 4s are used for the skids, while 2 by 4s are used for the rim joists and flooring. 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood is attached to the frame for the flooring.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer:Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel, cutting 4 x 4 skids to 70 2/4″, setting and leveling the skids, cutting 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4″ and six joists to 44 3/4″, assembling the floor frame, checking for square, anchoring with four joist clip angles, attaching 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, constructing walls separately and raising them onto the frame, and noting the shed can be 6 feet long by 4 feet wide with expandable dimensions in 2 or 4-foot increments.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 17.304, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval