or compounds where the parts retain their own identity and can be separated by physical means, with variable composition and properties of constituent substances.\", \"Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances composed of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.\", \"Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, while compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components retain their own identity and can be separated by physical means, unlike compounds which require chemical methods for separation. Mixtures have variable composition and show the properties of their constituent substances, as stated in the passages.\", \"Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances composed of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts retain their own identity and can be separated by physical means, with a variable composition.\"]", "time_sec": 26.548, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "212", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Here are my answers to the question based on the provided passages:\n\nQ: What are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures?\nA: Based on the passages provided, here are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures:\n\nElements:\n\n* Are the purest form of a chemical substance (Passage 3)\n* Consist of only one type of atom with the same number of protons (Passage 3)\n\nCompounds:\n\n* Are substances composed of two or more different elements (Passage 3)\n* Are also pure substances (Passage 3)\n\nMixtures:\n\n* Contain two or more substances that are relatively easy to separate (Passage 1)\n* Have a variable composition (Passage 2)\n* Show the properties of their constituent substances (Passage 2)\n* Can be separated by physical means (Passage 2)", "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, meaning all atoms have the same number of protons. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together, forming a new substance with uniform composition. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where components are not chemically bonded, retain their individual identities, have variable composition, and can be separated by physical methods.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, meaning all atoms have the same number of protons. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together, forming a new substance with uniform composition. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where components are not chemically bonded, retain their individual identities, have variable composition, and can be separated by physical methods.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, meaning all atoms have the same number of protons. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together, forming a new substance with uniform composition. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where components are not chemically bonded, retain their individual identities, have variable composition, and can be separated by physical methods.\", \"Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds with variable composition, where components retain their identity and can be separated by physical methods.\", \"Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of one type of atom, compounds are pure substances made of two or more chemically bonded elements, and mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds with variable composition that can be separated by physical means.\", \"Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, with all atoms having the same number of protons. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated easily by physical means, with variable composition and properties of the constituent substances.\", \"Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated easily by physical means, with variable composition and properties of the constituent substances.\"]", "time_sec": 26.476, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 42.96, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "213", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are:\n\n* Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. They have a fixed composition and cannot be broken down into simpler substances by physical means.\n* Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded together. They have a fixed composition and are pure substances.\n* Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity. They have a variable composition and can be separated by physical means.\n\nTherefore, the key differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are their composition, bonding, and separability. Elements are homogeneous and have a fixed composition, compounds are heterogeneous and have a fixed composition, and mixtures are heterogeneous and have a variable composition. Additionally, elements and compounds are chemically bonded, while mixtures are not.", "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components retain their own identity and can be separated by physical means, with variable composition and properties of the constituent substances.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components retain their own identity and can be separated by physical means, with variable composition and properties of the constituent substances.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components retain their own identity and can be separated by physical means, with variable composition and properties of the constituent substances.\", \"Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.\", \"Answer: Elements are pure substances made of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances composed of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts retain their own identity and can be separated by physical means, with variable composition and properties of the constituent substances.\", \"Answer: Elements are pure substances made of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances composed of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts retain their own identity and can be separated by physical means.\", \"Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, compounds are pure substances made of two or more chemically bonded different elements, and mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where components retain their identity and can be separated by physical means.\"]", "time_sec": 24.013, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "214", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To properly wash wine glasses, you should scrub them by hand as it's the safest cleaning method. First, lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink and fill it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time, cradling the bowl to protect the stem. Use a small amount of mild detergent only on the bottom and rim of the glass. If stubborn residue remains, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, then rinse. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint‑free cloth such as microfiber or a flour sack towel.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink and fill it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time, cradling the bowl to protect the stem. Use a small amount of mild detergent only on the bottom and rim of the glass. If stubborn residue remains, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, then rinse. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint‑free cloth such as microfiber or a flour sack towel.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink and fill it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time, cradling the bowl to protect the stem. Use a small amount of mild detergent only on the bottom and rim of the glass. If stubborn residue remains, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, then rinse. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint‑free cloth such as microfiber or a flour sack towel.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, fill a sink with hot water and lay a towel at the bottom to prevent damage. Wash one glass at a time, using a small amount of mild detergent only on the bottom and rim to avoid soap residue affecting future wine. Gently scrub with a soft-foam stemware brush if needed, then rinse thoroughly with hot water. Dry the glasses using a smooth, lint-free cloth such as microfiber or a flour sack towel to prevent spots. If stubborn wine residue remains, dissolve baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and allow the soda to dissolve the residue.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, fill a sink with hot water and place a towel inside to prevent damage. Wash one glass at a time, using a small amount of mild detergent only on the bottom and rim of the glass while cradling the bowl. If stubborn wine residue remains after using hot water and mild detergent, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and allow the soda to dissolve the residue. Rinse thoroughly with hot water, then dry with a smooth lint-free cloth such as microfiber or a flour sack towel. Avoid leaving red wine in the glass overnight to prevent staining.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, using a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand to protect the stem. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, then rinse thoroughly. After rinsing, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth such as microfiber or a flour sack towel. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside, and ensure the glass is dried completely to prevent red wine stains, especially if left overnight.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage, cradling the bowl of the glass in one hand to protect the stem. Use a small amount of mild detergent, applying it only to the bottom of the glass and around the rim to prevent soap from flavoring your next glass of wine. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass, and ensure the glasses are dried completely to avoid stains, especially if red wine has been left overnight.\"]", "time_sec": 54.861, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "215", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To wash wine glasses properly, start by using hot water and mild detergent to clean the outside of the glass. If there are stubborn wine residues, use baking soda to dissolve them by mixing a small amount of soda with hot water and letting it sit in the glass for a few minutes. For cleaning the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. Rinse thoroughly with hot water and dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth. To avoid damage, wash one wine glass at a time, use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, and cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of mild detergent, applying it only to the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Gently cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. If stubborn wine residue remains, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes to dissolve the residue. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of mild detergent, applying it only to the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Gently cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. If stubborn wine residue remains, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes to dissolve the residue. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of mild detergent, applying it only to the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Gently cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. If stubborn wine residue remains, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes to dissolve the residue. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—specifically in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. If stubborn wine residue remains after using hot water and mild detergent, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and allow the soda to dissolve the residue. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of mild detergent, applying it only to the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink and fill it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, cradling the bowl in one hand. Use a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—specifically in the bottom and around the rim—to prevent soap residue from affecting future wine. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, allowing it to dissolve any adhered residue. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glass with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. Avoid leaving red wine in the glass overnight, as it can cause stains.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, fill a sink with hot water and lay a towel inside to prevent damage. Wash one glass at a time, using a small amount of detergent only in the bottom and around the rim to avoid soap residue. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles for the inside, and rinse thoroughly with hot water. Dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel, to prevent stains. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes before rinsing.\"]", "time_sec": 52.039, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.13, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "216", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly wash wine glasses:\n\n1. If hot water and mild detergent cannot remove wine residue, use baking soda to dissolve and loosen the adhesive residue (Passage 1).\n2. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles and rinse thoroughly with hot water (Passage 2).\n3. For hand cleaning, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage (Passage 3). Use a small amount of detergent and only in the bottom of the glass and around the rim to avoid flavoring future wine. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, using a small amount of mild detergent only in the bottom and around the rim to prevent soap from flavoring the next glass of wine. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. If stubborn wine residue remains after using hot water and mild detergent, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes before rinsing thoroughly. After rinsing, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, using a small amount of mild detergent only in the bottom and around the rim to prevent soap from flavoring the next glass of wine. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. If stubborn wine residue remains after using hot water and mild detergent, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes before rinsing thoroughly. After rinsing, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, using a small amount of mild detergent only in the bottom and around the rim to prevent soap from flavoring the next glass of wine. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. If stubborn wine residue remains after using hot water and mild detergent, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes before rinsing thoroughly. After rinsing, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, using a small amount of detergent only in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. After washing, rinse thoroughly with hot water and dry the glasses using a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. If stubborn wine residue remains, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and then rinse. This method helps prevent chips, spots, and soap residue that could flavor your next glass of wine.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, fill the sink with hot water and lay a towel in it to prevent damage. Wash one glass at a time, using a small amount of mild detergent only on the bottom and rim of the glass while cradling the bowl. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glass with a smooth lint-free cloth such as microfiber or a flour sack towel to avoid stains and spots.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, fill a sink with hot water and lay a towel in it to prevent damage. Wash one glass at a time, using a small amount of mild detergent only on the bottom and rim. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to scrub gently, rinse thoroughly with hot water, and dry with a smooth lint-free cloth like microfiber or a flour sack towel. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, then rinse. Avoid leaving red wine in the glass overnight to prevent stains.\", \"Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage, cradling the bowl of the glass in one hand to protect the stem. Use a small amount of mild detergent only where needed, such as in the bottom of the glass and around the rim, to prevent soap from flavoring your next glass of wine. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\"]", "time_sec": 52.524, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "221", "question": "how to peel potatoes fast", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to peel potatoes fast:\n\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n2. Boil the potatoes for about 15 minutes.\n3. Place the potatoes in a bowl of ice water and swish them around for a few seconds.\n4. Remove the potatoes from the water and remove the skin.\n\nAlternatively, you can also try the following method:\n\n1. Cut the potato skin, making a cut all around the potato lengthwise.\n2. Boil the potato in a pot of boiling water.\n3. Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds.\n4. Rub the potato with both hands, and the skin should fall right off.\n\nThese methods should help you peel potatoes quickly and efficiently.", "pred": "To peel potatoes fast, follow these steps: 1) Cut the potato skin lengthwise, slicing only the skin. 2) Boil the potato in a pot of water for about 15 minutes. 3) Cool it off by plunging the potato in ice water for 10 seconds, which causes the surface to shrink. 4) Remove the skin by rubbing the potato with both hands, allowing the skin to fall off easily.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To peel potatoes fast, follow these steps: 1) Cut the potato skin lengthwise, slicing only the skin. 2) Boil the potato in a pot of water for about 15 minutes. 3) Cool it off by plunging the potato in ice water for 10 seconds, which causes the surface to shrink. 4) Remove the skin by rubbing the potato with both hands, allowing the skin to fall off easily.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To peel potatoes fast, follow these steps: 1) Cut the potato skin lengthwise, slicing only the skin. 2) Boil the potato in a pot of water for about 15 minutes. 3) Cool it off by plunging the potato in ice water for 10 seconds, which causes the surface to shrink. 4) Remove the skin by rubbing the potato with both hands, allowing the skin to fall off easily.\", \"Answer: To peel potatoes fast, follow these steps based on the passages: 1) Score the whole, unpeeled potato all the way around the center with a knife. 2) Boil the scored potato in a pot of water for about 15 minutes. 3) Immediately place the boiled potato in a bowl of ice water and swish it around for a few seconds to cool it. 4) Remove the potato from the ice water and peel the skin off, which will come off easily due to the skin shrinking from the cold. This method is faster than peeling raw potatoes, as mentioned in passage 2 (\\\"the easiest way I’ve discovered to peel a cooked potato\\\"). Passage 3 also supports this by stating that plunging the potato in ice water for 10 seconds causes the skin to shrink, making it easy to rub off with hands.\", \"Answer: To peel potatoes fast, follow these steps: 1) Cut the potato skin lengthwise all around the potato, slicing only the skin. 2) Boil the potato in a pot of water for about 15 minutes. 3) Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds to cool it and make the skin shrink. 4) Rub the potato with both hands to remove the skin easily. This method, as described in the passages, helps release the skin from the flesh and makes peeling quicker and easier, especially when dealing with a large quantity of potatoes.\", \"Answer: To peel potatoes fast, follow these steps: 1) Cut the potato skin lengthwise, slicing only the skin. 2) Boil the potato in a pot of water for about 15 minutes. 3) Cool it off by plunging the potato in ice water for 10 seconds, which causes the surface to shrink. 4) Remove the skin by rubbing the potato with both hands, allowing the skin to fall off easily.\", \"Answer: To peel potatoes fast, score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife, boil them for about 15 minutes, then plunge them into ice water for 10 seconds to cool and cause the skin to shrink. Finally, rub the potato with both hands to easily remove the skin.\"]", "time_sec": 43.075, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.96, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "223", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, to fix a lift valve in a toilet, you should follow these steps:\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain.\n4. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n5. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n6. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm closest to the edge.\n8. Use pliers to securely fasten the chain.\n9. Turn the water valve back on.\n10. Test the flush of the toilet and adjust the chain if needed.\n\nNote: The given passages provide step-by-step instructions for fixing a lift valve in a toilet.", "pred": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve (Step 1). Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any broken lift chain remnants (Step 2). Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, securing it tightly if a screw is included (Step 3). Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm (the hole closest to the edge) and fasten it securely with pliers (Step 3). Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links to make it tighter (Step 4). Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve (Step 1). Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any broken lift chain remnants (Step 2). Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, securing it tightly if a screw is included (Step 3). Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm (the hole closest to the edge) and fasten it securely with pliers (Step 3). Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links to make it tighter (Step 4). Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve (Step 1). Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any broken lift chain remnants (Step 2). Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, securing it tightly if a screw is included (Step 3). Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm (the hole closest to the edge) and fasten it securely with pliers (Step 3). Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links to make it tighter (Step 4). Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps: Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any broken lift chain from the lift arm. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and screw it in tightly if included, until it is secure with no more give. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve to the toilet (Passage 1). Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any broken lift chain from the lift arm (Passage 1). Connect the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm (Passage 3). Ensure the chain is securely fastened using pliers (Passage 3). If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm (Passage 3). Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation (Passage 2). If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links (Passage 2) and cut off any excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled (Passage 2).\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve (Step 1 from passage 1). Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any broken lift chain from the lift arm (Step 2 from passage 1). Connect the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge (passage 3). Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it with a screw if included, ensuring it is tight with no give (passage 3). Open the water valve to fill the tank (Step 4 from passage 2), then flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links (passage 2), and cut off any excess chain to prevent tangling (passage 2). If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm (passage 3).\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any broken lift chain from the lift arm. Then, push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and screw in any included screw tightly. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\"]", "time_sec": 63.802, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 72.16, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "224", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Fill the tank by turning on the water valve and then flushing the toilet. Adjust the lift chain as needed by moving the metal clip up or down a few links. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n5. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. Make sure it is securely fastened.\n6. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If it flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm.", "pred": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the lift arm into the flush handle, securing it with a screw if included. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer:To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the lift arm into the flush handle, securing it with a screw if included. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm.", "cot": "[\"Answer:To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the lift arm into the flush handle, securing it with a screw if included. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any broken lift chain from the lift arm. Then, push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and, if included, screw in the screw tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is closest to the edge, and ensure it is securely fastened with pliers. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve (Step 1 from passage 1). Then remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any broken lift chain from the lift arm. After that, install the new flapper valve and chain. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation (Step 4 from passage 2). If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links and cut off the excess lift chain to prevent tangling. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, screw in the screw tightly if included, and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm (the hole closest to the edge) using pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush; if it flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm (passage 3).\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve (Step 1). Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm. Then, push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and screw in any included screw tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and take out any broken lift chain from the lift arm. Then, push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it tightly if a screw is included. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and ensure it is securely fastened using pliers. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\"]", "time_sec": 55.961, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "225", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet before starting the repair (Passage 1).\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms, and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm (Passage 1).\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If necessary, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links (Passage 2).\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm (Passage 3). Secure it using pliers to ensure it is tightly fastened.\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test the toilet's flush function. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm (Passage 3).\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages. The passages do not provide instructions on how to fix a specific issue with the lift valve, such as a stuck or leaking valve.", "pred": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve to the toilet. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and, if included, screw in the screw tightly until there is no more give and it is secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve to the toilet. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and, if included, screw in the screw tightly until there is no more give and it is secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve to the toilet. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and, if included, screw in the screw tightly until there is no more give and it is secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps based on the provided passages: First, shut off the water supply valve to the toilet (Step 1). Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm (Step 1). After that, push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and screw in any included screw tightly until there is no more give and it is secure (Step 3). Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened (Step 3). Turn the water valve back on and test the flush of the toilet (Step 4). If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm (Step 4). Additionally, when checking for correct operation, if needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links and cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled (Step 4).\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve (Step 1). Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm (Step 2). Connect the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and ensure it is securely fastened using pliers (Step 3). If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm. Finally, push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and screw it in tightly if included, then turn the water valve back on and test the toilet’s flush (Steps 4 and 3).\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps based on the passages: First, shut off the water supply valve to the toilet (passage 1). Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm (passage 1). Next, if necessary, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links, and cut off any excess chain to prevent tangling (passage 2). Additionally, push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, screw in any included screw tightly, and ensure it is secure (passage 3). Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm (the hole closest to the edge), use pliers to secure it, and turn the water valve back on (passage 3). Finally, test the flush and adjust the chain to make it tighter if the toilet flushes slowly (passage 3).\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it with a screw if included. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is closest to the edge, and ensure it is securely fastened with pliers. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\"]", "time_sec": 65.297, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.1, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "226", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve and any remaining pieces of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install the new flapper valve and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, making sure it is securely fastened.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to test for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the chain as needed to ensure a proper flush. Cut off any excess chain to prevent tangling.\n\nNote: If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "pred": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps: 1) Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet. 2) Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm. 3) Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm, and ensure it is securely fastened using pliers. 4) Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until there is no more give and it is secure. 5) Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps: 1) Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet. 2) Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm. 3) Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm, and ensure it is securely fastened using pliers. 4) Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until there is no more give and it is secure. 5) Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps: 1) Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet. 2) Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm. 3) Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm, and ensure it is securely fastened using pliers. 4) Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until there is no more give and it is secure. 5) Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it with a screw if included. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is closest to the edge, and ensure it is securely fastened using pliers. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps based on the provided passages:  \\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet (passage 1).  \\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm (passage 1).  \\n3. Connect the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm (the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm) and ensure it is securely fastened using pliers (passage 3).  \\n4. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle; if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until there is no more give and it is secure (passage 3).  \\n5. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation (passage 2).  \\n6. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm (passage 3).  \\n7. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling (passage 2).\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps based on the passages: First, shut off the water supply valve to the toilet (Passage 1). Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm (Passage 1). After that, push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it by screwing in the included screw tightly if present, ensuring there is no more give (Passage 3). Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened (Passage 3). Turn the water valve back on and test the flush of the toilet (Passage 3). If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm (Passage 3). Finally, open the water valve to fill the tank, flush the toilet to check for correct operation, and if needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links, then cut off the excess lift chain to prevent tangling (Passage 2).\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve (Step 1, Passage 1). Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm (Step 2, Passage 1). After installing the new flapper valve and chain, open the water valve to fill the tank (Step 4, Passage 2). Flush the toilet to check for correct operation; if needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links (Passage 2). Cut off excess lift chain to prevent tangling (Passage 2). Secure the lift arm by pushing the small solid end into the flush handle and screwing in any included screw tightly until secure (Passage 3). Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm (closest to the edge) and ensure it is securely fastened with pliers (Passage 3). Turn the water valve back on and test the flush; if it flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm (Passage 3).\"]", "time_sec": 76.146, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.41, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "227", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here's a brief answer on how to fix a lift valve in a toilet based on the given passages:\n\nTo fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain for a 1.6 gallon per flush toilet.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if necessary. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n6. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, screw it in tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\n8. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Connect the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and ensure it is securely fastened using pliers. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until there is no more give. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Connect the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and ensure it is securely fastened using pliers. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until there is no more give. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Connect the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and ensure it is securely fastened using pliers. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until there is no more give. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve (passage 1). Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any broken lift chain remnants from the lift arm (passage 1). Then, proceed to Step 4: open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation (passage 2). If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links to make it tighter on the lift arm (passage 2). Additionally, ensure the chain is securely fastened to the third hole on the lift arm, which is closest to the edge of the lift arm, and push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle until it is secure with no more give (passage 3). If a screw is included, screw it in tightly (passage 3). Finally, turn the water valve back on and test the flush of the toilet (passage 3).\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve (passage 1). Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm (passage 1). After replacing the flapper valve and chain, push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it by screwing in the included screw if present (passage 3). Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and ensure it is securely fastened with pliers (passage 3). Turn the water valve back on and test the flush (passage 3). If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm (passage 3). Finally, open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation, readjusting the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if needed, and cutting off excess chain to prevent tangling (passage 2).\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Next, connect the new chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and ensure it is securely fastened using pliers. If a screw is included, screw it in tightly and push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle until it is secure with no more give. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links, and cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\"]", "time_sec": 67.811, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "231", "question": "oil stain on concrete driveway", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question \"How do you remove oil stains from a concrete driveway?\"\n\nTo remove oil stains from a concrete driveway, you can use one of the following methods:\n\n1. Oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, and carburetor cleaner (as mentioned in Passage 1).\n2. A commercial-grade cleaner applied with a brush or broom, followed by scrubbing with a pressure washer (as described in Passage 3).\n\nBefore starting the cleaning process, it is recommended to wash away any dirt or debris from the affected area (Passage 2). Additionally, it is important to avoid using high-pressure hoses to clean the stain, as this can push the oil deeper into the pavement (Passage 2).\n\nIt is also noted that the size of the oil spill and the length of time the stain has been present will affect the method of removal (Passage 3). For small and stubborn stains, the poultice method may be effective (Passage 2).", "pred": "Oil stains on concrete driveways can be removed using various methods. These include using oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, or carburetor cleaner, as compared in a video. Other methods involve cleaning the area with water from a hose or bucket, avoiding high pressure hoses to prevent pushing oil deeper into the pavement, and using a poultice method for fresh or small stubborn stains. Additionally, commercial-grade cleaners can be applied, followed by scrubbing with a brush or broom, and then using a pressure washer with detergent while maintaining an even pace and consistent nozzle distance from the concrete surface to prevent streaking.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Oil stains on concrete driveways can be removed using various methods. These include using oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, or carburetor cleaner, as compared in a video. Other methods involve cleaning the area with water from a hose or bucket, avoiding high pressure hoses to prevent pushing oil deeper into the pavement, and using a poultice method for fresh or small stubborn stains. Additionally, commercial-grade cleaners can be applied, followed by scrubbing with a brush or broom, and then using a pressure washer with detergent while maintaining an even pace and consistent nozzle distance from the concrete surface to prevent streaking.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Oil stains on concrete driveways can be removed using various methods. These include using oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, or carburetor cleaner, as compared in a video. Other methods involve cleaning the area with water from a hose or bucket, avoiding high pressure hoses to prevent pushing oil deeper into the pavement, and using a poultice method for fresh or small stubborn stains. Additionally, commercial-grade cleaners can be applied, followed by scrubbing with a brush or broom, and then using a pressure washer with detergent while maintaining an even pace and consistent nozzle distance from the concrete surface to prevent streaking.\", \"Answer: Oil stains on a concrete driveway can be removed using several methods, including using oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, or carburetor cleaner as compared in a video, or by using a poultice method for fresh or small stubborn stains. It is also recommended to first clean the area with water from a hose or bucket, avoiding high pressure to prevent pushing the oil deeper into the pavement, and to apply a commercial-grade cleaner and scrub with a brush or broom before using a pressure washer with detergent, ensuring an even pace and consistent nozzle distance to avoid streaking.\", \"Answer: Oil stains on concrete driveways can be removed using various methods such as oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, carburetor cleaner, poultice method, commercial-grade cleaner, or pressure washing with detergent. It is important to wash off any dirt and debris before cleaning, avoid using a high pressure hose, and apply the cleaner evenly to prevent streaking. The size of the oil spill and the length of time the stain has had to set will determine the process for removal.\", \"Answer: Oil stains on concrete driveways can be removed using various methods, including oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, carburetor cleaner, poultice method, commercial-grade cleaners, and pressure washing with detergent. It is important to first wash off dirt and debris and avoid using a high-pressure hose to prevent pushing the oil deeper into the pavement. The size and age of the oil stain will determine the appropriate cleaning process.\", \"Answer: Oil stains on a concrete driveway can be removed using several methods. The passages mention comparing oven cleaner, Goop hand cleaner, and carburetor cleaner as options for removing oil stains. Additionally, for fresh or small stubborn stains, the poultice method is recommended. Before cleaning, it's advised to wash off any dirt and debris from the driveway, avoiding the use of a high-pressure hose to prevent pushing the oil deeper into the pavement. For larger or older stains, commercial-grade cleaners and a pressure washer with detergent can be used, ensuring even spraying and consistent nozzle distance to avoid streaking.\"]", "time_sec": 43.038, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.09, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "233", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September and the lowest is 50 degrees in December. The city gets 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January. Snowfall is non-existent. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year. The July high is around 69 degrees and the January low is 43. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, however, the pollution index is 61% worse.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 7.496, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "235", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "Average weather in Sausalito can vary depending on the time of year. For example, during September, the average temperature is 58 degrees Fahrenheit (15 degrees Celsius), while in January, it is only 43 degrees Fahrenheit (4 degrees Celsius). The most precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches. However, throughout the year, the number of days with measurable precipitation is 56, and there are an average of 256 sunny days.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 7.5, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "236", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be summarized as follows:\n\n* Temperature: The average temperature in Sausalito ranges from 50°F (December) to 58°F (September).\n* Precipitation: Sausalito receives an average of 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January (0 inches).\n* Air Quality Index: The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average.\n* Sunshine: Sausalito experiences 256 sunny days per year, with an average of 56 days with measurable precipitation.\n* Comfort Index: According to Sperling's comfort index, Sausalito has a score of 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable year-round climate.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages regarding the average weather in Sausalito during a specific month or time period.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 7.495, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 10.1, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "240", "question": "how do crab traps work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a crab trap is a large square metal cage with a system of nets inside that allows crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the top. To set the trap, the ends with lead-ins are placed in the water and the crabs are attracted to the free meal offered by the trap. The Alaska Department of Fish and Game recommends using king crab pots that range from 6 by 6 feet to 8 by 8 feet with heights between 2 and 3 feet. Over time, these mechanisms may disable the trap, preventing it from ghost fishing.", "pred": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars, designed to allow crabs to enter but not exit. The crab pot is typically a large square, about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with two ends featuring lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot, which is the only entrance. Crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food, and the design ensures they cannot escape once inside.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars, designed to allow crabs to enter but not exit. The crab pot is typically a large square, about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with two ends featuring lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot, which is the only entrance. Crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food, and the design ensures they cannot escape once inside.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars, designed to allow crabs to enter but not exit. The crab pot is typically a large square, about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with two ends featuring lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot, which is the only entrance. Crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food, and the design ensures they cannot escape once inside.\", \"Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage, typically made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars, designed to allow crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the end but not exit. For example, a crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with two ends having lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot, which is the only entrance; crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food inside.\", \"Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs to enter but not let them out. The crabs enter through a narrow slit that is the only entrance into the trap, which is located at the end of lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom. Once inside, the crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food.\", \"Answer: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs to enter through a narrow slit entrance at the ends, which angles into the trap from the sides and bottom. Once inside, crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food, but they are unable to exit the trap. The size of crab pots varies, with king crab pots ranging from about 6 by 6 feet to about 8 by 8 feet, with heights between about 2 and 3 feet.\", \"Answer: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars, designed to allow crabs to enter through a narrow slit (the only entrance) at the bottom via angled lead-ins but prevent them from exiting, as described in the passages where \\\"the traps or pots are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out\\\" and \\\"the crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\\\"\"]", "time_sec": 43.259, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.92, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "242", "question": "how do crab traps work", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how crab traps work:\n\nCrab traps are made of a metal cage with a system of nets inside, which are designed to allow crabs to enter but not escape. The traps have two leads that angle into the pot from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit entrance. The crabs crawl up the leads to reach the bait inside the pot, but cannot exit through the slit. The pot is designed to keep the crabs inside until they can be retrieved by the fisherman.\n\nAdditionally, according to passage 3, crab pots can be equipped with mechanisms that disable them over time, preventing them from continuing to catch crabs after they have been abandoned or become lost. These mechanisms can include biodegradable mesh or dissolvable cords.", "pred": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. They are designed as large square structures (e.g., 2 feet high and 8 feet wide) with two angled lead-ins that create a narrow slit entrance (about 2 feet into the pot) as the only entry point. Crabs enter by crawling up the leads to access the bait, but the design prevents them from exiting.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. They are designed as large square structures (e.g., 2 feet high and 8 feet wide) with two angled lead-ins that create a narrow slit entrance (about 2 feet into the pot) as the only entry point. Crabs enter by crawling up the leads to access the bait, but the design prevents them from exiting.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. They are designed as large square structures (e.g., 2 feet high and 8 feet wide) with two angled lead-ins that create a narrow slit entrance (about 2 feet into the pot) as the only entry point. Crabs enter by crawling up the leads to access the bait, but the design prevents them from exiting.\", \"Answer: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the end, which angles into the trap from the sides and bottom. Once inside, crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food, but they are unable to find their way out, ensuring they remain trapped until retrieved.\", \"Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the end, which is the only entrance, but not to exit. Crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal. The size of crab pots varies, with king crab pots ranging from about 6 by 6 feet to about 8 by 8 feet, with heights between about 2 and 3 feet.\", \"Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs to enter but not exit. Specifically, they are large square structures, about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with two ends that have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot, which is the only entrance into the trap. Crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal. The Alaska Department of Fish and Game notes that king crab pots range from about 6 by 6 feet to about 8 by 8 feet, with heights between about 2 and 3 feet.\", \"Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the end, which is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal, and once inside, they are unable to escape. The size of crab traps varies, with king crab pots generally ranging from about 6 by 6 feet to about 8 by 8 feet, with heights between about 2 and 3 feet.\"]", "time_sec": 45.134, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "243", "question": "how do crab traps work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how crab traps work:\n\nCrab traps are large square structures made of wire or flat metal mesh, with two ends that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. Crabs are attracted to bait inside the pot and must crawl up the leads to reach it, but once they enter, they cannot escape due to the narrow opening. The pot is designed to allow crabs in but not let them out, making it an effective tool for catching crabs.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"How do crab traps work?\" is: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage with a narrow entrance that allows crabs to enter but not exit, making it an effective tool for catching crabs.", "pred": "Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the end of lead-ins but not letting them exit, as described in passage 1: \"Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\" The trap is a large square measuring about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with a metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars, and nets inside to contain the crabs. Passage 3 notes that pots like these are designed to make big catches, and the Alaska Department of Fish and Game specifies king crab pots range from 6 by 6 feet to 8 by 8 feet with heights of 2 to 3 feet, confirming the size and structure that facilitates crab entry while restricting escape.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the end of lead-ins but not letting them exit, as described in passage 1: \"Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\" The trap is a large square measuring about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with a metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars, and nets inside to contain the crabs. Passage 3 notes that pots like these are designed to make big catches, and the Alaska Department of Fish and Game specifies king crab pots range from 6 by 6 feet to 8 by 8 feet with heights of 2 to 3 feet, confirming the size and structure that facilitates crab entry while restricting escape.", "cot": "[\"Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the end of lead-ins but not letting them exit, as described in passage 1: \\\"Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\\\" The trap is a large square measuring about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with a metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars, and nets inside to contain the crabs. Passage 3 notes that pots like these are designed to make big catches, and the Alaska Department of Fish and Game specifies king crab pots range from 6 by 6 feet to 8 by 8 feet with heights of 2 to 3 feet, confirming the size and structure that facilitates crab entry while restricting escape.\", \"Answer: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh, reinforced with steel bars. The trap is designed as a large square (2 feet high and 8 feet wide) with two ends featuring lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit (about 2 feet into the pot), which is the only entrance. Crabs enter by crawling up the leads through this slit to reach the bait, but they are unable to exit due to the trap's design.\", \"Answer: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. The trap is designed to allow crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the end, which is the only entrance, but not to exit. The crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food inside the trap.\", \"Answer: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars, designed to allow crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the bottom but not exit. The trap is typically a large square, about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with two ends featuring lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, creating a narrow entrance slit about 2 feet into the pot. Crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to reach their food, which leads them into the trap where they become trapped.\", \"Answer: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. The trap is designed as a large square, about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with two ends featuring lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance, and crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food, which ensures they enter but cannot exit.\"]", "time_sec": 47.105, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "244", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "The FEHA (Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) have several differences. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Another important difference is the requirement of disability. The ADA requires a physical or mental impairment to substantially limit a major life activity, while the FEHA only requires that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without the need for it to be a substantial limit.", "pred": "One key difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a substantial limitation of a major life activity, whereas the FEHA requires only a limit (not necessarily substantial) of a major life activity.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: One key difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a substantial limitation of a major life activity, whereas the FEHA requires only a limit (not necessarily substantial) of a major life activity.", "cot": "[\"Answer: One key difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a substantial limitation of a major life activity, whereas the FEHA requires only a limit (not necessarily substantial) of a major life activity.\", \"Answer: One key difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, FEHA requires only that a disability limits a major life activity, whereas the ADA requires a substantial limitation.\", \"Answer: The key differences between the FEHA and the ADA are:  \\n1. The ADA applies to private sector employers with **4 to 15 employees**, while the FEHA applies to **more employees** and **does not distinguish between private and public employers** (unlike the ADA).  \\n2. Under the **FEHA, a disability requires only a limit** on a major life activity (without the \\\"substantial\\\" requirement), whereas the **ADA requires a \\\"substantial limitation\\\"** of a major life activity for disability qualification.  \\n3. The FEHA **requires a disability** as a condition for coverage, while the ADA’s disability definition is based on the \\\"substantial limitation\\\" standard.  \\n\\nAnswer: The ADA applies to private employers with 4–15 employees and requires a \\\"substantial limitation\\\" of a major life activity for disability, while the FEHA applies to more employees (including public employers) and requires only a \\\"limit\\\" (not \\\"substantial\\\") on a major life activity for disability.\", \"Answer: One difference between the FEHA and the ADA is that the ADA applies to all private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a substantial limitation of a major life activity, whereas the FEHA only requires that a disability limits a major life activity, without the \\\"substantial\\\" requirement.\", \"Answer: One key difference between FEHA and the ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, FEHA requires only that a disability limits a major life activity, whereas the ADA requires that a disability substantially limits a major life activity.\"]", "time_sec": 41.26, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 62.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "245", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "One difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA affects more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers like ADA does.", "pred": "One key difference between FEHA and the ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under FEHA, a disability is required to limit a major life activity, whereas under the ADA, the impairment must substantially limit a major life activity.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: One key difference between FEHA and the ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under FEHA, a disability is required to limit a major life activity, whereas under the ADA, the impairment must substantially limit a major life activity.", "cot": "[\"Answer: One key difference between FEHA and the ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under FEHA, a disability is required to limit a major life activity, whereas under the ADA, the impairment must substantially limit a major life activity.\", \"Answer: One key difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and covers both private and public employers without distinction. Additionally, under the FEHA, a disability is defined as a mental or physical condition that limits a major life activity, whereas the ADA requires the impairment to substantially limit a major life activity.\", \"Answer: The key differences between FEHA and the ADA are:  \\n1. **Scope of Employers**: The ADA applies to private-sector employers with **4–15 employees**, while FEHA applies to **more employees** and **does not distinguish** between private and public employers.  \\n2. **Definition of Disability**: Under the ADA, a disability requires a **substantial limitation** of a major life activity. FEHA requires only a **limit** (not necessarily substantial) of a major life activity.  \\n3. **Application**: FEHA covers both private and public employers, whereas the ADA applies only to private-sector employers with 4–15 employees.  \\n\\nThese distinctions are explicitly stated in the passages.  \\n\\nAnswer: The ADA applies to private-sector employers with 4–15 employees and requires a \\\"substantial limit\\\" of a major life activity for disability, while FEHA applies to more employees (including public employers) and requires only a \\\"limit\\\" (not substantial) of a major life activity for disability.\", \"Answer: The key differences between FEHA and the ADA include:  \\n1. **Scope of Coverage**: The ADA applies to private sector employers with 4–15 employees, while FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers.  \\n2. **Definition of Disability**: Under the ADA, a disability requires a physical or mental impairment that *substantially limits* a major life activity. FEHA requires only that a mental or physical disability *limits* a major life activity (without the \\\"substantial\\\" requirement).  \\n3. **Employer Type**: FEHA covers both private and public employers, whereas the ADA applies only to private sector employers with 4–15 employees.  \\n\\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: One difference between the FEHA (the Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) is that the ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity, while the FEHA only requires that a mental or physical disability limit a major life activity, without the \\\"substantial\\\" limitation requirement.\"]", "time_sec": 50.932, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.79, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "246", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) are:\n\n1. Scope of application: The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does.\n2. Definition of disability: The FEHA requires that a disability must limit a major life activity, while the ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limits a major life activity.\n3. Number of employees: The ADA applies to employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA has no such requirement.\n\nTherefore, the main difference between FEHA and ADA is the scope of application and the definition of disability.", "pred": "One key difference between the FEHA and the ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability is defined as a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity, whereas under the FEHA, a disability is defined as a mental or physical impairment that limits a major life activity, without requiring a substantial limitation.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: One key difference between the FEHA and the ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability is defined as a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity, whereas under the FEHA, a disability is defined as a mental or physical impairment that limits a major life activity, without requiring a substantial limitation.", "cot": "[\"Answer: One key difference between the FEHA and the ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability is defined as a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity, whereas under the FEHA, a disability is defined as a mental or physical impairment that limits a major life activity, without requiring a substantial limitation.\", \"Answer: One key difference between FEHA and the ADA is the scope of coverage and qualification criteria for disabilities. The ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees and requires that a disability substantially limit a major life activity. In contrast, FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers, and it requires only that a disability (physical or mental) limits a major life activity, without the \\\"substantial\\\" limitation requirement.\", \"Answer: One difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does. Another difference is that under FEHA, a disability is required, meaning a mental or physical disability that limits a major life activity, whereas under the ADA, the impairment must substantially limit a major life activity.\", \"Answer: One key difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees and distinguishes between private and public employers, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the FEHA, a disability is required, whereas under the ADA, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity to qualify as a disability.\", \"Answer: One key difference between FEHA and the ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, FEHA requires only that a disability limit a major life activity, whereas the ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limit a major life activity to qualify as a disability.\"]", "time_sec": 35.2, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.68, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "248", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nThe main difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to all employers in California, regardless of size or sector, while ADA applies to private employers with 4 to 15 employees and does not cover public employers. Additionally, FEHA has a broader definition of disability, requiring only that a mental or physical disability limit a major life activity, whereas ADA requires a substantial limitation.", "pred": "One key difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees and distinguishes between private and public employers, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a substantial limitation of a major life activity, whereas the FEHA requires only that a disability limits a major life activity, without the \"substantial\" requirement.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: One key difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees and distinguishes between private and public employers, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a substantial limitation of a major life activity, whereas the FEHA requires only that a disability limits a major life activity, without the \"substantial\" requirement.", "cot": "[\"Answer: One key difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees and distinguishes between private and public employers, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a substantial limitation of a major life activity, whereas the FEHA requires only that a disability limits a major life activity, without the \\\"substantial\\\" requirement.\", \"Answer: One difference between the FEHA (the Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) is that the ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does. Probably one of the most important differences between the ADA and FEHA is that with FEHA, a disability is required. Under the ADA, to qualify for disability, a physical or mental impairment substantially limits a major life activity, but the FEHA requires only that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity; not a substantial limit, but a limit.\", \"Answer: One key difference between FEHA and the ADA is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, FEHA requires only that a disability limits a major life activity, whereas the ADA requires that a disability substantially limits a major life activity.\", \"Answer: One difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and covers both private and public employers. Additionally, FEHA requires only that a disability limits a major life activity, whereas the ADA requires a substantial limitation.\", \"Answer: One key difference between the FEHA and the ADA is the scope of coverage and the definition of disability. The ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees and distinguishes between private and public employers, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, the FEHA requires only that a disability limit a major life activity, whereas the ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limit a major life activity.\"]", "time_sec": 36.783, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.45, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "249", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "To grill pork chops according to allrecipes.com, start by preheating an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse the pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow to stand for 10 minutes. Finally, grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring in a bowl. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 18.016, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "250", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "To grill pork chops according to allrecipes.com, preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring. Rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Massage the spice rub into the meat and let it stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat for about 12 minutes per side or until they are no longer pink inside.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Answer: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring in a bowl. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\"]", "time_sec": 24.453, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "251", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "To grill pork chops according to the instructions provided in Allrecipes.com, follow these steps: \n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat. \n2. Lightly oil the grate. \n3. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until well combined. \n4. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle them with the spice mixture on both sides. \n5. Massage the spice rub into the meat and let it stand for 10 minutes. \n6. Grill the chops over indirect heat for about 12 minutes per side, or until they are no longer pink inside.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring in a bowl. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Answer: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring in a bowl. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Answer: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring in a bowl. Rinse pork chops, then sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\"]", "time_sec": 24.057, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "252", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. (Passage 1)\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. (Passage 1)\n3. For Oven-Fried Pork Chops, use stuffing mix for the breading. The pork chops come out tender and juicy. This recipe takes 30 minutes to prepare and 10 minutes to prep. (Passage 2)\n4. To grill pork chops over indirect heat, rinse the chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Massage the spice rub into the meat for 10 minutes before grilling. Grill the chops until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com, you should preheat the grill, season the pork chops with a spice mixture, and grill them over indirect heat until they are cooked through.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 6.702, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 2.84, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "255", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove the cover.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole of the vent.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to remove lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n6. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning that area as well.\n7. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and remove the lint filter frame for easier access to clean.\n8. This thorough cleaning will help your dryer run efficiently and reduce the risk of house fires.\n\nNote: The information provided in the given passages is sufficient to answer the question.", "pred": "To clean the dryer vent, first locate the outside vent cover on your house and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to clear lint from the vent duct and the hole in the back of the dryer where the vent connects. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for a more thorough cleaning, as this can improve dryer efficiency.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean the dryer vent, first locate the outside vent cover on your house and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to clear lint from the vent duct and the hole in the back of the dryer where the vent connects. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for a more thorough cleaning, as this can improve dryer efficiency.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To clean the dryer vent, first locate the outside vent cover on your house and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to clear lint from the vent duct and the hole in the back of the dryer where the vent connects. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for a more thorough cleaning, as this can improve dryer efficiency.\", \"Answer: To clean a dryer vent, first locate and remove the outside cover, then use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe. Additionally, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint, and clean the lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Also, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and the lint filter frame to access and clean lint deposits more thoroughly.\", \"Answer: To clean the dryer vent, first locate the outside vent cover and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to clear lint from the vent duct and the vent itself. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter for better efficiency, as suggested in the passages.\", \"Answer: To clean your dryer vent, follow these steps based on the passages:  \\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it (Passage 1, Step 1-2).  \\n2. Use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the vent pipe (Passage 3).  \\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint (Passage 1, Step 4).  \\n4. Clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the dryer vent brush (Passage 1, Step 4).  \\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall (Passage 1, Step 5).  \\nAdditional steps include removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning around the lint filter for thoroughness (Passage 2).\", \"Answer: To clean a dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it, allowing the vent duct to slide out if not fastened. Then, use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole and the vent itself. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for more thorough cleaning.\"]", "time_sec": 41.965, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "256", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "To clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the outside cover on the vent.\n2. Use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.\n3. If possible, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there as well.\n4. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and clean it thoroughly.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "pred": "To clean the dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole and the vent duct. Additionally, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint, and clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Also, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and the lint filter frame to clean lint deposits and improve dryer efficiency.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean the dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole and the vent duct. Additionally, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint, and clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Also, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and the lint filter frame to clean lint deposits and improve dryer efficiency.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To clean the dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole and the vent duct. Additionally, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint, and clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Also, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and the lint filter frame to clean lint deposits and improve dryer efficiency.\", \"Answer: To clean a dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it; if it isn’t fastened, the vent duct should slide out easily. Then use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole and from the vent itself. Next, unscrew the vent clamp at the back of the dryer and slide the vent out of the elbow‑shaped joint, cleaning both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer with the brush. Finally, reconnect the vent and push the dryer back against the wall. Additional steps include removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and the lint filter frame to clean those areas and use a vacuum nozzle for thorough lint removal, which improves efficiency and reduces fire risk.\", \"Answer: To clean a dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it; if the vent duct isn’t fastened or sealed, it should slide out easily. Then, use a dryer vent brush to clear lint from the hole in the exterior wall. Next, disconnect the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow‑shaped joint, and brush lint from both the vent and the opening in the dryer. Finally, reconnect the vent and push the dryer back against the wall. Additional steps include removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning around the lint filter, as well as using the lint filter frame to gain easier access for vacuuming.\", \"Answer: To clean the dryer vent, first locate and remove the outside cover on the vent. Then, use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean the area around the lint filter for more thorough cleaning.\", \"Answer: To clean the dryer vent, first locate the outside vent cover and remove it. Then use a dryer vent brush to clear lint from the vent duct. Additionally, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the clamp and sliding it out of the joint, and clean lint from both the vent and the dryer opening. Also, consider removing the bottom front panel and the lint filter frame to clean lint deposits from those areas for improved efficiency.\"]", "time_sec": 44.63, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "257", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here are the steps to clean a dryer vent based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house (passage 1) and remove it by sliding it out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the exterior (step 2).\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from the hole where the vent connects to the dryer (step 3).\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint (step 4).\n4. Clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the dryer vent brush (step 4).\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall (step 5).\n6. If desired, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean the area around the lint filter (passage 2).\n7. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits in the area around the lint filter frame (passage 2).\n\nNote: Passage 3 provides additional information but does not provide specific instructions for cleaning the dryer vent. Therefore, these steps are based on the information provided in passages 1-2.", "pred": "To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps: remove the outside vent cover, use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe, and also clean the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint, then remove lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for more thorough cleaning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps: remove the outside vent cover, use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe, and also clean the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint, then remove lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for more thorough cleaning.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps: remove the outside vent cover, use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe, and also clean the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint, then remove lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for more thorough cleaning.\", \"Answer: To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps: First, locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the vent hole. Next, unscrew the vent clamp at the back of the dryer and slide the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Use the brush to clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for more thorough cleaning, as this can improve dryer efficiency.\", \"Answer: To clean the dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. Then, using a dryer vent brush, remove lint from inside the vent hole. Next, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the brush. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for a more thorough cleaning, as this can improve dryer efficiency.\", \"Answer: To clean a dryer vent, first locate and remove the outside vent cover on the exterior of your house. Then, use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean lint from inside the vent pipe. Additionally, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint, and clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. It is also recommended to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for more thorough cleaning.\", \"Answer: To clean a dryer vent, first locate the outside vent cover on your house and remove it. Then use a dryer vent brush to clear lint from inside the vent duct and the vent itself, which you can detach from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint. Also, clean the area around the lint filter by removing the filter frame and using a vacuum nozzle, and consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer for more thorough cleaning. Be sure to reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall afterward.\"]", "time_sec": 47.029, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.83, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "259", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "Sure, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to clean dryer vent\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo clean the dryer vent, start by locating the vent cover on the outside of the house and removing it. Then, remove the vent from the back of the dryer and use a dryer vent brush to clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning the area around the lint filter for a more thorough cleaning. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits and ensure your dryer runs efficiently.\n\nIf the passages did not contain the necessary information to answer the question, I would have replied with \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "To clean the dryer vent, first locate the outside vent cover and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to clear lint from the vent opening and the duct. Detach the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the clamp and sliding it out of the elbow joint, and clean lint from both the vent and the opening in the dryer. Additionally, you may remove the dryer’s bottom front panel and the lint filter frame to access and clean hidden lint deposits, using a vacuum nozzle for thorough cleaning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean the dryer vent, first locate the outside vent cover and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to clear lint from the vent opening and the duct. Detach the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the clamp and sliding it out of the elbow joint, and clean lint from both the vent and the opening in the dryer. Additionally, you may remove the dryer’s bottom front panel and the lint filter frame to access and clean hidden lint deposits, using a vacuum nozzle for thorough cleaning.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To clean the dryer vent, first locate the outside vent cover and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to clear lint from the vent opening and the duct. Detach the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the clamp and sliding it out of the elbow joint, and clean lint from both the vent and the opening in the dryer. Additionally, you may remove the dryer’s bottom front panel and the lint filter frame to access and clean hidden lint deposits, using a vacuum nozzle for thorough cleaning.\", \"Answer: To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps: locate and remove the outside vent cover, slide out the vent duct if not fastened, use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer, and reconnect the vent while moving the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter for more thorough cleaning, as this can improve dryer efficiency.\", \"Answer: To clean a dryer vent, first locate and remove the outside vent cover, then use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe. Additionally, you can remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint, then clean the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer with the brush. It’s also recommended to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for more thorough results.\", \"Answer: To clean your dryer vent, follow these steps: locate and remove the outside vent cover, then use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe. Additionally, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint, and clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the brush. Also, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning around the lint filter area for more thorough results, as this can improve dryer efficiency.\", \"Answer: To clean the dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. Then, use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the vent hole. Next, unscrew the vent clamp at the back of the dryer and slide the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the brush. Finally, reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for a more thorough cleaning, as this can improve dryer efficiency.\"]", "time_sec": 43.544, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "260", "question": "the benefits of msm powder", "gt": "MSM powder offers several benefits. It helps get oxygen into the blood more efficiently, thereby increasing energy levels. It also makes cell walls more permeable. The powder aids in the absorption of more nutrients, particularly when paired with Co-enzyme Q10. Additionally, MSM powder can help relieve muscular aches and pains and reduce inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.", "pred": "The benefits of MSM powder include helping oxygen enter the blood more efficiently with the same amount of work, increasing energy levels by making cell walls more permeable, improving nutrient absorption (vitamins and minerals) by supporting Co-enzyme Q10 utilization, relieving muscular aches and pains, and reducing inflammation caused by injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The benefits of MSM powder include helping oxygen enter the blood more efficiently with the same amount of work, increasing energy levels by making cell walls more permeable, improving nutrient absorption (vitamins and minerals) by supporting Co-enzyme Q10 utilization, relieving muscular aches and pains, and reducing inflammation caused by injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.", "cot": "[\"Answer: The benefits of MSM powder include helping oxygen enter the blood more efficiently with the same amount of work, increasing energy levels by making cell walls more permeable, improving nutrient absorption (vitamins and minerals) by supporting Co-enzyme Q10 utilization, relieving muscular aches and pains, and reducing inflammation caused by injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.\", \"Answer:MSM powder benefits the body by helping get oxygen into the blood more efficiently with the same amount of work, increasing energy levels (as it helps make cell walls more permeable and relieves muscular aches and pains), aiding nutrient absorption (particularly vitamins and minerals, with Co-enzyme Q10 requiring MSM for full utilization), reducing inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis (linked to cellular water pressure imbalance), and relieving muscular aches and pains.\", \"Answer: MSM powder benefits the body by helping get oxygen into the blood more efficiently with the same amount of work, increasing energy levels due to making cell walls more permeable, helping absorb more nutrients (vitamins and minerals), requiring MSM (sulfur) for Co-enzyme Q10 to be fully utilized, relieving muscular aches and pains, and reducing inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.\", \"Answer: MSM powder benefits the body by helping get oxygen into the blood more efficiently with the same amount of work, increasing energy levels by making cell walls more permeable, helping absorb more nutrients (vitamins and minerals) especially when combined with co-enzyme Q10, relieving muscular aches and pains, and reducing inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.\", \"Answer: MSM powder benefits the body by helping get oxygen into the blood more efficiently, increasing energy levels through improved cell wall permeability, enhancing nutrient absorption (especially when combined with Co-enzyme Q10), relieving muscular aches and pains, and reducing inflammation associated with injury or conditions like arthritis.\"]", "time_sec": 32.037, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
