e water heater to keep it hot. Alternatively, recirculating pumps can rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused, which can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump can be used to make the hot water heater circulate. The pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, and circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring that hot water is always available. Alternatively, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor to rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water back to be reheated and reused.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump can make the hot water heater circulate by sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater through a return line, which then reheats the water and reuses it, ensuring that hot water is always available. This can be done continuously or using demand systems controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.\"]", "time_sec": 32.991, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 78.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "300", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, one can install a recirculation system. The system consists of a pump that pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. This ensures that hot water is always available without having to wait for it to circulate naturally. Recirculation systems can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.", "pred": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep it hot.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: A hot water circulation pump can be used to circulate hot water in the water heater. This can be done by sending cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, which is then reheated and reused in a continuous loop. Demand systems for this process can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.", "cot": "[\"Answer: A hot water circulation pump can be used to circulate hot water in the water heater. This can be done by sending cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, which is then reheated and reused in a continuous loop. Demand systems for this process can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep it hot.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump can be used to make a hot water heater circulate water. According to passage 2, the pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep hot water available. Passage 3 adds that recirculating pumps can rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water back to be reheated, and these systems can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump can be used to circulate hot water in the pipes. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to ensure hot water is always available. Alternatively, recirculating pumps can rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused, which can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep it hot.\"]", "time_sec": 28.982, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
