is always available when a faucet is turned on. Demand systems for this process can be controlled by a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump can make a hot water heater circulate by sending cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep it hot.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump can be used to circulate hot water in a water heater system. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep hot water available. Demand systems can also be used, which can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor, rapidly pulling hot water from the water heater and sending cool water back to be reheated and reused.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump can make the hot water heater circulate by sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater through a return line, which then reheats the water and ensures that hot water is always available. This continuous loop of water through the water heater can be controlled by a push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.\"]", "time_sec": 28.811, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.39, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "302", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to make a hot water heater circulate:\n\nOption 1: Install a recirculating pump. Passage 3 explains that recirculating pumps can rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. These pumps can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.\n\nOption 2: Use a hot water circulation pump. Passage 2 describes how a hot water circulation pump can send cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, ensuring that hot water is always available when needed.\n\nIt is important to note that running a hot water circulation pump continuously can consume a significant amount of energy, as mentioned in passage 1. Therefore, it may be more cost-effective to only run the pump when needed, such as when you turn on the faucet.", "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a recirculating pump can be used. This pump rapidly pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. Demand systems for this circulation can be controlled by a push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To make a hot water heater circulate, a recirculating pump can be used. This pump rapidly pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. Demand systems for this circulation can be controlled by a push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To make a hot water heater circulate, a recirculating pump can be used. This pump rapidly pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. Demand systems for this circulation can be controlled by a push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.\", \"Answer: To make a hot water heater circulate, a recirculating pump can be used, which rapidly pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. Demand systems for this circulation can be controlled by a push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep it hot and ensure hot water is always available. Demand systems can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available. Instead, recirculating pumps rapidly pull hot water from a water heater, while simultaneously send cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. Demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor.\", \"Answer: To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump can be used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, which then circulates the water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring that hot water is always available when a faucet is turned on.\"]", "time_sec": 31.585, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4