on (2-3 bedrooms and a bath plus a flight of stairs), but can increase to $400-$500 per square foot based on complexity, quality of materials, and local labor rates. Building a second floor costs at least 20 percent more than building the same square footage at ground level.\"]", "time_sec": 29.154, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "318", "question": "how can i check taxes were filed", "gt": "Based on the given passages, you can check the status of your tax return by:\n\n1. Using the IRS2Go app on your smartphone to check the status of your tax return online.\n2. Checking the status of your tax return over the phone by calling the IRS.\n3. Checking the status of your state tax return online or over the phone.\n\nTo check the status of your tax return, you will need your Social Security number, tax filing status, and the amount of any refund due. If you e-filed your return, you can check the status 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return. If you mailed your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to check taxes were filed is:\n\nYou can check the status of your tax return online or over the phone using the methods described above.", "pred": "You can check if your taxes were filed by using the IRS2Go mobile application (available for Apple users via the App Store), checking the status online at the IRS website, or calling the IRS. If you e-filed, you can also check status within 72 hours by providing your Social Security number, filing status, and refund amount, or wait 24 hours after IRS acknowledgment of receipt (which may be confirmed via email from tax software). If mailed, allow 3-4 weeks before checking.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer:You can check if your taxes were filed by using the IRS2Go mobile application (available for Apple users via the App Store), checking the status online at the IRS website, or calling the IRS. If you e-filed, you can also check status within 72 hours by providing your Social Security number, filing status, and refund amount, or wait 24 hours after IRS acknowledgment of receipt (which may be confirmed via email from tax software). If mailed, allow 3-4 weeks before checking.", "cot": "[\"Answer:You can check if your taxes were filed by using the IRS2Go mobile application (available for Apple users via the App Store), checking the status online at the IRS website, or calling the IRS. If you e-filed, you can also check status within 72 hours by providing your Social Security number, filing status, and refund amount, or wait 24 hours after IRS acknowledgment of receipt (which may be confirmed via email from tax software). If mailed, allow 3-4 weeks before checking.\", \"Answer: You can check if your taxes were filed by using the IRS2Go mobile application (available for Apple users via the App Store) or by checking your email for a confirmation from your tax software, which typically sends an email when the IRS accepts your return. Additionally, you can log into your tax software account to check the status of your return. For federal returns, if you e-filed, you should be able to get a refund status within 72 hours, and you can also check online or by phone through the IRS. If you mailed your taxes, you will need to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes to check the status. You'll need your Social Security number, your tax filing status, and the amount of any refund due to check the status.\", \"Answer: You can check if your taxes were filed by using the IRS2Go mobile application, which can be downloaded from the Apple App Store for Apple users. Additionally, you can check the status of your federal tax return online or by phoning the IRS. To do so, you'll need your Social Security number, your tax filing status, and the amount of any refund due. If you e-filed your return, wait 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return before checking the status. You can also provide your email address to receive an email confirmation when the IRS accepts your tax return. Software programs typically have an application that allows you to check the status of your return by logging into your account.\", \"Answer: You can check if your taxes were filed by using the IRS2Go mobile application, which allows you to handle taxes online. If you are an Apple user, you can download this app from the Apple App Store. Additionally, you can check the status of your tax return online or by phoning the IRS, provided you have your Social Security number, tax filing status, and the amount of any refund due. If you e-filed your taxes, you should be able to get a refund status within 72 hours, or wait 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return if you provided your email address for confirmation. If you mailed your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.\", \"Answer: You can check that your taxes were filed by using the IRS2Go mobile application (available for Apple users via the Apple App Store), by checking your email for an IRS acceptance confirmation from your tax software, or by logging into your tax software account to view the return status.\"]", "time_sec": 48.149, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "320", "question": "what is the effect of carbon footprint", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that the effect of a carbon footprint is a measure of the negative impact of human activities on the environment. The measurement of a carbon footprint typically indicates the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced through daily activities. Additionally, reducing one's carbon footprint can have a positive impact on the environment, even if the changes may seem small.", "pred": "The passages state that a carbon footprint measures \"the environmental impact of your lifestyle\" and indicates \"the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases that are produced as a result of your daily activities.\" The effect is the environmental impact resulting from greenhouse gas emissions caused by human activities.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The passages state that a carbon footprint measures \"the environmental impact of your lifestyle\" and indicates \"the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases that are produced as a result of your daily activities.\" The effect is the environmental impact resulting from greenhouse gas emissions caused by human activities.", "cot": "[\"Answer: The passages state that a carbon footprint measures \\\"the environmental impact of your lifestyle\\\" and indicates \\\"the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases that are produced as a result of your daily activities.\\\" The effect is the environmental impact resulting from greenhouse gas emissions caused by human activities.\", \"Answer: A carbon footprint measures the environmental impact of your lifestyle, indicating the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced by your daily activities. It reflects the total greenhouse gases generated by human activities within a given time frame, typically measured in tons of carbon dioxide released into the atmosphere. The passages highlight that everything you do has a positive or negative impact on the environment, and reducing your footprint involves changing your lifestyle, as even small changes can make a significant difference.\", \"Answer: The passage states that a carbon footprint \\\"measures the environmental impact of your lifestyle\\\" and indicates \\\"the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases that are produced as a result of your daily activities.\\\" It further explains that carbon footprint is \\\"one method of measuring the environmental effect of your lifestyle.\\\" The passages describe this effect as being both positive or negative, with the concept centered on how human activities impact the environment through greenhouse gas emissions.\", \"Answer: The effect of a carbon footprint is the environmental impact of an individual's lifestyle, as it measures the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced by daily activities. This impact can be reduced through lifestyle changes, as even small changes can make a significant difference. The environmental effect is quantified in tons of greenhouse gases, with examples including an average per capita footprint of 6 tons per year, 20 tons per year in the U.S., and over 6 tons of CO2 annually from automobile emissions alone.\", \"Answer: A carbon footprint measures the environmental impact of a lifestyle by quantifying the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced by daily activities. It indicates the total greenhouse gas emissions associated with human activities within a given time frame, typically measured in tons of CO₂.\"]", "time_sec": 32.125, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.65, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "321", "question": "what is the effect of carbon footprint", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the effect of carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of an individual's lifestyle and daily activities, specifically the amount of greenhouse gases produced, such as carbon dioxide, as a result of those activities. The carbon footprint is typically measured in tons of CO2 released into the atmosphere. The passages also mention that reducing one's carbon footprint can have a significant impact on the environment, even with seemingly small changes. Additionally, the average carbon footprint is mentioned to be around 6 tons per year, with a higher amount in the US due to automobile emissions.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: A carbon footprint measures the environmental impact of your lifestyle, indicating the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced by your daily activities. It reflects the effect of human activities on the environment by quantifying the total greenhouse gases emitted, which contributes to climate change and environmental degradation.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: The passage states that a carbon footprint \\\"measures the environmental impact of your lifestyle\\\" and indicates \\\"the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases that are produced as a result of your daily activities.\\\" It also mentions that \\\"Everything you do has an impact --- positive or negative --- on the environment,\\\" showing the carbon footprint measures the environmental effect of human activities.\"]", "time_sec": 15.33, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.8, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "324", "question": "how well do patterned rollers work", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's what we can conclude about how well patterned rollers work:\n\nPassage 1 suggests that homemade texture or decorative paint rollers can work better than commercial ones for certain faux finishes because they can create a random pattern of texture.\n\nPassage 2 provides a personal testimonial about the effectiveness of the Dermaroller for improving the appearance of skin. The writer claims that it makes their skin look younger and healthier, and that it works best when used with serums or moisturizers. However, there is no direct mention of patterned rollers in this passage.\n\nPassage 3 provides instructions for creating a basic texture roller using an old roller pad with clumped tufts and random patterns created by stretching and twisting rubber bands. This passage suggests that patterned rollers can create a textured finish on walls, but there is no information on how effective they are or how well they work.\n\nTherefore, based on the given passages, it is difficult to say definitively how well patterned rollers work. Passage 1 suggests that they may be effective for certain applications, while passage 2 provides a personal endorsement of a specific product (Dermaroller) for improving skin appearance. Passage 3 provides instructions for creating a basic texture roller, but does not provide any information on its effectiveness. Therefore, the answer to the original question is: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Patterned rollers work better than commercial rollers because many faux finishes rely on applying a random pattern of texture to walls, and commercial rollers apply paint with a set pattern.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Patterned rollers work better than commercial rollers because many faux finishes rely on applying a random pattern of texture to walls, and commercial rollers apply paint with a set pattern.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Patterned rollers work better than commercial rollers because many faux finishes rely on applying a random pattern of texture to walls, and commercial rollers apply paint with a set pattern.\", \"Answer: Patterned rollers work well because many faux finishes rely on applying a random pattern of texture to walls, and commercial texture rollers apply paint with a set pattern, making homemade texture or decorative paint rollers more effective than commercial varieties.\", \"Answer: Patterned rollers work well for applying random patterns of texture to walls, often performing better than commercial texture rollers that apply a set pattern. The Basic Texture Roller technique, which uses a pad with 1-inch or thicker nap stretched and twisted with rubber bands to create clumps and random patterns, is effective for this purpose. This method is described as working better than commercial rollers because it allows for a random pattern application, which is essential for many faux finishes.\", \"Answer: Patterned rollers, such as homemade texture rollers, can work better than commercial rollers for faux finishes because they apply a random pattern of texture to walls, whereas commercial rollers apply paint with a set pattern.\", \"Answer: Patterned rollers work well because many faux finishes rely on applying a random pattern of texture to walls, and commercial texture rollers apply paint with a set pattern, making homemade texture or decorative paint rollers more effective.\"]", "time_sec": 22.439, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 15.47, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "325", "question": "how well do patterned rollers work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that patterned rollers can work well for creating textured finishes on walls, as they can produce a random pattern of texture that is often desired in faux finishing techniques. The third passage provides instructions for creating a DIY texture roller by modifying an existing roller pad with rubber bands to create clumps and random patterns, which can be used to apply paint and create a textured finish.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"How well do patterned rollers work?\" is:\n\nThey can work well for creating textured finishes on walls, especially when used with faux finishing techniques.", "pred": "Patterned rollers work better than commercial texture rollers for faux finishes that rely on random patterns, as homemade texture rollers with clumped tufts create random patterns that commercial rollers with set patterns cannot replicate.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Patterned rollers work better than commercial texture rollers for faux finishes that rely on random patterns, as homemade texture rollers with clumped tufts create random patterns that commercial rollers with set patterns cannot replicate.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Patterned rollers work better than commercial texture rollers for faux finishes that rely on random patterns, as homemade texture rollers with clumped tufts create random patterns that commercial rollers with set patterns cannot replicate.\", \"Answer: Patterned rollers work better than commercial rollers because they apply a random pattern of texture, which is more effective for faux finishes that rely on random patterns.\", \"Based on the provided passages, patterned rollers (such as homemade texture or decorative paint rollers) work better than commercial texture rollers for faux finishes because they apply paint with a random pattern rather than a set pattern. Specifically, passage 1 states: \\\"homemade texture or decorative paint rollers can work better than the commercial variety because many faux finishes rely on applying a random pattern of texture to your walls, and commercial texture rollers apply paint with a set pattern.\\\"\", \"Answer: Patterned rollers work well because many faux finishes rely on applying a random pattern of texture to walls, and commercial texture rollers apply paint with a set pattern, making homemade texture or decorative paint rollers more effective.\", \"Based on the given passages, patterned rollers work well because they apply a random pattern of texture to walls, which is more effective for many faux finishes than the set pattern of commercial texture rollers. Passage 1 specifically states that \\\"homemade texture or decorative paint rollers can work better than the commercial variety\\\" since \\\"many faux finishes rely on applying a random pattern of texture to your walls, and commercial texture rollers apply paint with a set pattern.\\\" Passage 3 provides instructions for creating a random pattern using a basic texture roller by stretching and twisting rubber bands around the pad to form \\\"clumps and random patterns with tufts and lines,\\\" confirming that this method produces the desired random texture for faux finishes. The passages indicate patterned rollers are effective for achieving the random texture needed in faux finishing techniques.\"]", "time_sec": 30.101, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "329", "question": "how to boil potatoes for easy peeling", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to boil potatoes for easy peeling:\n\nPassage 1 recommends boiling the potatoes until they are tender, then transferring them to an ice water bath to stop the cooking process. After cooling, the skin can be easily peeled off. This method takes 15 minutes to cook the potatoes and 5 seconds to peel each one.\n\nPassage 2 suggests peeling the potatoes before cooking, as their skin can be tough and papery. However, no specific instructions are provided for peeling.\n\nPassage 3 provides a step-by-step guide for peeling cooked potatoes. The method involves scoring the potatoes all the way around the center, boiling them for about 15 minutes, then placing them in an ice water bath to cool. Once cooled, the skin can be easily removed. This method takes about 30 minutes total time.\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, the best way to boil potatoes for easy peeling is to boil them until tender, then transfer them to an ice water bath to stop the cooking process and make the skin easier to remove. Scoring the potatoes before boiling can also help loosen the skin for easier peeling.", "pred": "To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Then, score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes until tender. After boiling, transfer the potatoes to an ice water bath and let them cool for a few seconds. Once cool enough to handle, remove the potatoes from the water and peel off the skin, which should come off easily.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer:To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Then, score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes until tender. After boiling, transfer the potatoes to an ice water bath and let them cool for a few seconds. Once cool enough to handle, remove the potatoes from the water and peel off the skin, which should come off easily.", "cot": "[\"Answer:To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Then, score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes until tender. After boiling, transfer the potatoes to an ice water bath and let them cool for a few seconds. Once cool enough to handle, remove the potatoes from the water and peel off the skin, which should come off easily.\", \"Answer: To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife, then boil them for about 15 minutes. After boiling, transfer the potatoes to an ice water bath for a few seconds to cool. Then, remove the potatoes from the water and easily peel off the skin.\", \"Answer: Bring a pot of water to a boil. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes. Then, place the potatoes in a bowl of ice water for a few seconds to cool. Remove the potato from the water and peel off the skin.\", \"Answer:To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes until tender. Then, transfer the potatoes to an ice water bath and let them cool for a few seconds. Finally, remove the potatoes from the water and peel off the skin, which should come off easily.\", \"Answer: To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Then, score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes. After boiling, transfer the potatoes to an ice water bath and let them cool for a few seconds. Once cool enough to handle, remove the potatoes from the water and peel off the skin. This method is mentioned in passage 3 and is supported by passage 1, which states that after boiling, the potatoes should be transferred to an ice water bath and the skin can be peeled off easily.\"]", "time_sec": 36.389, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.84, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "331", "question": "how to boil potatoes for easy peeling", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to boil potatoes for easy peeling:\n\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. Score your potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.\n\nThe ice water bath helps to stop the cooking process and cool down the potatoes quickly, making the skin easier to peel off.", "pred": "To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes until tender. Then, transfer them to an ice water bath and let them cool for a few seconds. The skin can be easily peeled off after this process.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes until tender. Then, transfer them to an ice water bath and let them cool for a few seconds. The skin can be easily peeled off after this process.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes until tender. Then, transfer them to an ice water bath and let them cool for a few seconds. The skin can be easily peeled off after this process.\", \"Answer:To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Then, score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes. After boiling, transfer the potatoes to an ice water bath and let them cool for a few seconds. Once cool enough to handle, remove the potatoes from the water and peel off the skin.\", \"Answer: To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes until tender. Then, transfer the potatoes to an ice water bath for a few seconds to cool. Finally, remove the potatoes from the water and peel off the skin, which should come off easily.\", \"Answer:To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife, then place them in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes. After boiling, transfer the potatoes to an ice water bath and let them cool for a few seconds. Then, remove the potatoes from the water and peel off the skin, which should come off easily.\", \"Answer: To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first bring a pot of water to a boil. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife. Place the potatoes in the boiling water and cook for about 15 minutes until tender. Then, transfer the potatoes to an ice water bath and let them cool for a few seconds. The skin can then be easily peeled off.\"]", "time_sec": 33.637, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.72, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "332", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, first, check common tick hiding places such as inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes. Once you locate a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the tick's head where it attaches to the skin. If you plan to use your fingers, wear gloves. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Regular use of tick control products can also prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Flea and tick shampoos can kill the ticks that are already on your pet.", "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes for ticks, as these are favorite hiding places. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause infection. It is also recommended to wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Additionally, regular use of tick control products advised by a veterinarian can help prevent ticks from attaching to dogs.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes for ticks, as these are favorite hiding places. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause infection. It is also recommended to wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Additionally, regular use of tick control products advised by a veterinarian can help prevent ticks from attaching to dogs.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes for ticks, as these are favorite hiding places. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause infection. It is also recommended to wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Additionally, regular use of tick control products advised by a veterinarian can help prevent ticks from attaching to dogs.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes, then use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving the mouth behind and causing infection, and wear gloves if using fingers. Additionally, use tick control products regularly as advised by a veterinarian to prevent ticks from attaching.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes for ticks, then use a pair of tweezers to grasp the tick's head where it attaches to the skin and pull gently and steadily. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Avoid yanking the tick away quickly to prevent leaving the mouth behind, which can cause infection.\", \"Answer: To remove a tick from a dog, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull gently and steadily. Wear gloves if using fingers, and avoid yanking to prevent leaving the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause infection. Also, check inside and behind the dog’s ears and around the eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull gently and steadily. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Avoid yanking the tick too quickly to prevent leaving the mouth behind, which can cause infection.\"]", "time_sec": 35.179, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 73.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "334", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps: 1) Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes, as these are common tick hiding places. 2) Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. 3) Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. 4) Gently and steadily pull on the tick to remove it. Avoid yanking the tick away too quickly, as this may leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps: 1) Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes, as these are common tick hiding places. 2) Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. 3) Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. 4) Gently and steadily pull on the tick to remove it. Avoid yanking the tick away too quickly, as this may leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps: 1) Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes, as these are common tick hiding places. 2) Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. 3) Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. 4) Gently and steadily pull on the tick to remove it. Avoid yanking the tick away too quickly, as this may leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull gently and steadily. Check inside and behind the dog’s ears and around the eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Avoid yanking the tick quickly to prevent leaving the mouthparts behind, which can cause infection.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps: use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, wear gloves if using fingers, and pull the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving the mouth behind, which can cause infection; also, check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes for ticks, and consult a veterinarian for tick control products to prevent future tick attachments.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps: check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and wear gloves if planning to use fingers. Pull the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving the mouth behind and causing infection, and check inside and behind the dog’s ears and around the eyes, which are favorite tick hiding places.\"]", "time_sec": 35.885, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "335", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, which are common hiding places for ticks. (Passage 1)\n2. Use tick control products recommended by a veterinarian to prevent ticks from attaching to the dog. (Passage 2)\n3. Remove ticks from the dog using a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages whether there are any specific products or methods for getting rid of ticks from dogs that are already infested.", "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving the tick's mouth behind, which can cause infection. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Regular use of tick control products, as advised by a veterinarian, is the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to dogs.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving the tick's mouth behind, which can cause infection. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Regular use of tick control products, as advised by a veterinarian, is the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to dogs.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving the tick's mouth behind, which can cause infection. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Regular use of tick control products, as advised by a veterinarian, is the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to dogs.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull gently and steadily. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around his eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Avoid yanking the tick quickly to prevent leaving the mouth behind and causing infection.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps: 1) Check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. 2) Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. 3) Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. 4) Pull on the tick gently and steadily, avoiding yanking it away too quickly to prevent leaving part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull gently and steadily. Check inside and behind the dog’s ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Avoid yanking the tick quickly to prevent leaving the mouthparts behind and causing infection.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving the mouth behind, and check inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places.\"]", "time_sec": 35.851, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "337", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check your dog's body thoroughly, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, around the eyes, and other favorite tick hiding places.\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and wear gloves if needed.\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily, making sure not to yank it away from your dog too quickly.\n4. Regularly use tick control products on your dog, as recommended by your veterinarian, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog in the first place.\n\nIf you have any further questions or concerns, consult your veterinarian for advice.", "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull gently and steadily. Check inside and behind the dog’s ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Avoid yanking the tick quickly to prevent leaving the mouth behind, which can cause infection. Regular use of tick control products, as advised by a veterinarian, is recommended for prevention.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull gently and steadily. Check inside and behind the dog’s ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Avoid yanking the tick quickly to prevent leaving the mouth behind, which can cause infection. Regular use of tick control products, as advised by a veterinarian, is recommended for prevention.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull gently and steadily. Check inside and behind the dog’s ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Avoid yanking the tick quickly to prevent leaving the mouth behind, which can cause infection. Regular use of tick control products, as advised by a veterinarian, is recommended for prevention.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving the mouth behind, and check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, which are favorite tick hiding places.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps: check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. Pull the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Additionally, prevent ticks by regularly using tick control products, as advised by a veterinarian, who can recommend the best product for your dog and situation.\", \"Answer: To remove a tick from a dog, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, wear gloves if using fingers, and pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving the tick’s mouth behind and causing an infection; additionally, check the dog’s ears, behind ears, and around the eyes for ticks, and prevent ticks by regularly using tick control products recommended by a veterinarian.\", \"Answer: To remove a tick from a dog, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull gently and steadily. Also, check inside and behind the dog's ears and around his eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Wear gloves if using fingers to remove the tick. To prevent ticks, use regular tick control products advised by a veterinarian, who can also recommend the best product for the dog and situation and is aware of local diseases that ticks may transmit to the dog.\"]", "time_sec": 38.429, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "338", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs with a knife. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them. Afterwards, line a baking pan with heavy duty foil. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer for heat circulation on all sides. Mix mustard and liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to make sure it adheres to the meat. To grill the ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and remove the ribs from the foil. Place them meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes. Continue this process until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 7.411, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "339", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Then, brush both sides of the ribs with a mixture of mustard and liquid smoke. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure it sticks to the meat. Next, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and place the ribs on the grill, meaty-side up. Brush the ribs with sauce, cover the grill, and cook for 5 minutes. Flip the ribs, brush with more sauce, and cook for another 5 minutes. Repeat this process, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 7.409, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "340", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\nTo grill the ribs:\n\n1. Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium temperature (350°F to 450°F).\n2. Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\n3. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\n4. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes.\n5. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\n\nTo prepare the ribs before grilling:\n\n1. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\n2. Season the ribs by mixing the mustard and liquid smoke (if using), and brushing the ribs on both sides.\n3. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\n\nFor oven-cooked BBQ ribs:\n\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag.\n3. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover the ribs.\n4. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil.\n5. Place the ribs in the baking pan and bake at 350°F for 2-3 hours, or until the ribs are tender and the meat starts to pull away from the bone.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 7.146, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 2.61, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "341", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ribs:\n\nStep 1: Prepare the ribs\n\n* Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs (passage 3)\n* Season the ribs with a dry rub and mustard mixture (passage 2)\n\nStep 2: Grill the ribs\n\n* Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium heat (passage 1)\n* Place the ribs meaty-side up on the grill and brush with some of the sauce (passage 1)\n* Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush the ribs with more sauce (passage 1)\n* Continue to cook and flip every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through (passage 1)\n\nTotal grilling time: 20 minutes\n\nNote: The passages do not mention the temperature at which to cook the ribs, but a medium heat of 350°F to 450°F is suggested.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 7.014, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.06, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "342", "question": "when you have a bowel movement do you lose weight", "gt": "While you may technically lose a small amount of weight after a bowel movement, this does not come from a loss of body fat. The decrease in body weight does not come from fat loss in stools, but rather from the elimination of undigested food and waste. Weight loss is primarily tied to your caloric intake and expenditure, not bowel movements. Unless your scale is highly accurate, you're unlikely to notice a difference in your body weight before and after a bowel movement.", "pred": "Yes, you do lose a small amount of weight when you have a bowel movement, but this is not due to a loss of body fat. The weight lost comes from the mass of the stool itself, which includes water and undigested dietary fiber. The passage states that \"A decrease in body weight after having a bowel movement does not come from a loss of body fat in stools.\" Body fat loss occurs through creating a calorie deficit, not from the elimination of waste. The passage also notes that \"the fat in stools does not come from a loss of body fat, but rather from dietary fat intake that is not properly absorbed,\" indicating that the weight lost is primarily from the stool's mass, not from fat stores in the body.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Yes, you do lose a small amount of weight when you have a bowel movement, but this is not due to a loss of body fat. The weight lost comes from the mass of the stool itself, which includes water and undigested dietary fiber. The passage states that \"A decrease in body weight after having a bowel movement does not come from a loss of body fat in stools.\" Body fat loss occurs through creating a calorie deficit, not from the elimination of waste. The passage also notes that \"the fat in stools does not come from a loss of body fat, but rather from dietary fat intake that is not properly absorbed,\" indicating that the weight lost is primarily from the stool's mass, not from fat stores in the body.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Yes, you do lose a small amount of weight when you have a bowel movement, but this is not due to a loss of body fat. The weight lost comes from the mass of the stool itself, which includes water and undigested dietary fiber. The passage states that \\\"A decrease in body weight after having a bowel movement does not come from a loss of body fat in stools.\\\" Body fat loss occurs through creating a calorie deficit, not from the elimination of waste. The passage also notes that \\\"the fat in stools does not come from a loss of body fat, but rather from dietary fat intake that is not properly absorbed,\\\" indicating that the weight lost is primarily from the stool's mass, not from fat stores in the body.\", \"Yes, you do lose a small amount of weight when you have a bowel movement, but this weight loss is not from body fat. The passages explain that a decrease in body weight after a bowel movement is due to the elimination of waste (including some dietary fat that was not properly absorbed), not from a loss of body fat. Body fat loss occurs through creating a calorie deficit, which forces the body to burn stored fat for energy. The passages also note that unless the scale is highly accurate, the weight difference from a bowel movement is unlikely to be noticeable. \\n\\nAnswer: Yes, you lose a small amount of weight from waste elimination, but this is not from body fat loss.\", \"Answer: Yes, you lose a small amount of weight when you have a bowel movement, but it is not due to a loss of body fat. The weight lost comes from the elimination of waste and water, not from fat loss. Body fat loss occurs through creating a calorie deficit, which forces the body to burn stored fat for energy. The weight loss from a bowel movement is temporary and does not reflect a significant or lasting change in body weight.\", \"Answer: Yes, you do lose a small amount of weight when you have a bowel movement, but it is not due to a loss of body fat. The weight lost comes from the elimination of waste and water from your body, not from a calorie deficit that results in fat loss. The passages explain that body fat loss occurs through creating a calorie deficit, which forces the body to burn stored fat for energy. The weight you might see on the scale after a bowel movement is simply the weight of the stool and the water it contains, and any noticeable change in weight would depend on the accuracy of the scale.\", \"Yes, you do lose a small amount of weight when you have a bowel movement, but this is not due to a loss of body fat. The weight lost comes from the waste in your intestines, which consists of water, undigested food, and some fat that was not properly absorbed from your diet. This weight is quickly regained when you eat and drink again. True weight loss, specifically the loss of body fat, occurs through creating a calorie deficit, where your body burns more calories than it consumes, forcing it to use stored fat for energy.\"]", "time_sec": 47.655, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
