{"id": "395", "question": "why should we serve others", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"Why should we serve others?\"\n\nWe should serve others because it is a way to show love and kindness to everyone, even those who may not treat us well. Serving others is an expression of our love for God and our desire to be like Him. When we truly know God, our natural response is a desire to love and serve Him in return, and serving others is a way to do so. Additionally, serving others without self-serving motives and expecting nothing in return allows us to serve out of love and build stronger character muscles.\n\nTherefore, serving others is not only a way to show love and kindness, but it is also a way to deepen our relationship with God and grow in our faith.", "pred": "We should serve others because we are called to love our neighbour as ourselves (Matthew 22:39) and to show love and kindness to everyone, even those who do not treat us well (passage 1). The spirit of service should be evident in all aspects of our work, including providing a “Second Mile Service” that goes the extra mile for customers and employers (passage 1). Serving others out of love, without self‑serving motives or expectations, reflects a proper relationship with God and aligns with His intention for us (passage 3).", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: We should serve others because we are called to love our neighbour as ourselves (Matthew 22:39) and to show love and kindness to everyone, even those who do not treat us well (passage 1). The spirit of service should be evident in all aspects of our work, including providing a “Second Mile Service” that goes the extra mile for customers and employers (passage 1). Serving others out of love, without self‑serving motives or expectations, reflects a proper relationship with God and aligns with His intention for us (passage 3).", "cot": "[\"Answer: We should serve others because we are called to love our neighbour as ourselves (Matthew 22:39) and to show love and kindness to everyone, even those who do not treat us well (passage 1). The spirit of service should be evident in all aspects of our work, including providing a “Second Mile Service” that goes the extra mile for customers and employers (passage 1). Serving others out of love, without self‑serving motives or expectations, reflects a proper relationship with God and aligns with His intention for us (passage 3).\", \"Answer: We should serve others as an expression of love and kindness, reflecting the Christian principle of \\\"Love your neighbour as yourself\\\" (Matthew 22:39). The Christian life emphasizes service to others in all aspects of work and relationships, including going \\\"the extra mile\\\" (Second Mile Service) even when not required, as taught in Matthew 5:41 (\\\"If anyone forces you to go one mile, go with them two miles\\\"). Serving others properly—motivated by love without self-interest or expectations—aligns with God’s intention for believers to serve out of genuine care, not selfish motives, and strengthens character while honoring God’s design for relationships.\", \"Answer: We should serve others as a way to show love and kindness, reflecting the Christian principle of \\\"Love your neighbour as yourself\\\" (Matthew 22:39). The passages emphasize that service should be selfless and motivated by love, not by personal gain. For example, serving others \\\"goes the extra mile\\\" (Second Mile Service) and involves helping everyone, even those who treat us poorly. This aligns with Jesus’ teaching to \\\"go with them two miles\\\" if forced to go one, demonstrating generosity and compassion. The Bible also connects genuine service to knowing God, as a relationship with Him (who is love, 1 John 4:8) naturally leads to serving Him and others out of love, not self-interest.\", \"Answer: We should serve others because we are called to love our neighbour as ourselves (Matthew 22:39) and to serve out of love with no expectations of reward. The Christian life is one of service to others, showing love and kindness even to those who do not treat us well, and using every opportunity to serve. This includes providing a “Second Mile Service” that goes the extra mile for customers and employers, reflecting the spirit of service in all aspects of work.\", \"Answer: We should serve others because the Christian life is one of service to others, where we show love and kindness to everyone, even to those who do not treat us well, as taught in Matthew 22:39 and demonstrated through practices like Second Mile Service, which involves going the extra mile for customers and employers.\"]", "time_sec": 44.71, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.46, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "399", "question": "temperature bucharest", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the current temperature in Bucharest, Romania is:\n\nPassage 1 does not provide real-time weather data, so I cannot find the current temperature in Bucharest.\n\nPassage 2 provides a map of UK weather warnings and flood warnings, but it does not provide information on the temperature in Bucharest.\n\nPassage 3 provides general information about the climate in Bucharest, including the average monthly weather patterns, but it does not provide the current temperature. Therefore, I am unable to answer your question based on these passages.", "pred": "In Bucharest, Romania, winter temperatures often dip below 0 °C (32 °F), sometimes reaching as low as -20 °C (4 °F), while summer temperatures average around 23 °C (73 °F) in July and August, with mid-summer highs frequently reaching 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F).", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: In Bucharest, Romania, winter temperatures often dip below 0 °C (32 °F), sometimes reaching as low as -20 °C (4 °F), while summer temperatures average around 23 °C (73 °F) in July and August, with mid-summer highs frequently reaching 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F).", "cot": "[\"Answer: In Bucharest, Romania, winter temperatures often dip below 0 °C (32 °F), sometimes reaching as low as -20 °C (4 °F), while summer temperatures average around 23 °C (73 °F) in July and August, with mid-summer highs frequently reaching 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F).\", \"Answer: The temperature in Bucharest can dip below 0 °C (32 °F) in winter, sometimes reaching as low as –20 °C (4 °F), while summer temperatures average around 23 °C (73 °F) and can rise to 35 °C (95 °F) or even 40 °C (104 °F) in mid‑summer.\", \"Answer: Temperature in Bucharest can dip below 0 °C (32 °F) in winter, sometimes reaching as low as –20 °C (4 °F), while summer temperatures average around 23 °C (73 °F) and can peak at 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid‑summer.\", \"Answer: The temperature in Bucharest varies seasonally. Winters can be windy with temperatures often below 0 °C (32 °F), sometimes dropping to as low as –20 °C (4 °F). In summer (July and August), average temperatures are around 23 °C (73 °F), with peak mid‑summer temperatures reaching 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F).\", \"Answer: The average temperature in Bucharest during summer (July and August) is around 23 °C (73 °F), with mid-summer temperatures often reaching 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F). In winter, temperatures frequently drop below 0 °C (32 °F), sometimes as low as minus 20 °C (4 °F).\"]", "time_sec": 36.9, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "400", "question": "temperature bucharest", "gt": "Based on passage 3, the average temperature in Bucharest, Romania during July and August is around 23 °C (73 °F). Temperatures can also reach 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.", "pred": "Bucharest, Romania has a humid continental climate with winter temperatures often dipping below 0 °C (32 °F), sometimes reaching minus 20 °C (4 °F), and summer (July and August) average temperatures around 23 °C (73 °F), with mid-summer highs reaching 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F).", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Bucharest, Romania has a humid continental climate with winter temperatures often dipping below 0 °C (32 °F), sometimes reaching minus 20 °C (4 °F), and summer (July and August) average temperatures around 23 °C (73 °F), with mid-summer highs reaching 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F).", "cot": "[\"Answer: Bucharest, Romania has a humid continental climate with winter temperatures often dipping below 0 °C (32 °F), sometimes reaching minus 20 °C (4 °F), and summer (July and August) average temperatures around 23 °C (73 °F), with mid-summer highs reaching 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F).\", \"Answer: Based on the provided passages, the temperature in Bucharest varies significantly by season. In winter, temperatures often dip below 0 °C (32 °F) and can drop to as low as -20 °C (4 °F). In summer (July and August), the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F), with mid-summer temperatures often reaching 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F).\", \"Answer: Temperature in Bucharest can dip below 0 °C (32 °F) in winter, sometimes reaching as low as minus 20 °C (4 °F), while summer temperatures average around 23 °C (73 °F) and often reach 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.\", \"Answer: Based on the provided passages, the temperature in Bucharest, Romania varies seasonally. In winter, temperatures often dip below 0 °C (32 °F) and can drop to as low as -20 °C (4 °F). In summer (July and August), the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F), with mid-summer temperatures often reaching 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F).\", \"Answer: The temperature in Bucharest varies significantly by season. Winters are often windy with temperatures frequently dipping below 0 °C (32 °F) and sometimes reaching as low as –20 °C (4 °F). In summer, average temperatures are about 23 °C (73 °F), with mid‑summer highs often reaching 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F).\"]", "time_sec": 38.566, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
