{"id": "422", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, a barcode symbology used extensively in multiple countries including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and in Europe. It is used for tracking trade items in stores. UPC consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. It is primarily used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "pred": "The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that consists of 12 numeric digits uniquely assigned to each trade item, used for tracking trade items in stores worldwide, particularly in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, Europe, and other countries, and is primarily used for scanning at the point of sale per GS1 specifications, as described in passage 1.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that consists of 12 numeric digits uniquely assigned to each trade item, used for tracking trade items in stores worldwide, particularly in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, Europe, and other countries, and is primarily used for scanning at the point of sale per GS1 specifications, as described in passage 1.", "cot": "[\"Answer: The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that consists of 12 numeric digits uniquely assigned to each trade item, used for tracking trade items in stores worldwide, particularly in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, Europe, and other countries, and is primarily used for scanning at the point of sale per GS1 specifications, as described in passage 1.\", \"Answer: The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that consists of 12 numeric digits uniquely assigned to each trade item. It is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, Europe, and other countries for tracking trade items in stores, particularly for scanning at the point of sale as specified by GS1.\", \"Answer: The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology consisting of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. It is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, Europe, and other countries for tracking trade items in stores and is the barcode mainly used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale, per GS1 specifications.\", \"Answer: The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that consists of 12 numeric digits uniquely assigned to each trade item, widely used in multiple countries for tracking trade items in stores and scanning at point-of-sale per GS1 specifications.\", \"Answer: The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores, consisting of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item, and is primarily used for point-of-sale scanning as per GS1 specifications.\"]", "time_sec": 28.673, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 83.52, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
