e) instead of \\\"Paris\\\" in the region field to search Paris and its suburbs. Additionally, you can contact the town hall in the person's city of birth if they were born in cities like Paris, Avignon, Bordeaux, Lyon, or Nice, especially if you have their middle name to narrow down the search.\", \"Answer: To find someone in France, you can use the French white pages (Pages Blanches) at www.pagesjaunes.fr. Enter the person's last name in the \\\"Nom\\\" field and their first name in the \\\"Prenom\\\" field if known. If you have an address, input it in the \\\"Ou\\\" section; otherwise, leave it blank to search the entire country. Additionally, for searching in Paris and its suburbs, use \\\"IDF\\\" or \\\"Ile de France\\\" in the department or region field instead of \\\"Paris.\\\" You can also send an email or letter to the town hall in the city of birth if the person was born there, and try to find their middle name for more accurate results. For more specific searches, consider posting a missed connection on Paris Craigslist.\", \"Answer: To find someone in France, you can use the French white pages (Pages Jaunes) by visiting www.pagesjaunes.fr. Enter the person's last name in the \\\"Nom\\\" field and their first name in the \\\"Prenom\\\" field if known. If you have an address, input it in the \\\"Ou\\\" section; otherwise, leave it blank to search the entire country. Click \\\"Trouver\\\" to view search results showing name, address, and phone number for matching listings. For more targeted searches, you can search for \\\"IDF\\\" (Ile de France) instead of \\\"Paris\\\" in the region field to cover Paris and its suburbs. Additionally, contacting the town hall in the person's city of birth via email or letter can be helpful, especially if you know their middle name to narrow down the search.\", \"Answer: To find someone in France, you can use the French white pages (Pages Jaunes) by visiting www.pagesjaunes.fr. Enter the person's last name in the Nom field and their first name in the Prenom field if known. You can also provide an address in the Ou section, or leave it blank to search the entire country. For Paris and its suburbs, enter IDF (Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field instead of typing Paris. If you have lost contact with someone for over ten or twenty years, pictures from a people search website may not help; try to find their middle name for better results. You can also send an email or letter to the town hall in the city where the person was born.\"]", "time_sec": 64.462, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.37, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "440", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "gt": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they help in the regeneration of the forest. Fires consume dead and decaying vegetation, clearing the way for new growth. Jack pines rely on fire to spread their seeds. They produce seratonous (resin-filled) cones that remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin, causing the cones to open and the seeds to fall or blow out. Furthermore, fires can disrupt the growth of other trees like spruce, providing an advantage to the more fire-tolerant jack pines and allowing them to proliferate.", "pred": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifer's seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then allows the jack pine to spread its seeds and regenerate.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifer's seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then allows the jack pine to spread its seeds and regenerate.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifer's seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then allows the jack pine to spread its seeds and regenerate.\", \"Fire is beneficial to conifers like jack pines because it melts the resin in their durable, seratonous cones, causing them to open and release seeds for new growth, which supports forest regeneration as stated by Hall. Answer: Fire melts the resin in jack pine cones, causing them to open and release seeds for new growth.\", \"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the jack pine's seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then fall or blow out to enable new growth, as stated in passage 2 and passage 3.\", \"Fire melts the resin in jack pine cones, causing them to open and release their seeds, which enables the species to spread and regenerate.\", \"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the trees' seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then fall or blow out to enable new growth; additionally, fires clear dead and decaying vegetation from the forest floor, creating space for new growth and allowing fire-tolerant species like jack pine and aspen to regain advantage when they die out due to competition from other trees like spruce.\"]", "time_sec": 26.616, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.48, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "443", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines in several ways:\n\n1. Fire helps to clear the way for new growth by consuming dead, decaying vegetation on the forest floor, creating a clean slate for seed germination and seedling establishment (Passage 2).\n2. Jack pine seeds are adapted to fire, as they are stored in serotinous cones that only open after a fire has melted the resin holding them closed. This allows the seeds to disperse and establish new populations (Passage 2).\n3. Fire can create a favorable environment for jack pine and aspen regrowth by reducing competition from other tree species, such as spruce, which have better access to sunlight while shading the other trees (Passage 3).\n\nTherefore, forest fires can benefit jack pines by providing a means of seed dispersal and creating conditions that promote their growth and regeneration.", "pred": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the cones, causing them to pop open and release seeds, which aids in the regeneration of the forest.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the cones, causing them to pop open and release seeds, which aids in the regeneration of the forest.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the cones, causing them to pop open and release seeds, which aids in the regeneration of the forest.\", \"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifers' durable, seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then fall or blow out to enable new growth; this process is essential for the regeneration of jack pine populations, as they rely on fire to spread their seeds, and fire also clears dead vegetation from the forest floor, creating favorable conditions for new growth.\", \"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifer's durable, seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds. This process enables the jack pine to spread its seeds and regenerate, as stated in passage 2.\", \"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the jack pine's seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then allows the seeds to fall or blow out and spread, aiding in the regeneration of the forest.\", \"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the tree's seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds. This process allows the seeds to fall or blow out, facilitating the spread and regeneration of jack pine species. As stated in passage 2, \\\"Some species, such as the jack pine, even rely on fire to spread their seeds.\\\"\"]", "time_sec": 29.136, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "444", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they help to clear away dead vegetation and promote new growth. According to passage 2, the jack pine produces serotonous cones that are dormant until a fire occurs, at which point they melt and release their seeds. This suggests that fire is a mechanism for the dispersal of jack pine seeds, and that the tree relies on fires to spread its seeds. Additionally, passage 3 suggests that while spruce trees may outcompete jack pine and aspen in some areas, fires can disrupt this cycle and allow jack pine and aspen to regain an advantage. Therefore, it seems that fires play a role in promoting the growth and survival of jack pine and other pioneer species in the boreal forest.", "pred": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifers' seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then fall or blow out to enable new growth; this is specifically noted for jack pine in the Canadian boreal forest, where fires serve as a mechanism for continual forest regeneration by clearing dead vegetation and creating conditions for new species to establish.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifers' seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then fall or blow out to enable new growth; this is specifically noted for jack pine in the Canadian boreal forest, where fires serve as a mechanism for continual forest regeneration by clearing dead vegetation and creating conditions for new species to establish.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifers' seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then fall or blow out to enable new growth; this is specifically noted for jack pine in the Canadian boreal forest, where fires serve as a mechanism for continual forest regeneration by clearing dead vegetation and creating conditions for new species to establish.\", \"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifer's durable, seratonous cones, causing them to pop open and release seeds, which then allows the seeds to fall or blow out and germinate, aiding in the regeneration of the forest.\", \"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the jack pine's seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then fall or blow out to enable new growth; this process is essential for the regeneration of jack pine populations, as they are fire-dependent species that rely on fire to spread their seeds.\", \"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the jack pine's seratonous cones, causing them to pop open and release seeds, which aids in seed dispersal and regeneration.\", \"Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the trees' seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds. This process allows the seeds to fall or blow out, facilitating the spread and regeneration of jack pine species. As stated in passage 2, \\\"The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.\\\"\"]", "time_sec": 31.852, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.