{"id": "467", "question": "benefits of hiking as a hobby facts", "gt": "Hiking as a hobby has numerous benefits for both the body and the mind. It is an inexpensive and accessible activity that can be enjoyed by individuals of all fitness levels. Hiking allows people to explore and discover beautiful natural areas, promoting a deeper connection with the environment. It also has positive effects on mental health, reducing stress and anxiety. Additionally, hiking is a cardiovascular activity that can improve overall fitness and reduce the risk of heart disease. Exposure to sunshine during hiking can also increase vitamin D levels in the body. Overall, hiking offers a wide range of benefits for individuals seeking physical and mental well-being.", "pred": "Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, including being inexpensive and accessible to all fitness levels. It promotes mental health by providing varied exercise compared to gym activities, increases vitamin D levels through sunshine exposure, supports cardiovascular health by reducing heart disease risk and improving fitness, and combats stress and anxiety through immersion in nature, as highlighted by Gregory A. Miller, PhD, president of the American Hiking Society.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, including being inexpensive and accessible to all fitness levels. It promotes mental health by providing varied exercise compared to gym activities, increases vitamin D levels through sunshine exposure, supports cardiovascular health by reducing heart disease risk and improving fitness, and combats stress and anxiety through immersion in nature, as highlighted by Gregory A. Miller, PhD, president of the American Hiking Society.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, including being inexpensive and accessible to all fitness levels. It promotes mental health by providing varied exercise compared to gym activities, increases vitamin D levels through sunshine exposure, supports cardiovascular health by reducing heart disease risk and improving fitness, and combats stress and anxiety through immersion in nature, as highlighted by Gregory A. Miller, PhD, president of the American Hiking Society.\", \"Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, including promoting mental health through varied exercise compared to gym activities, increasing vitamin D levels via sunshine exposure, improving cardiovascular health by reducing heart disease risk and enhancing overall fitness, and combating stress and anxiety symptoms, as highlighted by research from the American Hiking Society.\", \"Answer: Hiking as a hobby offers numerous benefits, including promoting mental health through varied outdoor exercise compared to gym activities, increasing vitamin D levels via sun exposure, providing cardiovascular benefits such as reduced heart disease risk and improved fitness, and combating stress and anxiety by engaging with nature, which is described as ingrained in human DNA.\", \"Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, is inexpensive and accessible to all fitness levels, promotes mental health through varied exercise compared to gym activities, increases vitamin D levels via sun exposure, provides cardiovascular benefits including reduced heart disease risk and improved fitness, and combats stress and anxiety by connecting individuals with nature, as highlighted by Gregory A. Miller of the American Hiking Society.\", \"Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits as a hobby, including promoting mental health through varied exercise compared to gym activities, increasing vitamin D levels via sun exposure, providing cardiovascular benefits that reduce heart disease risk and improve overall fitness, and combating stress and anxiety symptoms by connecting with nature, as stated by Gregory A. Miller of the American Hiking Society.\"]", "time_sec": 29.613, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "469", "question": "benefits of hiking as a hobby facts", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here are the benefits of hiking as a hobby:\n\n1. Outdoor hiking promotes mental health (Passage 1).\n2. Hiking can help increase your levels of vitamin D through exposure to sunshine (Passage 2).\n3. Hiking has a positive impact on combating symptoms of stress and anxiety (Passage 3).\n\nTherefore, the main benefits of hiking as a hobby are its positive effects on mental health, physical health, and stress reduction.", "pred": "Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, including promoting mental health through varied exercise compared to gym activities, increasing vitamin D levels via sun exposure, providing cardiovascular benefits that reduce heart disease risk and boost overall fitness, and combating stress and anxiety as confirmed by research and the American Hiking Society president.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, including promoting mental health through varied exercise compared to gym activities, increasing vitamin D levels via sun exposure, providing cardiovascular benefits that reduce heart disease risk and boost overall fitness, and combating stress and anxiety as confirmed by research and the American Hiking Society president.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, including promoting mental health through varied exercise compared to gym activities, increasing vitamin D levels via sun exposure, providing cardiovascular benefits that reduce heart disease risk and boost overall fitness, and combating stress and anxiety as confirmed by research and the American Hiking Society president.\", \"Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind. It is inexpensive, easy to start, and accessible regardless of current fitness level. Hiking promotes mental health by providing varied outdoor exercise compared to gym activities. Being exposed to sunshine increases vitamin D levels. As a cardiovascular activity, it supports heart health and overall fitness. Research indicates hiking helps combat stress and anxiety, with being in nature aligning with our innate connection to the environment.\", \"Answer: Hiking offers numerous benefits as a hobby, including being inexpensive and easy to start, making it accessible regardless of current fitness level. It provides mental health benefits by being more varied than gym-based exercise and helps combat stress and anxiety, as noted by Gregory A. Miller, PhD, president of the American Hiking Society, who states that being in nature is ingrained in our DNA. Additionally, hiking promotes cardiovascular health by reducing heart disease risk and increasing overall fitness, and exposure to sunshine during hikes boosts vitamin D levels.\", \"Answer: Hiking offers numerous benefits as a hobby, including promoting mental health through varied outdoor exercise, increasing vitamin D levels via sun exposure, improving cardiovascular health by reducing heart disease risk and boosting overall fitness, and combating stress and anxiety, as research indicates its positive impact on mental well-being.\", \"Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, is inexpensive and easy to start for all fitness levels, can be done near most people's homes, promotes mental health through varied outdoor exercise compared to gym activities, increases vitamin D levels via sun exposure, provides cardiovascular benefits including reduced heart disease risk and improved fitness, and combats stress and anxiety by connecting with nature as noted by Gregory A. Miller of the American Hiking Society.\"]", "time_sec": 32.759, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
