more varied than gym exercise, reduces stress and anxiety through exposure to nature, and supports cardiovascular health by lowering heart disease risk and improving overall fitness. Additionally, hiking increases vitamin D levels through sunshine exposure and provides opportunities to discover local natural areas.\", \"Answer: Hiking is an inexpensive and easy-to-start hobby suitable for all fitness levels, with most people having access to nearby hiking spots. It promotes mental health through varied outdoor exercise compared to gym activities, increases vitamin D levels via sun exposure, supports cardiovascular health by reducing heart disease risk and boosting fitness, and combats stress and anxiety by leveraging nature’s positive psychological impact as noted by Gregory A. Miller of the American Hiking Society.\", \"Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, is inexpensive and easy to start for all fitness levels, can be done near most people's homes, promotes mental health through varied outdoor exercise, increases vitamin D from sunshine exposure, provides cardiovascular benefits like reduced heart disease risk, and helps combat stress and anxiety by connecting with nature as noted by Gregory A. Miller of the American Hiking Society.\", \"Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, is inexpensive and accessible to all fitness levels, can be done near most residential areas, promotes mental health through varied outdoor exercise, increases vitamin D levels via sun exposure, supports cardiovascular health by reducing heart disease risk and improving fitness, and combats stress and anxiety by connecting individuals with nature, as noted by Gregory A. Miller of the American Hiking Society.\"]", "time_sec": 32.43, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "471", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, has no discernible taste or smell, and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F.", "pred": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a high smoke point of 450 degrees F, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, has a lower smoke point of 350 degrees F, and retains a distinct coconut aroma and flavor.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a high smoke point of 450 degrees F, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, has a lower smoke point of 350 degrees F, and retains a distinct coconut aroma and flavor.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a high smoke point of 450 degrees F, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, has a lower smoke point of 350 degrees F, and retains a distinct coconut aroma and flavor.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F, and retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma due to being unprocessed and not deodorized.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and undergoes a refining process that removes its distinct aroma and flavor, while unrefined (virgin) coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh and retains its mild coconut flavor and aroma. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it better suited for high-temperature cooking like frying.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil (also called pure or virgin) is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct coconut aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450°F vs. 350°F for unrefined), making it better suited for high-temperature cooking like frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and lacks a discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined coconut oil retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining, and refined coconut oil has no discernible taste or smell. Additionally, refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it better suited for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying.\"]", "time_sec": 36.787, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 74.07, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "473", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is the process used to extract it. Refined coconut oil is extracted from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is extracted from the flesh of the fresh coconut. Another difference is that refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point and is therefore better suited for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no taste or smell, while unrefined oil retains its distinctive coconut flavor and aroma.", "pred": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined (virgin) coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil retains a distinct coconut aroma and flavor, whereas refined coconut oil is deodorized, losing its coconut taste and smell. Additionally, refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point of 450°F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350°F, making refined coconut oil more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined (virgin) coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil retains a distinct coconut aroma and flavor, whereas refined coconut oil is deodorized, losing its coconut taste and smell. Additionally, refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point of 450°F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350°F, making refined coconut oil more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined (virgin) coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil retains a distinct coconut aroma and flavor, whereas refined coconut oil is deodorized, losing its coconut taste and smell. Additionally, refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point of 450°F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350°F, making refined coconut oil more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined (virgin) coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Refined oil has no distinct aroma or flavor because it is deodorized, whereas unrefined oil retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma. Additionally, refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450°F compared to unrefined coconut oil’s 350°F, making refined oil more suitable for high‑temperature cooking such as frying.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and undergoes processing that removes its coconut flavor and aroma, resulting in a neutral taste and odor. It has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking like frying. Unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts, retains a distinct coconut aroma and mild flavor, and is less heat-tolerant due to its lower smoking point.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and undergoes a process that removes its coconut flavor and aroma, while unrefined (virgin) coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh and retains a mild coconut taste and aroma. Refined oil has a higher smoking point (450°F) compared to unrefined (350°F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking like frying.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a high smoke point of 450 degrees F, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh and has a lower smoke point of 350 degrees F. Unrefined coconut oil retains a distinct coconut flavor and aroma, whereas refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no discernible taste or smell.\"]", "time_sec": 38.999, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 70.49, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "474", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are:\n\n1. Source: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\n2. Aroma and flavor: Unrefined coconut oil retains its distinct aroma and flavor, while refined coconut oil loses these qualities during the refining process.\n3. Smoking point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) than unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\n\nTherefore, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their source, aroma, flavor, and smoking point.", "pred": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined (pure or virgin) coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil retains a distinct coconut aroma and flavor, whereas refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its signature taste and smell. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point (450°F) compared to unrefined coconut oil (350°F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined (pure or virgin) coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil retains a distinct coconut aroma and flavor, whereas refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its signature taste and smell. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point (450°F) compared to unrefined coconut oil (350°F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined (pure or virgin) coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil retains a distinct coconut aroma and flavor, whereas refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its signature taste and smell. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point (450°F) compared to unrefined coconut oil (350°F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil (also called pure or virgin) is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct coconut aroma and flavor that is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it better suited for high-temperature cooking like frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined coconut oil retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and undergoes a refining process that removes its aroma, flavor, and smell, resulting in a neutral taste and a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking like frying. Unrefined coconut oil, also called pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts, retains a distinct coconut aroma and mild flavor, has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F, and is better suited for lower-temperature cooking methods.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and undergoes deodorization, resulting in a product with no distinct coconut flavor or smell and a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking like frying. Unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts, retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma, has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F, and is less suitable for high-temperature cooking. The key differences are in their source, processing, taste, aroma, and heat tolerance.\", \"Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a high smoke point of 450°F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking, while unrefined (virgin) coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma, has a lower smoke point of 350°F, and is better suited for lower-heat cooking methods.\"]", "time_sec": 42.576, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "478", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "Passage 3 provides information on how to change your address with the U.S. Postal Service. You can visit their website, call the USPS Call Center, or fill out and submit a form at a U.S. Post Office.", "pred": "Change your U.S. postal service address quickly and securely. The service is fast (as little as 1 minute), versatile (can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS), and secure (uses latest encryption technologies to protect data). You can change your address by: (1) visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ and paying a $1 credit/debit card charge for identity validation, (2) calling 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or (3) filling out and submitting PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office, mailing it, or giving it to a Postal Mail Carrier.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Change your U.S. postal service address quickly and securely. The service is fast (as little as 1 minute), versatile (can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS), and secure (uses latest encryption technologies to protect data). You can change your address by: (1) visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ and paying a $1 credit/debit card charge for identity validation, (2) calling 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or (3) filling out and submitting PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office, mailing it, or giving it to a Postal Mail Carrier.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Change your U.S. postal service address quickly and securely. The service is fast (as little as 1 minute), versatile (can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS), and secure (uses latest encryption technologies to protect data). You can change your address by: (1) visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ and paying a $1 credit/debit card charge for identity validation, (2) calling 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or (3) filling out and submitting PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office, mailing it, or giving it to a Postal Mail Carrier.\", \"Answer: The U.S. Postal Service allows you to change your postal address quickly, in as little as 1 minute, through various methods including online at https://moversguide.usps.com/, by calling 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or by filling out and submitting PS Form 3575, which can be obtained from any U.S. Post Office and submitted in person, mailed, or given to a postal carrier. This service is secure, using the latest encryption technologies to protect your data, and is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service.\", \"Answer: The U.S. Postal Service offers a fast, versatile, and secure Change of Address service. It can be completed in as little as 1 minute and allows you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. The service uses the latest encryption technologies to ensure data safety. You can change your address by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation charge), calling the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575, which can be picked up at any U.S. Post Office, mailed, or provided to a Postal Mail Carrier.\", \"Answer: Change your U.S. Postal Service address quickly and securely using the Postal Change of Address service, which can be completed in as little as 1 minute. The service is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS, and it uses the latest encryption technologies to ensure your data is safe. You can change your address by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation charge), calling the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575, which can be picked up at any U.S. Post Office, mailed, or given to a postal carrier. This service is especially important for businesses undergoing permanent moves, temporary relocations, or disaster-related address changes.\", \"Answer: Change your U.S. Postal Service address quickly and securely. The service allows you to change your address in as little as 1 minute and can notify up to 100 organizations, including the Postal Service itself. Your data is protected with the latest encryption technologies. You can change your address by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation charge), calling 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575, which can be obtained at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to a Post Office, or given to a Postal Mail Carrier. This service is useful for both permanent and temporary relocations, including business mail forwarding after disasters.\"]", "time_sec": 61.047, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
