ng latest encryption technologies). You can change your address by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation charge), calling 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575 (available at any U.S. Post Office, mailable to any Post Office, or deliverable to any Postal Mail Carrier).\", \"Answer: Change your U.S. postal service address quickly and securely with the USPS Change of Address service, which can be completed in as little as 1 minute. You can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service, and your data is protected by the latest encryption technologies. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation fee), call 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office, mail it to a Post Office, or give it to a Postal Mail Carrier.\", \"Answer: You can change your U.S. Postal Service address in as little as 1 minute using the Postal Change of Address service, which is fast, versatile (notifying up to 100 organizations), and secure (using latest encryption technologies). Methods to change your address include visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation fee), calling 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office, mailing it, or providing it to a Postal Mail Carrier.\", \"Answer: Change your U.S. Postal Service address quickly and securely with features like fast processing (as little as 1 minute), versatility in notifying up to 100 organizations, and enhanced security through encryption technologies. You can change your address by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation fee), calling 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office, mailing it, or providing it to a Postal Mail Carrier.\", \"Answer: Change your postal service address in 1 minute 