{"id": "480", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"change of address u.s. postal service\":\n\nTo change your address with the U.S. Postal Service, you can visit the USPS website (moversguide.usps.com), call the USPS Call Center (1-800-ASK-USPS), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. You can also use the USPS change of address feature to notify up to 100 organizations, including the Postal Service, with secure encryption technology to protect your data.", "pred": "Change your U.S. postal address with the USPS service that allows you to complete the change in as little as 1 minute. You can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service, and your data is secured with the latest encryption technologies. The service includes three methods for changing your address: visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation charge), call 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be obtained at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to a Post Office, or given to a Postal Mail Carrier. This service is useful for permanent moves, temporary relocations, or business mail forwarding after disasters.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Change your U.S. postal address with the USPS service that allows you to complete the change in as little as 1 minute. You can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service, and your data is secured with the latest encryption technologies. The service includes three methods for changing your address: visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation charge), call 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be obtained at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to a Post Office, or given to a Postal Mail Carrier. This service is useful for permanent moves, temporary relocations, or business mail forwarding after disasters.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Change your U.S. postal address with the USPS service that allows you to complete the change in as little as 1 minute. You can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service, and your data is secured with the latest encryption technologies. The service includes three methods for changing your address: visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation charge), call 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be obtained at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to a Post Office, or given to a Postal Mail Carrier. This service is useful for permanent moves, temporary relocations, or business mail forwarding after disasters.\", \"Answer: Change your U.S. Postal Service address quickly and securely with features like fast processing (as little as 1 minute), versatility in notifying up to 100 organizations, and enhanced security through encryption. Methods to change your address include visiting the USPS Mover’s Guide website (with identity validation via a $1 credit/debit card charge), calling 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or completing and submitting PS Form 3575 at any Post Office, mailing it, or providing it to a postal carrier.\", \"Answer: Change your U.S. postal address quickly (as little as 1 minute) using the Postal Service's Fast, Versatile, and Secure Change of Address service. You can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS, with data protected by the latest encryption technologies. To change your address, you can: 1) Visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ and pay a $1 identity validation fee; 2) Call the USPS at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777); or 3) Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, available at any U.S. Post Office, by mail, or to a Postal Mail Carrier.\", \"Answer: Change your U.S. Postal Service address quickly and securely using the Postal Change of Address service, which can be completed in as little as 1 minute. The service is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS, and it uses the latest encryption technologies to ensure your data is safe. You can change your address by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation fee), calling the USPS Call Center at 1-800-275-8777, or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office, mailing it, or providing it to a Postal Mail Carrier.\", \"Answer: Change your U.S. postal service address quickly and securely with the USPS Change of Address service, which can be completed in as little as 1 minute. The service is fast, versatile (allowing notification to up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS), and secure (using latest encryption technologies to protect data). You can change your address through three methods: (1) Visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ and pay a $1 identity validation fee with a credit/debit card; (2) Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777); or (3) Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be obtained at any U.S. Post Office and submitted in person, mailed, or provided to a postal carrier.\"]", "time_sec": 60.28, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.47, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "481", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "gt": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked if you have used third-party apps to access Snapchat. The company does not guarantee your security when using these apps and may send you a warning message before locking your account. If you have been warned multiple times and continue using third-party apps, your account may remain locked.", "pred": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat’s terms of service and can trigger warnings or a lockout.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat’s terms of service and can trigger warnings or a lockout.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat’s terms of service and can trigger warnings or a lockout.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat’s terms and can trigger a lock.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third‑party apps to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat’s policies and can lead to warnings or a lock. The passages note that using third‑party apps may trigger a lock, that users have been warned multiple times (e.g., “more than 4 times”) before being locked, and that Snapchat is taking steps to punish those who use such apps.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third‑party apps to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat’s terms and can trigger a lock. The passages state that using third‑party applications puts your account at risk, may cause Snapchat to send a warning, and can result in the account being locked.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third-party applications to access the platform. Passage 1 states that \\\"if you used third-party apps to get into snapchat and they warned you more them 4 times then yes your account is locked,\\\" and Passage 2 confirms that \\\"if you have been locked out of your account and don’t know why, using third party apps may be a reason.\\\" Additionally, Passage 3 notes that \\\"200,000 private Snapchat photos were leaked via one of the photo messaging app's many third-party apps,\\\" indicating Snapchat's strict stance against third-party app usage. The passages consistently identify third-party app usage as the cause of account locks, with no other reasons specified in the provided text.\"]", "time_sec": 31.215, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "482", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "gt": "Based on the given passages, Snapchat may temporarily lock an account if the user has been using third-party applications to access the app. These third-party apps can compromise the security of the account and put the user and their friends at risk. Snapchat may send a warning message before locking the account, but if the user continues to use third-party apps, their account may be locked.", "pred": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third-party apps to access it, which violates Snapchat's policies and puts your account and possibly your friends at risk. The passages indicate that Snapchat locks accounts when users employ third-party applications, with examples including receiving warnings (e.g., \"they warned me 3 times\" and \"they warned me more them 4 times\") and the company taking steps to \"punish individuals who use those apps\" after incidents like the \"200,000 private Snapchat photos were leaked via one of the photo messaging app's many third-party apps.\"", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third-party apps to access it, which violates Snapchat's policies and puts your account and possibly your friends at risk. The passages indicate that Snapchat locks accounts when users employ third-party applications, with examples including receiving warnings (e.g., \"they warned me 3 times\" and \"they warned me more them 4 times\") and the company taking steps to \"punish individuals who use those apps\" after incidents like the \"200,000 private Snapchat photos were leaked via one of the photo messaging app's many third-party apps.\"", "cot": "[\"Answer: Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third-party apps to access it, which violates Snapchat's policies and puts your account and possibly your friends at risk. The passages indicate that Snapchat locks accounts when users employ third-party applications, with examples including receiving warnings (e.g., \\\"they warned me 3 times\\\" and \\\"they warned me more them 4 times\\\") and the company taking steps to \\\"punish individuals who use those apps\\\" after incidents like the \\\"200,000 private Snapchat photos were leaked via one of the photo messaging app's many third-party apps.\\\"\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access Snapchat. The platform warns users that using such apps puts their account at risk, and repeated warnings (e.g., three warnings) can lead to a lock.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access Snapchat. The platform warns users that using such apps can lead to account lockouts, and multiple warnings (e.g., three warnings) may result in the account being locked.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third-party applications to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat's policies. The first passage states that if third-party apps warn you more than 4 times, your account will be locked, and you experienced this with 3 warnings. The second passage confirms that using third-party apps can lead to account locks, as Snapchat may send warnings before locking accounts. Additionally, the third passage highlights that Snapchat is taking action against users of third-party apps due to security risks, such as the 200,000 private photos leaked through such apps. Therefore, using unauthorized third-party apps is the reason for your temporary lock.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used a third-party application to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat's policies and puts your account and potentially your friends at risk.\"]", "time_sec": 33.215, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.2, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "483", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that Snapchat may lock accounts that use third-party applications to access the platform more than four times. If a user has been locked out of their account and doesn't know why, using third-party apps may be a reason. Third-party apps are applications that are not developed or officially supported by Snapchat, such as third-party messaging or camera apps. Using these apps may put the user's account at risk, as well as their friends'. Additionally, there are many reasons why people are getting locked out of Snapchat, including using third-party apps.", "pred": "Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third-party applications to access Snapchat. The passages state that using third-party apps puts your account at risk, may result in a lock, and Snapchat may send a warning message before locking the account. For example, one user was warned three times before their account locked, and another user was told they were using third-party applications when they tried to log in. Additionally, Snapchat mentioned that 200,000 private photos were leaked through third-party apps, leading the company to take steps to punish users who use those apps.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third-party applications to access Snapchat. The passages state that using third-party apps puts your account at risk, may result in a lock, and Snapchat may send a warning message before locking the account. For example, one user was warned three times before their account locked, and another user was told they were using third-party applications when they tried to log in. Additionally, Snapchat mentioned that 200,000 private photos were leaked through third-party apps, leading the company to take steps to punish users who use those apps.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third-party applications to access Snapchat. The passages state that using third-party apps puts your account at risk, may result in a lock, and Snapchat may send a warning message before locking the account. For example, one user was warned three times before their account locked, and another user was told they were using third-party applications when they tried to log in. Additionally, Snapchat mentioned that 200,000 private photos were leaked through third-party apps, leading the company to take steps to punish users who use those apps.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access the service. The passages state that using such third‑party apps can trigger a lock, often after multiple warnings, and that uninstalling the third‑party app and waiting for an official Snapchat update is the recommended remedy.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access the service. The passages indicate that using such third‑party apps can trigger a lock, often after multiple warnings, and that uninstalling the third‑party app and waiting for an official Snapchat update is the recommended remedy.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third-party apps to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat's policies. The passages indicate that using third-party apps can lead to account lockouts, including warnings before locking and potential permanent suspension. For example, passage 1 describes users being locked after third-party apps warned them multiple times, and passage 3 states that Snapchat is taking steps to punish individuals who use such apps due to security risks, like the 200,000 private photos leaked via third-party apps.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third-party applications to access Snapchat. The first passage states that if third-party apps warn you more than 4 times, your account gets locked. The second passage explains that Snapchat may lock accounts for using third-party apps and typically sends a warning message beforehand. The third passage confirms this by mentioning that Snapchat is taking steps to punish individuals who use third-party apps, which led to the leak of 200,000 private photos. Therefore, using third-party apps is the reason your account is temporarily locked.\"]", "time_sec": 37.943, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.8, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "484", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is why your Snapchat account might be temporarily locked:\n\n1. Using third-party apps to access Snapchat without authorization: According to passage 2, Snapchat does not guarantee the security of accounts accessed through third-party apps. If you have been using such apps, it could result in your account being locked.\n2. Exceeding the limit of warnings for third-party app usage: Passage 1 mentions that Snapchat sends warnings before locking accounts that use third-party apps excessively. If you have exceeded the limit of warnings, your account might be temporarily locked.\n\nTherefore, the most likely reason for your Snapchat account being temporarily locked is due to the unauthorized use of third-party apps.", "pred": "Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access the service, which violates Snapchat’s policies and can trigger a warning or lock.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access the service, which violates Snapchat’s policies and can trigger a warning or lock.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access the service, which violates Snapchat’s policies and can trigger a warning or lock.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used a third‑party app to access Snapchat. The passages indicate that using third‑party applications can trigger a lock, and they warn users that such activity puts accounts at risk of being locked.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third-party applications to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat's security policies. As stated in the passages, Snapchat warns users about using third-party apps and may lock accounts to protect user security. For example, passage 2 mentions that \\\"if you have been locked out of your account and don’t know why, using third party apps may be a reason,\\\" and passage 3 notes that \\\"200,000 private Snapchat photos were leaked via one of the photo messaging app's many third-party apps\\\" leading to Snapchat taking steps to \\\"punish individuals who use those apps.\\\"\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access Snapchat. The passages indicate that using such third‑party apps can trigger a lock, often after multiple warnings, and that uninstalling the third‑party app and waiting for an official Snapchat app (e.g., for Windows Phone) may resolve the issue.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used a third-party application to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat's policies and puts your account and possibly your friends at risk. The passages indicate that Snapchat may lock accounts for using third-party apps, often after sending a warning message, and in one instance, 200,000 private Snapchat photos were leaked via a third-party app, leading the company to take steps to punish users of those apps.\"]", "time_sec": 31.802, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 13.08, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "485", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, it appears that your Snapchat account has been temporarily locked due to using third-party apps. According to passage 2, Snapchat does not guarantee security when using third-party apps, and they may lock your account if they detect such usage. Passage 3 also mentions that Snapchat has taken steps to punish individuals who use third-party apps, which could result in account lockout.\n\nIt's possible that you have been warned multiple times by Snapchat about using third-party apps, as mentioned in passage 1, and your account has been locked as a result. To regain access to your account, you may need to stop using third-party apps and wait for an official Snapchat app to become available for your device, as suggested in passage 2.", "pred": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third-party applications to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat's terms of service and poses security risks, as warned by Snapchat in the passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third-party applications to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat's terms of service and poses security risks, as warned by Snapchat in the passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third-party applications to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat's terms of service and poses security risks, as warned by Snapchat in the passages.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third-party apps to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat's security policies. The passages indicate that Snapchat warns users multiple times before locking accounts due to third-party app usage, and using such apps can also lead to risks like private photos being leaked (as seen when 200,000 private Snapchat photos were leaked via third-party apps).\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used a third-party application to access it, which violates Snapchat's policies and poses security risks, as stated in the passages. Passage 1 describes users being locked after third-party apps warned them multiple times (e.g., \\\"they warned you more them 4 times then yes your account is locked\\\"), and passage 2 confirms that \\\"using third party apps may be a reason\\\" for being locked out. Passage 3 also highlights the risks, noting that \\\"200,000 private Snapchat photos were leaked via one of the photo messaging app's many third-party apps\\\" and that Snapchat is taking steps to punish users of such apps.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used third‑party applications to access the service. The passages indicate that using such third‑party apps can trigger warnings or lockouts, and they advise uninstalling the unauthorized app and waiting for an official Snapchat update.\", \"Answer: Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked because you used third-party applications to access Snapchat, which violates Snapchat's policies and can lead to account restrictions or temporary locks. This is supported by passage 2, which states that using third-party apps may be a reason for being locked out of your account, and passage 3, which mentions that Snapchat is taking steps to punish individuals who use third-party apps after a significant leak of private photos via such apps. Passage 1 also indicates that users have experienced account locks after receiving warnings about third-party app usage.\"]", "time_sec": 35.593, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 23.53, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "488", "question": "how to plan a trip to germany", "gt": "To plan a trip to Germany, it is important to plan ahead and be aware of the rules and regulations regarding travel with pets. It is also recommended to research the best ways to save money during your trip, such as looking into discounted flights, cheap hotels and hostels, and affordable dining options. Additionally, learning about German life and culture can enhance your overall trip experience.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 7.326, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "489", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "You can see who liked your tweets by using tracking websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These sites can give you an idea of who is favouriting your tweets. Alternatively, you can also set up notifications on Twitter itself. By going to your account settings and clicking on the notifications link, you can arrange to be notified via email whenever someone likes one of your tweets.", "pred": "You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, which track favorited tweets and show you who has favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, which track favorited tweets and show you who has favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you.", "cot": "[\"Answer: You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, which track favorited tweets and show you who has favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you.\", \"Answer: You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, which track favorited tweets and show you who has favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you.\", \"Answer: You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or by checking Twitter’s notifications: go to Twitter.com, log in, click your name in the upper‑right corner, select Settings, then click the Notifications link, where you can view users who favorited your tweets.\", \"Answer: You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, which track favorited tweets and show you who has favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you.\", \"Answer: You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, which track favorited tweets and show you who has favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you.\"]", "time_sec": 21.476, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 42.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
