igh temperature of 79 degrees (Fahrenheit) and an average low of 56 degrees (Fahrenheit). Freezing temperatures (20 °F/-8 °C or lower) occur sporadically from November to March, with two or three nights on average dropping to this temperature. The city also experiences rare days when the temperature never rises above 32 °F, which typically happens just once a decade.\", \"Answer: The average high temperature in Tallahassee is 79 degrees, and the average low is 56 degrees. Freezing temperatures occur sporadically from November to March, with two or three nights on average dropping to 20 °F (-8 °C) or lower, and a rare day when temperatures never rise above 32 °F.\", \"Answer: Tallahassee, Florida has an overall average high temperature of 79 degrees and an average low of 56 degrees. Freezing temperatures occur sporadically from November to March, with two or three nights on average dropping to 20 °F (-8 °C) or lower, and a rare event of a day when the temperature never rises above 32 °F, which typically occurs once a decade.\"]", "time_sec": 35.511, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.9, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "530", "question": "how does ez pass charges work", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here is how E-ZPass charging works:\n\nWhen you sign up for E-ZPass, a certain amount is charged to your credit card to establish a balance (specifically, $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag). This balance is used to pay for tolls as you drive through toll lanes. When you drive through a toll booth, the toll tag mounted on your windshield is read by the antennae, and your E-ZPass account is charged the appropriate amount. The amount is deducted from your balance. If your balance falls below a certain threshold ($10 for the TX-Tag), E-ZPass will charge your credit card an additional $100 or $25 to top up your balance.", "pred": "E-ZPass charges work by first charging a certain amount to establish a balance on your credit card—$100 for an EZ‑Tag and $25 for a TX‑Tag. As you travel through toll lanes, the system reads the tag on your windshield and deducts the toll amount from that balance. When the balance falls below a set threshold (e.g., $10 for the TX‑Tag), the system automatically charges your credit card again for the same amount ($100 or $25) to replenish the balance. If a vehicle does not have a tag, it is treated as a violator and photos of the license plate are taken for processing.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: E-ZPass charges work by first charging a certain amount to establish a balance on your credit card—$100 for an EZ‑Tag and $25 for a TX‑Tag. As you travel through toll lanes, the system reads the tag on your windshield and deducts the toll amount from that balance. When the balance falls below a set threshold (e.g., $10 for the TX‑Tag), the system automatically charges your credit card again for the same amount ($100 or $25) to replenish the balance. If a vehicle does not have a tag, it is treated as a violator and photos of the license plate are taken for processing.", "cot": "[\"Answer: E-ZPass charges work by first charging a certain amount to establish a balance on your credit card—$100 for an EZ‑Tag and $25 for a TX‑Tag. As you travel through toll lanes, the system reads the tag on your windshield and deducts the toll amount from that balance. When the balance falls below a set threshold (e.g., $10 for the TX‑Tag), the system automatically charges your credit card again for the same amount ($100 or $25) to replenish the balance. If a vehicle does not have a tag, it is treated as a violator and photos of the license plate are taken for processing.\", \"Answer: E-ZPass charges work by first requiring a credit card charge to establish a balance, which is $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag. The tolls are then deducted from this balance until it falls below a certain threshold (e.g., $10 for the TX-Tag), at which point another $100 or $25 is charged to the credit card to replenish the balance. When a vehicle with a toll tag enters a toll lane, the tag is read by antennas, and the E-ZPass account is charged the correct toll amount, with feedback provided on an electronic display. If no toll tag is present, the vehicle is classified as a violator, and cameras capture license plate images for processing.\", \"Answer: E-ZPass charges work by initially charging a set amount to establish a balance on your account (e.g., $100 for an EZ-Tag or $25 for a TX-Tag). As you travel through toll lanes, the toll amount is deducted from this balance. When the balance drops below a specific threshold (e.g., $10 for the TX-Tag), an additional charge (e.g., $100 or $25) is applied to replenish the balance. If no toll tag is present, the system identifies the vehicle as a violator and uses license plate photos for processing, which may result in additional charges.\", \"Answer: E-ZPass charges work by first charging a set amount to establish a balance on your account: $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag. As you travel through toll lanes, the toll amount is deducted from this balance. When the balance falls below a certain threshold (e.g., $10 for the TX-Tag), an additional charge (another $100 for EZ-Tag or $25 for TX-Tag) is applied to replenish the balance. If a vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system classifies it as a violator, and cameras capture license plate photos for processing, which involves separate charges.\", \"Answer: E-ZPass charges work by initially requiring a deposit to establish a balance on your account—$100 for an EZ-Tag and $25 for a TX-Tag. When you travel through a toll lane, the toll amount is deducted from this balance. Once the balance falls below a threshold (e.g., $10 for the TX-Tag), the system automatically charges your credit card again for the same deposit amount ($100 or $25) to replenish the balance. This cycle repeats as needed.\"]", "time_sec": 52.868, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.07, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "532", "question": "what are safety pins in a first aid box used for", "gt": "Safety pins in a first aid box are used for various purposes such as immobilizing an arm by creating a makeshift sling, securing a bandana over a wounded arm or leg, closing severe wounds in emergency situations, and removing splinters.", "pred": "Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters.\", \"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and remove splinters.\", \"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters in the wilderness.\", \"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and to remove splinters.\", \"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters.\"]", "time_sec": 29.977, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "533", "question": "what are safety pins in a first aid box used for", "gt": "Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for various purposes such as immobilizing an injured arm, securing a bandana over a bleeding wound, and helping to keep a severe wound closed. Additionally, safety pins can be used to remove splinters in the wilderness.", "pred": "Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters.\", \"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to the chest to create a makeshift sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping to keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters.\", \"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping to keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters.\", \"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, and helping keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances. They can also be used to remove splinters.\", \"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters.\"]", "time_sec": 30.029, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "534", "question": "what are safety pins in a first aid box used for", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for the following purposes:\n\n1. Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to create a makeshift arm sling (Passage 2).\n2. Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg (Passage 2).\n3. Helping to keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances (Passage 2).\n4. Removing splinters (Passage 3).\n\nThe passages mention these specific uses for safety pins in a first aid context, but do not provide any additional information regarding their use in a survival kit.", "pred": "Safety pins in a first aid box are used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and to remove splinters.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and to remove splinters.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and to remove splinters.\", \"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to the chest to create a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, and keeping a severe wound closed in dire circumstances as a substitute for stitches. They can also be used to remove splinters.\", \"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, helping keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and removing splinters in the wilderness.\", \"Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for the following purposes in first aid:\\n\\n1.  **Immobilizing an arm:** They can be used to pin the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to the chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling for immobilizing an arm (Passage 2).\\n2.  **Securing a bandana:** They can be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg (Passage 2).\\n3.  **Closing a severe wound:** They can be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances (Passage 2).\\n4.  **Removing splinters:** They can be used to remove splinters from the skin (Passage 2).\\n\\nThese uses are explicitly stated in the provided text as applications of safety pins within a survival or first aid context.\", \"Answer: Safety pins in a first aid box are used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and to remove splinters.\"]", "time_sec": 38.611, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.66, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
