{"id": "542", "question": "what traits do people have that are born in october?", "gt": "People born in October are described as having a keen interest in and an eye for form and structure, which can make them good architects, interior decorators, designers, or any profession that combines art and structure. They are also described as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful individuals. They are at their best when they are in control, their own boss, or working on their own. They can also get along with others and possess necessary \"people skills\", although they can occasionally show impatience. Despite being restless at heart, they crave stability and security, which is why they work hard at whatever they do.", "pred": "People born in October are described as having a great interest in and an eye for form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, and design (Passage 1). Those born on October 1 are characterized as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful individuals who thrive when in control or working independently, though they may exhibit impatience at times (Passage 2). People born on October 5 are described as restless at heart but deeply craving stability and security, which drives their hard work and dedication (Passage 3).", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: People born in October are described as having a great interest in and an eye for form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, and design (Passage 1). Those born on October 1 are characterized as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful individuals who thrive when in control or working independently, though they may exhibit impatience at times (Passage 2). People born on October 5 are described as restless at heart but deeply craving stability and security, which drives their hard work and dedication (Passage 3).", "cot": "[\"Answer: People born in October are described as having a great interest in and an eye for form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, and design (Passage 1). Those born on October 1 are characterized as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful individuals who thrive when in control or working independently, though they may exhibit impatience at times (Passage 2). People born on October 5 are described as restless at heart but deeply craving stability and security, which drives their hard work and dedication (Passage 3).\", \"Answer: People born in October are described as having a great interest in, and an eye for, form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, or design. They are also described as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful individuals who thrive when in control or working independently, though they possess strong \\\"people skills\\\" and may occasionally display impatience. Additionally, those born in October are noted as being restless at heart but craving stability and security, which drives their hard work.\", \"Answer: People born in October are described as having a great interest in form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, and design. They are also success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful, with a strong desire for control and independence. Additionally, they are hardworking and value stability and security, though they may experience restlessness at heart.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: People born in October have the following traits based on the provided passages:  \\n- They have a great interest in and eye for form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, and design (from passage 1).  \\n- They are described as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful, with a strong drive for control and independence, though they also possess people skills and may exhibit occasional impatience (from passage 2).  \\n- They crave stability and security, which motivates them to work hard at their endeavors (from passage 3).  \\n\\nAnswer: People born in October have a great interest in form and structure, are success-oriented, charming, personally powerful, enjoy being in control or working independently, possess people skills, may show impatience, and crave stability and security, driving them to work hard.\"]", "time_sec": 38.253, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.12, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "546", "question": "what traits do people have that are born in october?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some traits associated with people born in October:\n\n* Interest in form and structure (Passage 1)\n* Success-oriented and charming (Passage 2)\n* Personal power and impatience (Passage 2)\n* Crave stability and security (Passage 3)\n\nHowever, it's important to note that these are generalizations based on astrological signs and not all individuals will exhibit these traits. Additionally, there is no information about specific personality traits or characteristics of people born in October. Therefore, I cannot provide a more detailed answer based solely on the given passages.", "pred": "People born in October are described as having a great interest in and an eye for form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, and design. They are also described as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful individuals who are at their best when they are in control or working independently, though they may exhibit impatience occasionally. Additionally, those born in October are said to crave stability and security, which drives them to work hard at whatever they do.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: People born in October are described as having a great interest in and an eye for form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, and design. They are also described as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful individuals who are at their best when they are in control or working independently, though they may exhibit impatience occasionally. Additionally, those born in October are said to crave stability and security, which drives them to work hard at whatever they do.", "cot": "[\"Answer: People born in October are described as having a great interest in and an eye for form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, and design. They are also described as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful individuals who are at their best when they are in control or working independently, though they may exhibit impatience occasionally. Additionally, those born in October are said to crave stability and security, which drives them to work hard at whatever they do.\", \"Answer: People born in October have the following traits:  \\n- A great interest in and eye for form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, or design (Passage 1).  \\n- Success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful personalities who thrive when in control or working independently, though they may display impatience (Passage 2).  \\n- A desire for stability and security, leading them to work hard at their endeavors despite being restless at heart (Passage 3).  \\n- The passage references October 1 and October 5 specifically, but no general traits are provided for all October births beyond these examples. No comprehensive list of traits for \\\"October\\\" as a whole is given, only specific dates.\", \"Answer: People born in October are described as having a great interest in and an eye for form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, and design that combine art and structure (Passage 1). They may also be success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful, with a tendency toward being in control and having strong people skills, though they can occasionally show impatience (Passage 2). Additionally, they might be restless at heart yet crave stability and security, leading them to work hard at their endeavors (Passage 3).\", \"Based solely on the provided passages, people born in October have the following traits:\\n\\n1.  People born on October 14 have \\\"a great interest in, and eye for, form and structure\\\" and would make a good \\\"architect, interior decorator, designer, or any profession that combines art and structure.\\\"\\n2.  People born on October 5 are described as having a \\\"restless at heart\\\" nature but \\\"crave stability and security,\\\" which is why \\\"you work so hard at whatever you do.\\\"\\n\\nAnswer: People born in October (specifically October 14 and October 5 as mentioned) have a great interest in form and structure, making them suited for professions like architecture or design, and they may also crave stability and security while working hard to achieve it.\", \"Answer: People born in October are described as having an interest in form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, and design. They are also characterized as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful, with a strong desire for control and independence, though they possess good interpersonal skills. Additionally, they may exhibit impatience and a restless nature while still craving stability and security.\"]", "time_sec": 47.721, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "547", "question": "what traits do people have that are born in october?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some traits associated with people born in October:\n\n* A keen eye for form and structure (October 14)\n* Success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful (October 1)\n* Restless at heart but craving stability and security (October 5)\n\nIt's important to note that these are generalizations and not necessarily applicable to every individual born in October.", "pred": "People born in October are described as having a great interest in form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, or design (Passage 1). They are also characterized as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful, with a strong desire for control and independence, though they may exhibit impatience at times (Passage 2). Additionally, individuals born in October are noted to be restless yet value stability and security, working hard to achieve their goals (Passage 3).", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: People born in October are described as having a great interest in form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, or design (Passage 1). They are also characterized as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful, with a strong desire for control and independence, though they may exhibit impatience at times (Passage 2). Additionally, individuals born in October are noted to be restless yet value stability and security, working hard to achieve their goals (Passage 3).", "cot": "[\"Answer: People born in October are described as having a great interest in form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, or design (Passage 1). They are also characterized as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful, with a strong desire for control and independence, though they may exhibit impatience at times (Passage 2). Additionally, individuals born in October are noted to be restless yet value stability and security, working hard to achieve their goals (Passage 3).\", \"Answer: People born in October have diverse traits, including a great interest in and eye for form and structure (making them suitable for professions like architecture, interior decoration, or design), success-oriented and charming personalities with personal power and strong \\\"people skills\\\" (though sometimes impatience), and a restless yet stability-craving nature that drives hard work. Specific examples include architect/designer inclinations, control-oriented ambition, and a need for security in their endeavors.\", \"Answer: People born in October have a great interest in and eye for form and structure, making them well-suited for professions that combine art and structure such as architecture, interior decoration, or design. They are also described as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful, with a desire for control and independence, though they may occasionally exhibit impatience. Additionally, they are said to crave stability and security, which drives them to work hard at whatever they do.\", \"Answer: People born in October are described as having a great interest in form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, or design that combine art and structure. Those born on October 1 are characterized as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful individuals who thrive when in control or working independently, though they may display impatience. People born on October 5, while restless at heart, crave stability and security and work hard to achieve their goals.\", \"Answer: People born in October are described as having an interest in form and structure, making them well-suited for professions like architecture, interior decoration, or design (Passage 1). They may also exhibit success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful traits, with a tendency toward being control-oriented and having strong \\\"people skills,\\\" though they can occasionally display impatience (Passage 2). Additionally, those born in October may crave stability and security, working hard to achieve them despite a restless nature (Passage 3).\"]", "time_sec": 39.208, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.93, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "548", "question": "what is a transistor how does it work", "gt": "A transistor is a miniature electronic component made of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. It can function as an amplifier or a switch. As an amplifier, it takes a small electric current at one end (input current) and produces a larger electric current (output current) at the other end. As a switch, it uses a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a larger supply of electricity. The transistor works when the electrons and the holes start moving across the two junctions between the n-type and p-type silicon. The current passes from the emitter to the collector through the base. The amount of collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current.", "pred": "A transistor is a miniature semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals. It functions by using a small amount of electricity to control a larger supply, similar to a valve controlling water flow. When working as an amplifier, it takes in a tiny input current and produces a much larger output current, with the collector current being approximately β times the base current, where β is typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors. As a switch, it normally blocks current flow from the emitter to the collector when off, but allows it when the electrons and holes start moving across the junctions between n-type and p-type silicon. This operation is achieved through the base, which has a more positive voltage than the emitter, pulling electrons to create a flow of electricity from the emitter to the collector through the base.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: A transistor is a miniature semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals. It functions by using a small amount of electricity to control a larger supply, similar to a valve controlling water flow. When working as an amplifier, it takes in a tiny input current and produces a much larger output current, with the collector current being approximately β times the base current, where β is typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors. As a switch, it normally blocks current flow from the emitter to the collector when off, but allows it when the electrons and holes start moving across the junctions between n-type and p-type silicon. This operation is achieved through the base, which has a more positive voltage than the emitter, pulling electrons to create a flow of electricity from the emitter to the collector through the base.", "cot": "[\"Answer: A transistor is a miniature semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals. It functions by using a small amount of electricity to control a larger supply, similar to a valve controlling water flow. When working as an amplifier, it takes in a tiny input current and produces a much larger output current, with the collector current being approximately β times the base current, where β is typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors. As a switch, it normally blocks current flow from the emitter to the collector when off, but allows it when the electrons and holes start moving across the junctions between n-type and p-type silicon. This operation is achieved through the base, which has a more positive voltage than the emitter, pulling electrons to create a flow of electricity from the emitter to the collector through the base.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device that can function as an amplifier or a switch. As an amplifier, it takes in a small input current and produces a larger output current. As a switch, it controls the flow of electricity from the emitter to the collector through the base, using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a larger supply of electricity, similar to turning a valve to control water flow. The base pulls electrons from the emitter due to its more positive voltage, creating a flow of electricity through the transistor. In a transistor, collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, which is typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors but can be smaller in high-power transistors.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device that can function as an amplifier or a switch. As an amplifier, it takes in a small input current and produces a larger output current, with the collector current being approximately β times the base current (greater than 100 for small-signal transistors). As a switch, it normally blocks current flow from the emitter to the collector in its off state due to a barrier created by holes in the base, but it works when electrons and holes move across the junctions between n-type and p-type silicon, allowing current to flow. The base controls a larger supply of electricity from the emitter to the collector by using a small amount of electricity to control a gate, similar to turning a valve to control water flow.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power. It is composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. It works by using a small amount of electricity to control a larger supply of electricity, similar to turning a valve to control a supply of water. This is achieved by using a base with a more positive voltage than the emitter to pull electrons from the emitter, creating a flow of electricity through the transistor from the emitter to the collector through the base. A transistor can work as an amplifier, taking in a tiny electric current at one end and producing a much bigger electric current at the other, or as a switch, where normally the holes in the base act like a barrier, preventing any significant current flow from the emitter to the collector while the transistor is in its off state. The collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, and it is typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors but can be smaller in transistors designed for high-power applications.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals. It works by using a small amount of electricity to control a larger supply of electricity; for example, in an amplifier configuration, a tiny input current at the base controls a much larger output current flowing from the emitter to the collector, with the base current being approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the input current (typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors). In a switch configuration, the transistor is normally off (with holes in the base acting as a barrier preventing current flow from emitter to collector), and it turns on when electrons and holes move across the n-type and p-type silicon junctions.\"]", "time_sec": 63.946, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.7, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "550", "question": "what is a transistor how does it work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a transistor is an electronic component made of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. It functions as an amplifier or a switch depending on the flow of electrons through its base. When working as an amplifier, it takes in a small electric current at one end and produces a larger electric current at the other. The flow of electrons is controlled by using a small amount of electricity to turn a valve-like structure in the transistor. In its off state, the holes in the base act as a barrier, preventing any significant current flow from the emitter to the collector. Transistors can have common-emitter configuration where collector current is approximately β times the base current.", "pred": "A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals. It works by using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a much larger supply of electricity, allowing it to function as an amplifier or a switch. When acting as an amplifier, it takes in a tiny input current and produces a much larger output current. When functioning as a switch, it uses a barrier of holes in the base to prevent significant current flow from the emitter to the collector in its off state, and it operates when electrons and holes move across the junctions between n-type and p-type silicon. The collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, which can be greater than 100 for small-signal transistors.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals. It works by using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a much larger supply of electricity, allowing it to function as an amplifier or a switch. When acting as an amplifier, it takes in a tiny input current and produces a much larger output current. When functioning as a switch, it uses a barrier of holes in the base to prevent significant current flow from the emitter to the collector in its off state, and it operates when electrons and holes move across the junctions between n-type and p-type silicon. The collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, which can be greater than 100 for small-signal transistors.", "cot": "[\"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals. It works by using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a much larger supply of electricity, allowing it to function as an amplifier or a switch. When acting as an amplifier, it takes in a tiny input current and produces a much larger output current. When functioning as a switch, it uses a barrier of holes in the base to prevent significant current flow from the emitter to the collector in its off state, and it operates when electrons and holes move across the junctions between n-type and p-type silicon. The collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, which can be greater than 100 for small-signal transistors.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device that can function as either an amplifier or a switch. As an amplifier, it takes in a small input current and produces a much larger output current. As a switch, it controls the flow of electricity from the emitter to the collector through the base, using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a larger supply of electricity. The transistor is composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals, and the collector current is approximately β times the base current, where β is the common-emitter current gain.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power. It functions by using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a much larger supply of electricity, creating a flow of electricity through the transistor. This movement of electrons allows the current to pass from the emitter to the collector through the base. When used as an amplifier, it takes in a tiny electric current at one end and produces a much bigger electric current at the other. As a switch, it normally has a barrier (holes in the base) that prevents significant current flow from the emitter to the collector while in its off state. The transistor works when electrons and holes start moving across the two junctions between n-type and p-type silicon. The collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power. It is composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. A transistor works by using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a much larger supply of electricity, allowing it to function as an amplifier or a switch. When acting as an amplifier, it takes in a tiny electric current at one end (an input current) and produces a much bigger electric current (an output current) at the other. When functioning as a switch, it normally has holes in the base acting as a barrier, preventing any significant current flow from the emitter to the collector while in its off state, and it works when electrons and holes start moving across the two junctions between n-type and p-type silicon. The collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors but can be smaller in transistors designed for high-power applications.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. It functions as an amplifier by taking in a small input current (base current) and producing a larger output current (collector current), where the collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors. It operates as a switch by controlling the flow of electrons and holes across the junctions between n-type and p-type silicon; when the base voltage is more positive than the emitter, electrons are pulled from the emitter through the base to the collector, creating current flow, while in its off state, holes in the base act as a barrier preventing significant current flow from the emitter to the collector.\"]", "time_sec": 62.83, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.76, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "551", "question": "what is a transistor how does it work", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how a transistor works:\n\n1. A transistor functions as both an amplifier and a switch.\n2. The transistor's design allows it to control a larger supply of electricity with a small amount of electricity, much like turning a valve to control a supply of water.\n3. The base of the transistor pulls electrons from the emitter, creating a flow of electricity through the transistor.\n4. The transistor can take in a tiny electric current at one end (the input current) and produce a much bigger electric current at the other end (the output current) when it works as an amplifier.\n5. The holes in the base of the transistor act as a barrier, preventing any significant current flow from the emitter to the collector when the transistor is in its off state.\n6. When the electrons and holes move across the two junctions between the n-type and p-type silicon, the transistor begins to work.\n7. The collector current is approximately beta (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, and it is typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors but can be smaller in transistors designed for high-power applications.\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages.", "pred": "A transistor is a semiconductor device that can function as either an amplifier or a switch. As an amplifier, it takes in a small input current and produces a much larger output current. As a switch, it controls the flow of electricity from the emitter to the collector, with the base acting as a barrier to prevent significant current flow when in its off state. The transistor works when electrons and holes move across the two junctions between n-type and p-type silicon. The base pulls electrons from the emitter due to its more positive voltage, creating a flow of electricity through the transistor. The collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, which can be greater than 100 for small-signal transistors but can be smaller in high-power transistors.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device that can function as either an amplifier or a switch. As an amplifier, it takes in a small input current and produces a much larger output current. As a switch, it controls the flow of electricity from the emitter to the collector, with the base acting as a barrier to prevent significant current flow when in its off state. The transistor works when electrons and holes move across the two junctions between n-type and p-type silicon. The base pulls electrons from the emitter due to its more positive voltage, creating a flow of electricity through the transistor. The collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, which can be greater than 100 for small-signal transistors but can be smaller in high-power transistors.", "cot": "[\"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device that can function as either an amplifier or a switch. As an amplifier, it takes in a small input current and produces a much larger output current. As a switch, it controls the flow of electricity from the emitter to the collector, with the base acting as a barrier to prevent significant current flow when in its off state. The transistor works when electrons and holes move across the two junctions between n-type and p-type silicon. The base pulls electrons from the emitter due to its more positive voltage, creating a flow of electricity through the transistor. The collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, which can be greater than 100 for small-signal transistors but can be smaller in high-power transistors.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. It functions as an amplifier by taking in a small input current at one end and producing a larger output current at the other, with the collector current being approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors. As a switch, it operates by using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a larger supply of electricity, where normally the holes in the base act as a barrier preventing current flow from the emitter to the collector in its off state, and it works when electrons and holes move across the two junctions between n-type and p-type silicon.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals. It functions as an amplifier by taking in a small input current and producing a much larger output current, and as a switch by controlling the flow of current between the emitter and collector through the base, using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a larger supply of electricity, similar to turning a valve to control water flow.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. It functions as an amplifier by taking in a small input current and producing a much larger output current, as described in passage 2. It works as a switch by using electrons and holes to control current flow between the emitter and collector, where the base acts as a barrier in its off state, as explained in passage 2. The base pulls electrons from the emitter due to a more positive voltage, creating a flow of electricity from the emitter to the collector through the base, as stated in passage 1. Additionally, the collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors, as mentioned in passage 3.\", \"Answer: A transistor is a miniature semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power, composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. It functions as an amplifier by taking in a small input current at one end and producing a much larger output current at the other, or as a switch by controlling the flow of current from the emitter to the collector through the base, where electrons and holes move across the junctions between n-type and p-type silicon, with the collector current being approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors.\"]", "time_sec": 54.976, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "554", "question": "why does the company Oracle have 2 CEOs", "gt": "Oracle has two CEOs because the former CEO, Larry Ellison, stepped down and chose to have two of his co-presidents, Safra Catz and Mark Hurd, share the role of CEO.", "pred": "Oracle has 2 CEOs because Larry Ellison announced that he was stepping down from his CEO post and naming co-president and CFO Safra Catz and co-president Mark Hurd to share the role of CEO.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Oracle has two CEOs because Larry Ellison stepped down as CEO and named both Safra Catz and Mark Hurd to share the role of CEO, as stated in the passages: \"Larry Ellison announced Thursday he has agreed to step down as CEO of Oracle... Mark Hurd and Safra Catz, co-presidents of Oracle, will take the role as CEO\" and \"Larry Ellison unexpectedly announced that he was stepping down from his CEO post and naming not one, but two CEOs to replace him. Co-president and CFO Safra Catz and co-president Mark Hurd will share the role of CEO.\"", "cot": "[\"Answer: Oracle has two CEOs because Larry Ellison stepped down as CEO and named both Safra Catz and Mark Hurd to share the role of CEO, as stated in the passages: \\\"Larry Ellison announced Thursday he has agreed to step down as CEO of Oracle... Mark Hurd and Safra Catz, co-presidents of Oracle, will take the role as CEO\\\" and \\\"Larry Ellison unexpectedly announced that he was stepping down from his CEO post and naming not one, but two CEOs to replace him. Co-president and CFO Safra Catz and co-president Mark Hurd will share the role of CEO.\\\"\", \"Answer: Oracle has two CEOs because Larry Ellison, the company's founder, stepped down as CEO and named co-presidents Mark Hurd and Safra Catz to share the role, as stated in the passages: \\\"Larry Ellison announced Thursday he has agreed to step down as CEO of Oracle... Mark Hurd and Safra Catz, co-presidents of Oracle, will take the role as CEO\\\" and \\\"Larry Ellison unexpectedly announced that he was stepping down from his CEO post and naming not one, but two CEOs to replace him. Co-president and CFO Safra Catz and co-president Mark Hurd will share the role of CEO.\\\"\", \"Answer: Oracle has 2 CEOs because Larry Ellison stepped down as CEO and named both co-president and CFO Safra Catz and co-president Mark Hurd to share the role of CEO.\", \"Answer: Oracle has 2 CEOs because Larry Ellison announced that he was stepping down from his CEO post and naming co-president and CFO Safra Catz and co-president Mark Hurd to share the role of CEO.\", \"Answer: Oracle has 2 CEOs because Larry Ellison announced that he was stepping down from his CEO post and naming co-president and CFO Safra Catz and co-president Mark Hurd to share the role of CEO.\"]", "time_sec": 32.41, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.83, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "562", "question": "global egalitarianism meaning", "gt": "Sure! Here's my answer based on the three provided passages:\n\nGlobal egalitarianism refers to the idea that all individuals should have equal rights and opportunities regardless of their background, location, or culture. However, the passages suggest that achieving global egalitarianism is challenging due to difficulties in measuring resources and opportunities across different cultures. Additionally, the passages hint that there may be different types of egalitarianism, such as instrumental and non-instrumental, but do not provide further explanation or clarification. Therefore, without more information, it is difficult to give a more specific definition of global egalitarianism based solely on these passages.", "pred": "Global egalitarianism is a free-standing conception of global justice, as defined in the first passage. It is a principle that seeks to achieve equality in the distribution of resources and opportunities across different societies worldwide. However, the passage also indicates that this concept is challenged because it is difficult to measure resources or opportunities in a neutral way between cultures, which is seen as essential for a global principle of justice.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Global egalitarianism is a free-standing conception of global justice, as defined in the first passage. It is a principle that seeks to achieve equality in the distribution of resources and opportunities across different societies worldwide. However, the passage also indicates that this concept is challenged because it is difficult to measure resources or opportunities in a neutral way between cultures, which is seen as essential for a global principle of justice.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Global egalitarianism is a free-standing conception of global justice, as defined in the first passage. It is a principle that seeks to achieve equality in the distribution of resources and opportunities across different societies worldwide. However, the passage also indicates that this concept is challenged because it is difficult to measure resources or opportunities in a neutral way between cultures, which is seen as essential for a global principle of justice.\", \"Answer: Global egalitarianism is a free-standing conception of global justice, as described in the first passage. It is discussed in the context of examining reasons for rejecting it, particularly focusing on the challenges of measuring resources or opportunities in a neutral way across different cultures, which is considered essential for a global principle of justice. The concept is further differentiated into instrumental and non-instrumental forms, where instrumental egalitarianism views equality as a means to an end, while non-instrumental egalitarianism values equality for its own sake. However, the passages do not provide a direct definition of \\\"global egalitarianism\\\" beyond its examination as a concept in global justice and its rejection based on measurement neutrality issues.\", \"Answer: Global egalitarianism is a free-standing conception of global justice that argues against equality of resources and equality of opportunity as workable principles for global justice, stating that we cannot measure resources or opportunities in a neutral way between cultures.\", \"Answer: Global egalitarianism is a free-standing conception of global justice, as stated in passage 1. It examines the principle of equality as applied to the global level, focusing on justice across nations and societies. The passage discusses challenges in implementing equality of resources or equality of opportunity as viable principles for global justice, highlighting the difficulty in measuring resources or opportunities neutrally across different cultures. Passage 2 further contextualizes global inequality, referencing data from 2008 that illustrates socio-economic disparities on a global scale, though specific details about the Gini coefficient are not provided in the excerpt. Passage 3 differentiates between instrumental and non-instrumental egalitarianism, where global egalitarianism could be interpreted as either valuing equality as a means to achieve other goals or as an end in itself. However, the passages do not provide a direct definition of global egalitarianism beyond its examination as a concept in global justice.\\n\\nAnswer: Global egalitarianism is a concept examined as a free-standing principle of global justice, which challenges the feasibility of equality of resources or equality of opportunity as measures for global fairness, emphasizing the need for neutral assessment across cultures, and differentiated by instrumental and non-instrumental approaches to equality.\", \"Answer: Global egalitarianism is a free-standing conception of global justice that examines reasons for rejecting it, such as the inability to measure resources or opportunities neutrally across cultures, as stated in the first passage.\"]", "time_sec": 43.839, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 22.22, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "571", "question": "how to do the skill moves on fifa 16 for xbox one", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to perform skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One:\n\n1. Ball Juggle (while standing): Press and hold the LT button on the Xbox controller, followed by a quick tap of the RB button.\n\nThat's it! This combination will allow you to perform the ball juggling skill move while standing on the field in FIFA 16 on Xbox One.", "pred": "To execute skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) while standing for the Ball Juggle skill move, as specified for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To execute skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) while standing for the Ball Juggle skill move, as specified for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To execute skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) while standing for the Ball Juggle skill move, as specified for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.\", \"Answer: To do skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) while standing for the Ball Juggle skill move, as specified for Xbox 360, Xbox One, and PC with a controller in the given passages.\", \"Answer: To execute skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) while standing for the Ball Juggle skill move, as specified in the passage for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.\", \"Answer: To do skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) while standing for the Ball Juggle skill move, as specified in the passage for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.\", \"Answer: To do skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) for the Ball Juggle (while standing), as specified in the passage for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.\"]", "time_sec": 24.571, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "572", "question": "how to do the skill moves on fifa 16 for xbox one", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's how to do skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One:\n\n1. Ball Juggle (while standing): Hold LT + tap RB.\n\nNote that this combination works for Xbox 360 and Xbox One controllers. If you're playing on PC with a controller, the buttons may be different. Additionally, there are tutorial videos available online that show what each skill move looks like, which can be helpful in mastering these moves.", "pred": "To do skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) for the Ball Juggle (while standing), as specified in the passage for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To do skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) for the Ball Juggle (while standing), as specified in the passage for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To do skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) for the Ball Juggle (while standing), as specified in the passage for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.\", \"Answer: To do skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) for the Ball Juggle (while standing) skill move, as specified in the passage for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.\", \"Answer: To do skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) while standing for the Ball Juggle skill move, as specified in the passage for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.\", \"Answer: To execute skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) while standing for the Ball Juggle skill move, as specified in the guide for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.\", \"Answer: To execute skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, use the button combination LT (hold) + RB (tap) for the Ball Juggle (while standing), as specified for Xbox 360 & Xbox One consoles and PC with a controller.\"]", "time_sec": 24.545, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.6, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "573", "question": "how to quickly get rid of mice", "gt": "To quickly get rid of mice, you need to take immediate action. You can start by identifying all possible entry points that mice use to get into your house. Once identified, consider putting steel wool inside these holes or vents before sealing them off. This will prevent the mice from using these paths to re-enter your home. By doing so, you eliminate their access to food or shelter in your house, which can help in getting rid of them quickly.", "pred": "To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action, as mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting. Seal entry points, such as pipes or vents, and stuff steel wool inside them before sealing to prevent mice from re-entering, providing extra protection if they are persistent. This approach addresses their ability to fit through tiny openings and access food sources, which they readily exploit.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action, as mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting. Seal entry points, such as pipes or vents, and stuff steel wool inside them before sealing to prevent mice from re-entering, providing extra protection if they are persistent. This approach addresses their ability to fit through tiny openings and access food sources, which they readily exploit.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action, as mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting. Seal entry points, such as pipes or vents, and stuff steel wool inside them before sealing to prevent mice from re-entering, providing extra protection if they are persistent. This approach addresses their ability to fit through tiny openings and access food sources, which they readily exploit.\", \"Answer: Take immediate action to eliminate mice quickly, as they can rapidly nest and take residence in homes. Seal entry points (e.g., using steel wool in pipes or vents, as noted in passage 2 to block access and prevent reentry) and remove food sources (mentioned in passage 3 as rodents consume discarded human food). The passages emphasize speed and prevention, with steel wool providing \\\"extra protection\\\" against persistent mice.\", \"Answer: Take immediate action to eliminate mice quickly, as they can rapidly nest and infest a home. Seal entry points (e.g., using steel wool in pipes or vents, as noted in passage 2) and remove food sources (as mentioned in passage 3), since mice exploit any available shelter or discarded human food.\", \"Answer:To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action, as mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting; seal entry points (e.g., using steel wool in pipes or vents to block access), and eliminate food sources and shelter, since mice exploit any available food or tiny openings to enter homes.\", \"Answer:To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as it is a critical step. Mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting, so prompt measures are essential. For example, seal entry points (such as pipes or vents) and stuff steel wool inside them to prevent mice from re-entering, as this adds an extra layer of protection. Additionally, eliminate food sources and shelter by removing discarded human food and sealing tiny openings that mice can fit through, as these steps address the root causes of infestation.\"]", "time_sec": 32.042, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "574", "question": "how to quickly get rid of mice", "gt": "To quickly get rid of mice, it is important to take immediate action as they can quickly infest your home. One effective method is to seal off any entry points that mice can use to enter your house, such as pipes and vents. Placing steel wool inside these openings before sealing them can prevent mice from reentering. Additionally, eliminating any potential food sources and shelter can help deter mice from your home.", "pred": "Take immediate action to get rid of mice quickly, as they can rapidly take up residence and start nesting; seal entry points (e.g., use steel wool in pipes/vents before sealing) to prevent re-entry, and eliminate food sources and shelter to stop them from thriving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Take immediate action to get rid of mice quickly, as they can rapidly take up residence and start nesting; seal entry points (e.g., use steel wool in pipes/vents before sealing) to prevent re-entry, and eliminate food sources and shelter to stop them from thriving.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Take immediate action to get rid of mice quickly, as they can rapidly take up residence and start nesting; seal entry points (e.g., use steel wool in pipes/vents before sealing) to prevent re-entry, and eliminate food sources and shelter to stop them from thriving.\", \"Answer: To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as it is a critical step, since mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting in your home.\", \"Answer: Take immediate action to eliminate mice quickly, as they can rapidly nest and infest a home. Seal entry points (e.g., using steel wool in pipes or vents, as noted in passage 2) to prevent re-entry, and remove food sources or shelter, since mice exploit any available food or tiny openings (passage 3).\", \"Answer: To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as stated in the passages, since mice can rapidly take up residence and nest. The passages emphasize sealing entry points (e.g., using steel wool in pipes or vents, as noted in passage 2, point 3, to prevent mice from re-entering) and eliminating food sources or shelter, as mentioned in passage 3, which states mice \\\"will quickly take advantage of any source of food or shelter\\\" and \\\"consume any food discarded by humans.\\\"\", \"Answer: To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action, as mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting. The passages emphasize the need for swift measures, such as sealing entry points (e.g., using steel wool in pipes or vents to block access) and eliminating food sources or shelter that attract them.\"]", "time_sec": 27.316, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "575", "question": "how to quickly get rid of mice", "gt": "To quickly get rid of mice, you should take immediate action by sealing off entry points that mice could use to enter your home. Steel wool is a good material to use for this purpose as it will prevent mice from using the hole to get back into your house. Additionally, getting rid of rats and mice involves eliminating any sources of food and shelter for these rodents and preventing them from returning.", "pred": "Take immediate action to eliminate mice quickly, as they can rapidly nest and take up residence in your home. Seal entry points (e.g., using steel wool in pipes or vents to block access) and remove food sources, as mice exploit any shelter or discarded human food.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer:Take immediate action to eliminate mice quickly, as they can rapidly nest and take up residence in your home. Seal entry points (e.g., using steel wool in pipes or vents to block access) and remove food sources, as mice exploit any shelter or discarded human food.", "cot": "[\"Answer:Take immediate action to eliminate mice quickly, as they can rapidly nest and take up residence in your home. Seal entry points (e.g., using steel wool in pipes or vents to block access) and remove food sources, as mice exploit any shelter or discarded human food.\", \"Answer: To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as it is a critical step, since mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting in your home.\", \"Answer: To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as stated in passage 1, which emphasizes the critical need for fast action to prevent mice from quickly taking up residence and nesting. Passage 3 supports this by noting that mice will quickly take advantage of food and shelter sources. Passage 2 suggests specific actions such as sealing entry points with steel wool to prevent mice from re-entering, which is part of the immediate action needed to get rid of mice.\", \"Answer: Take immediate action to get rid of mice quickly, as they can rapidly take up residence and start nesting.\", \"Answer: To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting. The passages emphasize the critical need for speed and mention using steel wool inside entry points (such as pipes or vents) before sealing them off to prevent mice from re-entering, adding extra protection against persistent mice.\"]", "time_sec": 23.117, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.64, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "576", "question": "how to quickly get rid of mice", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to quickly get rid of mice:\n\n1. Take immediate action to get rid of mice as soon as possible, as they can quickly take up residence in your home and start nesting (Passage 1).\n2. Seal off all entry points into your home, including holes around pipes and vents, using steel wool to prevent mice from getting back in (Passage 2).\n3. Get rid of any sources of food for mice and rats, as they will quickly take advantage of any food left behind by humans (Passage 3).\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to quickly get rid of mice once they have entered a home.", "pred": "To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as stated in the passages. Mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting, so prompt measures are critical. One specific method mentioned is to seal entry points (e.g., pipes or vents) by stuffing steel wool inside the openings before sealing them off. This prevents mice from re-entering the house, especially if they are persistent or resilient, and addresses their ability to fit through \"the tiniest of openings\" to access the home.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer:To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as stated in the passages. Mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting, so prompt measures are critical. One specific method mentioned is to seal entry points (e.g., pipes or vents) by stuffing steel wool inside the openings before sealing them off. This prevents mice from re-entering the house, especially if they are persistent or resilient, and addresses their ability to fit through \"the tiniest of openings\" to access the home.", "cot": "[\"Answer:To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as stated in the passages. Mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting, so prompt measures are critical. One specific method mentioned is to seal entry points (e.g., pipes or vents) by stuffing steel wool inside the openings before sealing them off. This prevents mice from re-entering the house, especially if they are persistent or resilient, and addresses their ability to fit through \\\"the tiniest of openings\\\" to access the home.\", \"Answer:To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as it is a critical step. Mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting in your home. For example, passage 1 states, \\\"the best way to get rid of the mice is do it fast. You need to take immediate action.\\\"\", \"Answer: To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as stated in passage 1: \\\"the best way to get rid of the mice is do it fast. You need to take immediate action.\\\" Passage 3 supports this by emphasizing that mice \\\"will quickly take up residence\\\" and \\\"can very quickly take up residence in your home and start nesting,\\\" underscoring the urgency. Passage 2 provides a specific method for sealing entry points (e.g., \\\"putting steel wool inside the pipe or vent before you seal it off\\\") to prevent mice from re-entering, which is part of the immediate action required. Passage 1 also notes that \\\"mice can very quickly take up residence,\\\" reinforcing that speed is critical. \\n\\nAnswer: Take immediate action, such as sealing entry points with steel wool (as in passage 2) and eliminating food sources (as implied in passage 3), to prevent mice from quickly establishing residence.\", \"Answer:Take immediate action to eliminate mice quickly, as they can rapidly nest and infest homes. Seal entry points (e.g., use steel wool in pipes or vents before sealing) to prevent re-entry, and remove food sources or shelter that attract them.\", \"Answer: To quickly get rid of mice, take immediate action as stated in the passages. Mice can rapidly take up residence and start nesting, so prompt measures are critical. One specific method mentioned is to seal entry points (e.g., pipes or vents) and stuff steel wool inside them before sealing, as this prevents mice from re-entering and adds extra protection if they are persistent. Additionally, eliminating food sources and shelter (as noted in passage 3) is essential to address the root cause of the infestation.\"]", "time_sec": 40.274, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.84, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "580", "question": "what do i do if i got my sperrys wet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, if your Sperry shoes get wet, it is recommended to use a leather conditioner to help revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it. This is especially important if you wash your shoes with detergent, as it tends to dry out the leather. If you don't have a leather conditioner on hand, you can use a suede bar or leather brush to clean the shoes. It's best to avoid getting light tan Sperry shoes wet, as water might stain them. However, if you do get them wet, using a suede bar or leather brush should help remove any stains.", "pred": "If your Sperrys get wet, you can get them wet (it's not a big deal), but if they are light tan, water might stain them. After washing with detergent, use a leather conditioner to revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it, then reassemble the shoes. You may also need a suede bar and leather brush (or a cleaning toothbrush) to handle any stains, which cost between $5-$10 and are worth the investment.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: If your Sperrys get wet, you can get them wet (it's not a big deal), but if they are light tan, water might stain them. After washing with detergent, use a leather conditioner to revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it, then reassemble the shoes. You may also need a suede bar and leather brush (or a cleaning toothbrush) to handle any stains, which cost between $5-$10 and are worth the investment.", "cot": "[\"Answer: If your Sperrys get wet, you can get them wet (it's not a big deal), but if they are light tan, water might stain them. After washing with detergent, use a leather conditioner to revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it, then reassemble the shoes. You may also need a suede bar and leather brush (or a cleaning toothbrush) to handle any stains, which cost between $5-$10 and are worth the investment.\", \"Answer: If your Sperry shoes get wet, you can reassemble them after washing with detergent, as detergent can dry out the leather and a leather conditioner helps revitalize it by infusing moisture back in. For light tan Sperrys, water might cause staining, so be cautious. To clean stains, use a suede bar and leather brush (or a cleaning toothbrush), which are affordable at $5-$10 and essential for handling stains effectively.\", \"Answer: If you got your Sperrys wet, you can reassemble the shoes after washing them with detergent and using a leather conditioner to revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it, as stated in passage 1. Additionally, passage 2 suggests that getting your topsiders (which are Sperry shoes) wet is not a big deal, especially for regular dark brown ones, but water might stain light tan ones. Passage 3 recommends using a suede bar and leather brush (or a cleaning toothbrush) to handle any stains, as these tools are effective and worth the $5-$10 investment.\", \"Answer: If your Sperrys get wet, you can reassemble the shoes after washing them with detergent and using a leather conditioner to revitalize the leather and prevent it from drying out, as suggested in passage 1. For light tan Sperrys, be cautious of potential water stains, as mentioned in passage 2. Additionally, you can use a suede bar and leather brush (or a cleaning toothbrush) to handle any stains, as recommended in passage 3.\", \"Answer: Use a leather conditioner to revitalize the leather, as detergent can dry it out, and reassemble the shoes once done. For light tan Sperrys, water might cause staining, so handle with care. Use a suede bar, leather brush, or cleaning toothbrush (costing $5-$10) to manage stains effectively.\"]", "time_sec": 38.424, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 4.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "589", "question": "where does 1099-patr go on 1040", "gt": "Per the IRS instructions, patronage dividends and other distributions in boxes 1,2,3, and 5 from a cooperative, which are reported in Form 1099-PATR, are reported on Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835 of the Form 1040.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835", "cot": "[\"Answer: Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 7.819, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "592", "question": "where does 1099-patr go on 1040", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the answer to the question \"Where does 1099-PATR go on 1040?\" is:\n\nSchedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835.\n\nAccording to the instructions for Form 1099-PATR, patronage dividends and other distributions in boxes 1, 2, 3, and 5 from a cooperative are reported on one of these forms.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835", "cot": "[\"Answer: Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835\", \"Answer:Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835\"]", "time_sec": 8.2, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 20.51, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "598", "question": "where is dove soap headquarters", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the headquarters of Dove Soap can be located in:\n\nPassage 1 states that if you want to speak to a live representative, you can call them at 1-800-761-DOVE (3683) from Monday to Friday between 8:30 AM to 6:00 PM Eastern Time. This suggests that the headquarters of Dove Soap is located in the Eastern Time zone.\n\nPassage 2 provides the same phone number as Passage 1 for contacting a live representative, but also notes that this number is available 24 hours a day / 7 days a week for medical or product safety emergencies. This indicates that the headquarters of Dove Soap is open for business operations 24/7.\n\nPassage 3 does not provide any information about the location of Dove Soap's headquarters.\n\nTherefore, based on the given passages, the headquarters of Dove Soap can be located in the Eastern Time zone and is open for business operations 24/7.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 6.825, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.61, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
