{"id": "620", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "gt": "IT technology has significantly changed the workplace in several ways. It has improved efficiency and increased productivity, as it allows for a complete shift in how time is spent in the modern workplace. The continuous evolution of technology also changes how business is conducted and the dynamics of the workplace. Over the last 10 to 15 years, technology has drastically changed attitudes and processes in the workplace. Technology has also dramatically reshaped the average American workplace, allowing employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "pred": "It technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics and workplace attitudes, and enabling global interaction and remote work.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: It technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics and workplace attitudes, and enabling global interaction and remote work.", "cot": "[\"Answer: It technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics and workplace attitudes, and enabling global interaction and remote work.\", \"Answer: Technology has changed the workplace in several ways, including improving efficiency and increasing productivity, transforming business dynamics and workplace attitudes, and enabling employees to interact with a global market and work remotely.\", \"Answer: Technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics, enabling global market interaction, and allowing employees to work remotely, as described in the passages which highlight shifts in workplace attitudes, processes, and the replacement of traditional office environments with rapid technological advancement over the past decades.\", \"Answer: IT technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, enabling employees to interact with a global market, and allowing them to work remotely.\", \"Answer: Technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics and workplace attitudes over the past 10-15 years, and enabling employees to interact with a global market and work remotely, as evidenced by the shift from traditional office environments to modern, technology-driven workplaces that support global interaction and mobility.\"]", "time_sec": 19.665, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "625", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "gt": "Based on the given passages, technology has changed the workplace in several ways, including:\n\n1. Increased efficiency and productivity: Technology has enabled automation of many tasks, allowing employees to focus on more complex and creative work, leading to increased productivity.\n2. Changes in workplace dynamics: Technology has transformed the way people communicate and collaborate in the workplace, enabling remote work and virtual teams.\n3. Rapid advancements: Technology has rapidly advanced in recent years, allowing employees to access new tools and resources, and adapt to changing market conditions.\n4. Global connectivity: Technology has enabled employees to interact with a global market and work remotely, allowing for greater flexibility and mobility.\n\nTherefore, technology has had a significant impact on the modern workplace, transforming the way people work, communicate, and collaborate.", "pred": "Technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics and workplace attitudes over the past 10-15 years, enabling global market interaction, and allowing employees to work remotely.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: It technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics and workplace attitudes, enabling global market interaction, and allowing employees to work remotely.", "cot": "[\"Answer: It technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics and workplace attitudes, enabling global market interaction, and allowing employees to work remotely.\", \"Answer: Technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics and workplace attitudes over the past 10-15 years, enabling global market interaction, and allowing employees to work remotely.\", \"Answer: Technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics, and enabling employees to interact with a global market and work remotely, as stated in the passages.\", \"Answer: Technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics and workplace attitudes over the past 10-15 years, enabling global market interaction, and allowing employees to work remotely.\", \"Answer: IT technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, transforming business dynamics and workplace attitudes over the past 10 to 15 years, and enabling employees to interact with a global market and work remotely, as described in the passages.\"]", "time_sec": 18.38, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "627", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "gt": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay close to them when they are near the three-point line, actively sliding your feet to minimize shot opportunities (passage 1). It is important to create a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against a tall player (passage 3).", "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them near the three-point line, actively slide your feet side to side to limit their shot opportunities, and maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them near the three-point line, actively slide your feet side to side to limit their shot opportunities, and maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them near the three-point line, actively slide your feet side to side to limit their shot opportunities, and maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.\", \"Answer: To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them near the three-point line and actively slide your feet side to side. Additionally, keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.\", \"Answer:To guard a tall person in basketball, stay as close as possible to them near the three-point line and actively slide your feet from side to side to minimize their shot opportunities, and keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.\", \"Answer: To guard a tall person in basketball, stay close to them near the three-point line, actively slide your feet side to side to minimize shot opportunities, and keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.\", \"Answer: To guard a tall person in basketball, stay as close as possible to them near the three-point line and actively slide your feet from side to side to minimize their shot opportunities. Additionally, keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.\"]", "time_sec": 20.147, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.52, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
