{"id": "695", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, you start by stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until the mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Next, transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mix thoroughly, for at least 2 hours. Once chilled, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "pred": "To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, heating just until the mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then, pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer’s directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. The recipe makes one quart of ice cream.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, heating just until the mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then, pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer’s directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. The recipe makes one quart of ice cream.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, heating just until the mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then, pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer’s directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. The recipe makes one quart of ice cream.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, heating just until the mixture is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge, then transfer it to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract before chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker, churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes, and when the ice cream is softly frozen, either serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved and the mixture is hot with a small ring of foam appearing around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract, then chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. This process yields one quart of ice cream, and doubling the recipe will make more. Cream-based ice cream is lighter and icier than custard-based ice cream.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, first, pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze it to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. Alternatively, you can stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mix until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge, then transfer it to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours before churning.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, start by mixing sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, then heat until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Once chilled, pour the mix into an ice cream maker, turn it on, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes until it is softly frozen. Serve immediately or cover with plastic wrap and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to ripen. This process yields one quart of ice cream, and the base can be doubled for more.\"]", "time_sec": 55.303, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 80.49, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "696", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for about 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and put it in the freezer for 2 to 3 hours to ripen.", "pred": "Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place plastic wrap on the surface and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to ripen. Alternatively, stir sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until sugar dissolves and the mixture is hot with a small ring of foam around the edge. Transfer to a container, stir in vanilla extract, chill thoroughly for at least 2 hours, then churn in an ice cream maker.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place plastic wrap on the surface and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to ripen. Alternatively, stir sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until sugar dissolves and the mixture is hot with a small ring of foam around the edge. Transfer to a container, stir in vanilla extract, chill thoroughly for at least 2 hours, then churn in an ice cream maker.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place plastic wrap on the surface and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to ripen. Alternatively, stir sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until sugar dissolves and the mixture is hot with a small ring of foam around the edge. Transfer to a container, stir in vanilla extract, chill thoroughly for at least 2 hours, then churn in an ice cream maker.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, you can follow these steps based on the passages:  \\n1. **Prepare the base**: In a saucepan, stir sugar, cream, and milk over low heat until the sugar dissolves (passage 2, step 1). Heat until the mixture is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge (passage 2, step 2). Transfer the mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract (passage 2, step 3). Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours (passage 2, step 4).  \\n2. **Churn the ice cream**: Pour the chilled mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes (passage 1, step 1).  \\n3. **Set and serve**: When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or cover it with plastic wrap and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to ripen (passage 1, step 2).  \\n\\nNote: This recipe yields one quart of ice cream (passage 3). While passage 3 mentions that cream-based ice cream is icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream, the specific steps for making the base (e.g., custard vs. cream-based) are not detailed in the passages, so the above steps reflect the general process described.\", \"Answer: Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place plastic wrap directly on it and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. Alternatively, stir sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, heat until a small ring of foam appears, transfer to a container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill the mix for at least 2 hours before churning.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, first, pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes according to the manufacturer's directions. When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can either serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and put it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. Alternatively, you can stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge, then transfer it to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mix thoroughly, at least for 2 hours. Finally, mix your base, keeping in mind that cream-based ice cream is icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream, and this recipe will make one quart of ice cream, so double it if you want more.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, then heat until the mixture is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour the chilled mix into an ice cream maker, churn for 20 to 25 minutes according to the manufacturer's directions. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or cover with plastic wrap and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to ripen. The recipe yields one quart of ice cream, which can be doubled for more.\"]", "time_sec": 66.11, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 79.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "697", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to manufacturer's instructions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. For a creamy and flavorful base, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly before using it as a base for your desired ice cream flavor.", "pred": "To make ice cream, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To make ice cream, follow these steps:  \n1. **Prepare the base**: Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves (Passage 2, Step 1). Heat until the mixture is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.  \n2. **Chill thoroughly**: Transfer the mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill for at least 2 hours (Passage 2, Step 4).  \n3. **Churn**: Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes (Passage 1, Step 1).  \n4. **Freeze or ripen**: When softly frozen, serve immediately or cover with plastic wrap and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to ripen (Passage 1, Step 2).  \n5. **Base note**: The recipe yields one quart of ice cream; double for more (Passage 3).  \n\nAnswer: To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk over low heat until sugar dissolves, heat until a small ring of foam appears, transfer to a container, stir in vanilla, chill for 2 hours, churn in an ice cream maker for 20–25 minutes, then serve immediately or freeze 2–3 hours with plastic wrap.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To make ice cream, follow these steps:  \\n1. **Prepare the base**: Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves (Passage 2, Step 1). Heat until the mixture is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.  \\n2. **Chill thoroughly**: Transfer the mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill for at least 2 hours (Passage 2, Step 4).  \\n3. **Churn**: Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes (Passage 1, Step 1).  \\n4. **Freeze or ripen**: When softly frozen, serve immediately or cover with plastic wrap and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to ripen (Passage 1, Step 2).  \\n5. **Base note**: The recipe yields one quart of ice cream; double for more (Passage 3).  \\n\\nAnswer: To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk over low heat until sugar dissolves, heat until a small ring of foam appears, transfer to a container, stir in vanilla, chill for 2 hours, churn in an ice cream maker for 20–25 minutes, then serve immediately or freeze 2–3 hours with plastic wrap.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, start by stirring sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves and the mixture is hot with a small ring of foam around the edge, then transfer it to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract before chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Once chilled, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes until softly frozen. Serve immediately or cover the ice cream with plastic wrap and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to ripen. This process yields one quart of ice cream, which can be doubled for a larger quantity.\", \"Answer: You make ice cream by first preparing the base: stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, then heat until hot with a small ring of foam, transfer to a container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill for at least 2 hours. Then, pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, churn for 20 to 25 minutes, and either serve immediately when softly frozen or place plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, start by stirring sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture just until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge, then transfer it to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. This process yields one quart of ice cream, which can be doubled for a larger batch.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, follow these steps:  \\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar dissolves (passage 2, step 1).  \\n2. Heat the mixture just until hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge (passage 2, step 2).  \\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract (passage 2, step 3).  \\n4. Chill the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours (passage 2, step 4).  \\n5. Pour the chilled mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes (passage 1, step 1).  \\n6. When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (passage 1, step 2).  \\n7. Note: The recipe makes one quart of ice cream (passage 3).\"]", "time_sec": 70.399, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "698", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\nPassage 1 provides instructions for making ice cream using an ice cream maker. To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes). Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nPassage 2 provides a recipe for making ice cream from scratch. To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Then, heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n\nPassage 3 provides general instructions for making ice cream bases. To make ice cream, you will need to start with a good vanilla ice cream base. This type of base is made with cream rather than custard, and it results in a lighter and less icy texture. To make one quart of ice cream, you will need to double the recipe.\n\nTherefore, to summarize:\n\nTo make ice cream using an ice cream maker:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker and turn on the machine.\n2. Churn the ice cream according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes).\n3. Serve the ice cream immediately or place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nTo make ice cream from scratch:\n\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved.\n2. Heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges.\n3. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract.\n4. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n", "pred": "To make ice cream, you can follow these steps based on the passages:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To make ice cream, you can follow these steps based on the passages:  \n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes (Passage 1).  \n2. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (Passage 1).  \n3. Alternatively, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, heat until a small ring of foam appears around the edge, transfer to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours (Passage 2).  \n4. Mix the base, noting that cream-based ice cream is icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream, and the recipe yields one quart of ice cream (Passage 3).  \n\nAnswer: To make ice cream, pour cold mix into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes, then either serve immediately or freeze with plastic wrap for 2 to 3 hours; alternatively, heat sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves and foam forms, chill the mixture for at least 2 hours, and churn.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To make ice cream, you can follow these steps based on the passages:  \\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes (Passage 1).  \\n2. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (Passage 1).  \\n3. Alternatively, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, heat until a small ring of foam appears around the edge, transfer to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours (Passage 2).  \\n4. Mix the base, noting that cream-based ice cream is icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream, and the recipe yields one quart of ice cream (Passage 3).  \\n\\nAnswer: To make ice cream, pour cold mix into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes, then either serve immediately or freeze with plastic wrap for 2 to 3 hours; alternatively, heat sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves and foam forms, chill the mixture for at least 2 hours, and churn.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, first, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, heating just until the mixture is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract, then chill the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn it on, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and put it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. This process yields one quart of ice cream, which can be doubled for more.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, start by mixing sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves and the mixture is hot with a small ring of foam forming around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Once chilled, pour the mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or cover with plastic wrap and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. This process yields one quart of ice cream, which can be doubled for more.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, follow these steps based on the passages:  \\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.  \\n2. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.  \\n3. For the base, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar dissolves, heat until a small ring of foam appears around the edge, transfer to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours.  \\n4. Mix the base (e.g., a good vanilla ice cream base) to create one quart of ice cream; double the recipe for more.  \\n\\nAnswer: To make ice cream, pour cold mix into an ice cream maker, churn for 20–25 minutes, then either serve immediately or freeze with plastic wrap on the surface for 2–3 hours. Prepare the base by heating sugar, cream, and milk until sugar dissolves and foam forms, chill for at least 2 hours, then churn.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, then heat until the mixture is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\"]", "time_sec": 73.768, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.53, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "699", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine, following the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n2. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved, then heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge (passage 2).\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract before chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours (passage 2).\n4. Once the ice cream base is ready, pour it into the ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n5. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (passage 1).\n\nNote that the passages do not provide a specific recipe for making ice cream, but rather provide general steps and tips for making ice cream using an ice cream maker.", "pred": "To make ice cream, start by mixing sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves and the mixture is hot with a small ring of foam around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a large measuring cup, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or cover it with plastic wrap and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. This process yields one quart of ice cream, which can be doubled for more.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To make ice cream, start by mixing sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves and the mixture is hot with a small ring of foam around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a large measuring cup, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or cover it with plastic wrap and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. This process yields one quart of ice cream, which can be doubled for more.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To make ice cream, start by mixing sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves and the mixture is hot with a small ring of foam around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a large measuring cup, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or cover it with plastic wrap and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. This process yields one quart of ice cream, which can be doubled for more.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, first pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn for 20 to 25 minutes according to the manufacturer's directions. Alternatively, you can stir sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, heat until the mixture is hot with a small ring of foam around the edge, then transfer it to a container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill for at least 2 hours. After churning, serve immediately or place plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze for 2 to 3 hours to ripen. For a quart of ice cream, use the base recipe and double it if you want more.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, start by stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves (passage 2). Heat the mixture just until hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge, then transfer it to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours (passage 2). Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker, turn it on, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes (passage 1). When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place plastic wrap directly on the surface and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (passage 1). For a basic vanilla base, mix cream-based ingredients (passage 3), noting that this recipe yields one quart of ice cream, so double the recipe for more.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, heating just until the mixture is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge (passage 2). Transfer the mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours (passage 2). Pour the chilled mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes (passage 1). When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (passage 1). Alternatively, start with a good vanilla ice cream base (passage 3), noting that cream-based ice cream is icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream, and the recipe yields one quart of ice cream.\", \"Answer: To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves, then heat until the mixture is hot with a small ring of foam around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour the chilled mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or cover with plastic wrap and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. The recipe makes one quart of ice cream, so double it for more.\"]", "time_sec": 61.04, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.98, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "701", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "gt": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play. It aids in the development of gross motor skills as they engage in activities like running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water from buckets. Water play also facilitates academic learning in areas such as science and math. Children learn about the concept of floating and sinking, and understand that different objects have different buoyancies. In math, they learn about measurement by determining the amount of water that fits into a bucket, and concepts of more and less by comparing water levels in different buckets. Water play also promotes creativity, allowing children to use their imagination.", "pred": "Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts like measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts like measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts like measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play.\", \"Answer: Children learn gross motor skills, such as running through sprinklers or pouring water, academic concepts including science (floating and sinking) and math (measuring water volume), and creativity through imaginative play.\", \"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts such as measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play during water play.\", \"Answer: Children learn gross motor skills, such as running through sprinklers or filling and pouring buckets; academic concepts like science (floating and sinking) and math (measuring water volume); and creativity through imaginative play.\", \"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts like measuring water, and creativity through imagination and pretend play.\"]", "time_sec": 16.982, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "702", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "gt": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers and pouring water. Water play also provides opportunities for academic learning, such as understanding concepts like floating and sinking, measuring water, and comparing quantities. Additionally, water play encourages creativity and imagination as children pretend and engage in imaginative play with water.", "pred": "Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts such as measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts such as measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play during water play.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts such as measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play during water play.\", \"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts like measuring water, and creativity through imaginative play.\", \"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts such as measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play.\", \"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts such as measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play.\", \"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts such as floating and sinking, math concepts like measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play during water play.\"]", "time_sec": 15.483, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.61, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "705", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "gt": "Based on the given passages, children learn the following through water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Running, pouring, and manipulating water helps develop fine and gross motor skills. (Passage 1)\n2. Science concepts: Floating and sinking, measurement, and experimentation with different objects in water. (Passage 1)\n3. Creativity and imagination: Water play encourages children to use their imagination and engage in pretend play. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not mention any other specific academic learning outcomes beyond gross motor skills, science concepts, and creativity.", "pred": "Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts such as measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play, as stated in passage 1.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts such as measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play, as stated in passage 1.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts such as measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play, as stated in passage 1.\", \"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts like measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play.\", \"Answer: Children learn gross motor skills, science concepts about floating and sinking, math concepts about measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play during water play.\", \"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts like floating and sinking, math concepts such as measuring and comparing quantities, and creativity through imaginative play during water play.\", \"Answer: Children learn about gross motor skills, science concepts such as floating and sinking, math concepts like measuring volume, and creativity through imaginative play during water play.\"]", "time_sec": 16.073, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.79, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.3, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "706", "question": "what do the colors of the tennessee flag mean", "gt": "The colors on the Tennessee Flag have significant meanings. The white color symbolizes purity, the blue color stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and the red color represents the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. The three white stars within the blue circle symbolize the three disparate forms of land that divide the state.", "pred": "According to the designer of the Tennessee Flag, the colors have specific meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red signifies the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. These colors are also the national colors of the US.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: According to the designer of the Tennessee Flag, the colors have specific meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red signifies the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. These colors are also the national colors of the US.", "cot": "[\"Answer: According to the designer of the Tennessee Flag, the colors have specific meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red signifies the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. These colors are also the national colors of the US.\", \"Answer: White symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\", \"Answer: According to the designer of the Tennessee Flag, the colors have the following meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red represents the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\", \"Answer: The colors of the Tennessee flag have specific meanings according to the designer: white symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\", \"Answer: According to the designer of the Tennessee Flag, the colors have the following meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\"]", "time_sec": 20.858, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.46, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "709", "question": "what do the colors of the tennessee flag mean", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nThe colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings:\n\n* White represents purity\n* Blue represents patriotism\n* Red represents the willingness to shed blood during warfare\n\nThe three white stars on the flag represent the three grand divisions of Tennessee: East, Middle, and West. The blue field with the white stars is meant to symbolize the three divisions bound together as one.", "pred": "The colors of the Tennessee flag have specific meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red signifies the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. These colors are the national colors of the United States.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The colors of the Tennessee flag have specific meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red signifies the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. These colors are the national colors of the United States.", "cot": "[\"Answer: The colors of the Tennessee flag have specific meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red signifies the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. These colors are the national colors of the United States.\", \"Answer: The colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red signifies the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\", \"Answer: White symbolizes purity, blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\", \"Answer: According to the designer of the Tennessee Flag, the colors have the following meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red represents the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\", \"Answer: The colors of the Tennessee flag have specific meanings according to the designer. White symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red signifies the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. These colors are the national colors of the US and are extremely significant on the flag.\"]", "time_sec": 21.171, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.1, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "710", "question": "what do the colors of the tennessee flag mean", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the colors of the Tennessee flag are said to have the following meanings:\n\n* White: Purity\n* Red: Readiness to shed blood during warfare\n* Blue: Patriotism of the people of Tennessee\n\nTherefore, the colors of the Tennessee flag are meant to symbolize the state's patriotism, willingness to defend itself, and purity.", "pred": "According to the designer of the Tennessee Flag, the colors have specific meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: According to the designer of the Tennessee Flag, the colors have specific meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.", "cot": "[\"Answer: According to the designer of the Tennessee Flag, the colors have specific meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\", \"Answer: The colors of the Tennessee flag have specific meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\", \"Answer: According to the designer of the Tennessee Flag, the colors have specific meanings: white symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. These are the national colors of the US, and their significance is explicitly stated in the passage.\", \"Answer: White symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red signifies the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\", \"Answer: The colors of the Tennessee flag have specific meanings according to the designer. White symbolizes purity, blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red represents the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.\"]", "time_sec": 20.921, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "712", "question": "what exercises tone the chest", "gt": "Passage 2: The exercises that tone the chest include modified tri-set for the chest, pushups, and dumbbell bench presses.", "pred": "The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest, pushups, and very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest, pushups, and very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.", "cot": "[\"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest, pushups, and very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest and a chest blast that pairs pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses. The specific dumbbell exercise described involves lying on your back with a dumbbell in each hand, extending your arms out to your side, and then curling your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest before slowly returning your arms back to your sides.\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest, as described in the passages, are a modified tri-set for the chest (the first workout) and a combination of pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses (the second chest blast).\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest, as described in the passages, are pushups and heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest, as described in the passages, include a modified tri-set for the chest and a combination of pushups with heavy dumbbell bench presses. Specifically, the first exercise involves lying on your back with dumbbells, extending your arms out to the sides, and then curling your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest before slowly returning your arms to your sides. The second exercise pairs pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.\"]", "time_sec": 25.534, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 81.48, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "715", "question": "what exercises tone the chest", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the exercises that tone the chest are:\n\n1. Modified tri-set for the chest (mentioned in passage 2)\n2. Pushups with heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses (mentioned in passage 2)\n\nThese exercises are designed to pump the pecs and stretch the connective tissue surrounding them, allowing for more muscle growth.", "pred": "The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest, which is designed to pump the pecs and stretch the connective tissue surrounding them, and a combination of pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest, which is designed to pump the pecs and stretch the connective tissue surrounding them, and a combination of pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.", "cot": "[\"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest, which is designed to pump the pecs and stretch the connective tissue surrounding them, and a combination of pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest, as described in the passages, are pushups paired with heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest and a combination of pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses. The dumbbell bench press exercise involves lying on your back with a dumbbell in each hand, extending your arms out to your side, and then slowly curling your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest, before slowly returning your arms back to your sides.\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest, which is designed to pump the pecs and stretch the connective tissue surrounding them, and a combination of pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses. The specific dumbbell exercise involves laying on your back with a dumbbell in each hand, extending your arms out to your side, and then slowly curling your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest before returning your arms back to your sides.\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest, as described in the passages, include a modified tri-set for the chest and a chest blast combining pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses. The specific dumbbell exercise involves lying on your back with a dumbbell in each hand, extending your arms out to your sides, curling your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest, and then slowly returning your arms back to your sides. These exercises are part of The Anarchy Workout, a 6-week high-intensity interval training program designed to build lean muscle and transform the body.\"]", "time_sec": 32.548, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.8, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "716", "question": "what exercises tone the chest", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, the following exercises are mentioned as toning the chest:\n\n* Modified tri-set for the chest (not specified)\n* Pushups\n* Dumbbell bench presses\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What exercises tone the chest?\" based on the given passages is:\n\nModified tri-set for the chest, pushups, and dumbbell bench presses.", "pred": "The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest, which is designed to pump the pecs and stretch the connective tissue, and a combination of pushups with heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses. The specific dumbbell exercise involves lying on your back with a dumbbell in each hand, extending your arms out to your side, curling your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest, and then slowly returning your arms back to your sides.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest, which is designed to pump the pecs and stretch the connective tissue, and a combination of pushups with heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses. The specific dumbbell exercise involves lying on your back with a dumbbell in each hand, extending your arms out to your side, curling your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest, and then slowly returning your arms back to your sides.", "cot": "[\"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest, which is designed to pump the pecs and stretch the connective tissue, and a combination of pushups with heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses. The specific dumbbell exercise involves lying on your back with a dumbbell in each hand, extending your arms out to your side, curling your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest, and then slowly returning your arms back to your sides.\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest, as described in the passage, are pushups paired with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses and a modified tri-set for the chest. The modified tri-set involves laying on your back with dumbbells, extending your arms out to your sides, curling your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest, and then slowly returning your arms back to your sides.\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest include a modified tri-set for the chest, which is designed to pump the pecs and stretch the connective tissue surrounding them, and a combination of pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses. To perform the dumbbell bench press exercise, you lay on your back with a dumbbell in each hand, extend your arms out to your side as if forming a cross, slowly curl your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest, and then slowly return your arms back to your sides.\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest, as described in the passages, are a modified tri-set for the chest (which pumps the pecs and stretches the connective tissue) and a combination of pushups with heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.\", \"Answer: The exercises that tone the chest, as described in the passages, are a modified tri-set for the chest and a combination of pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses. The modified tri-set involves laying on your back with a dumbbell in each hand, extending your arms out to your side, and then slowly curling your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest before slowly returning your arms back to your sides. The second chest exercise is done by pairing pushups with very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses.\"]", "time_sec": 37.563, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 27.27, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "717", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, first, bring a large pot of water to a boil. Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod, then crack an egg and gently slide it into the PoachPod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the PoachPod in the boiling water, ensuring it remains upright and no water gets inside. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for about six minutes. After cooking, use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water. Finally, flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate. The PoachPod can be cleaned in a dishwasher.", "pred": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk. Carefully float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and lift the pod out of the water using a large slotted spoon or tongs. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk. Carefully float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and lift the pod out of the water using a large slotted spoon or tongs. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk. Carefully float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and lift the pod out of the water using a large slotted spoon or tongs. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg.\", \"Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil (or use simmering water as per some instructions). Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk. Lightly oil the pod before adding the egg, as instructed in some passages. Carefully float the pod upright in the boiling/simmering water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and cook for 4-6 minutes, as recommended in the instructions. After cooking, remove the pod using a large slotted spoon or tongs, flip it upside down over a plate, and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg. The PoachPod® is then easy to clean, as it can be placed in the dishwasher.\", \"Answer: Bring a large pot of water to a boil, crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, making sure not to break the yolk. Carefully float the pod upright in the boiling water, ensuring no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. Then, remove the lid and lift the pod out of the water using a large slotted spoon or tongs. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\", \"Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk. Carefully float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. Remove the lid and lift the pod out of the water with a large slotted spoon or tongs. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\", \"Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk. Float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the water. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg onto the plate. Finally, clean the pod by placing it in the dishwasher.\"]", "time_sec": 54.14, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 70.83, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "719", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n\n1. Begin by bringing a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Gently slide an egg into your silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring that the pod stays upright and no water gets inside.\n4. Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and allow the egg to cook for 6 minutes.\n5. After 6 minutes, remove the lid from the pot and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to carefully lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "pred": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed-shaped poached egg. For easy cleanup, place the pod in the dishwasher.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed-shaped poached egg. For easy cleanup, place the pod in the dishwasher.", "cot": "[\"Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed-shaped poached egg. For easy cleanup, place the pod in the dishwasher.\", \"Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, bring a large pot of water to a boil (as stated in passage 2). Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, ensuring the yolk remains intact (passage 2). Carefully float the pod in the boiling water, keeping it upright and preventing water from entering the pod (passage 2). Cover the pot with a lid and cook for six minutes (passage 2), or for about 4-6 minutes as mentioned in passage 3 (though passage 2 specifies six minutes). Remove the lid, then lift the pod out with a large slotted spoon or tongs (passage 2). Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg (passage 2). Note that passage 1 mentions flipping the pod inside out after cooking to release the egg, which aligns with the described steps. Passage 3 adds that lightly oiling the pod before adding the egg is recommended, though passage 2 does not specify this step. The key steps are boiling water, sliding the egg into the pod, floating it in the water, covering and cooking for 4-6 minutes (with passage 2 specifying six minutes), and flipping to release.\", \"Answer:To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk. Carefully float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. Remove the lid, then use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the water. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg.\", \"Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, bring a large pot of water to a boil (or simmering water, as noted in some instructions). Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the pod upright in the water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and cook for 4–6 minutes (as specified in passage 3) or six minutes (as stated in passage 2). Remove the pod with a slotted spoon or tongs, flip it upside down over a plate, and gently press the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg. Specific details include using a nonstick pod that can be cleaned in a dishwasher (passage 1), lightly oiling the pod before use (passage 3), and avoiding water entry into the pod during cooking (passage 2).\", \"Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, bring a large pot of water to a boil, crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod while being careful not to break the yolk. Carefully float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and cook for six minutes. Remove the lid, then use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the water. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg.\"]", "time_sec": 66.247, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": 