{"id": "731", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that the breathing process involves the contraction and relaxation of various muscles, including the diaphragm muscle, to move air in and out of the lungs. This process involves an exchange of gases between the body and the external environment, specifically oxygen and carbon dioxide. Increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity by contracting the muscles involved in breathing draws air into the lungs, causing them to expand and decreasing air pressure below atmospheric pressure. Therefore, the passage does not mention any specific step involved in processing air before it reaches the lungs.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 7.315, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 8.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "732", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the process of processing the air we breathe before it reaches the lungs involves the following steps:\n\n1. The diaphragm muscle contracts to take air into the lungs, moving down from the bottom of the rib cage towards the abdominal region. (Passage 1)\n2. The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases between the body and the outside environment, occurring in the lungs. (Passage 2)\n3. Increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity, including the lungs, decreases the air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure, forcing air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing us to inhale. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the main steps in processing the air we breathe before it reaches the lungs are:\n\n1. Contraction of the diaphragm muscle to draw air into the lungs.\n2. Exchange of gases between the body and the outside environment in the lungs.\n3. Expansion of the thoracic cavity to decrease air pressure in the lungs and facilitate inhalation.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 7.454, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 8.47, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "733", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how the air you breathe is processed before it reaches your lungs:\n\nWhen you inhale, the diaphragm muscle contracts, moving down from the bottom of your rib cage towards your abdominal region, which causes the thoracic cavity to increase in volume. This decrease in air pressure in the lungs below atmospheric pressure forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing you to inhale.\n\nTherefore, the air you breathe is processed by the diaphragm muscle before it reaches your lungs, which contracts to take air into the lungs and relax to let it out again. Additionally, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, such as oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment, which occurs in the lungs.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: The passages do not provide information on how air is processed before it reaches the lungs. They describe the mechanics of breathing (e.g., diaphragm movement, thoracic cavity volume changes) but do not mention any processing of air (such as filtering, warming, or humidifying) prior to lung entry. Therefore, the answer is: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 12.075, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.59, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "735", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "SMS stands for Short Message Service, commonly referred to as a text message, and allows you to send a text message of up to 160 characters to another device. MMS, which stands for Multimedia Messaging Service, is an evolution of SMS. It allows you to send messages that include pictures, video, or audio content to another device. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB. SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, whereas MMS allows a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.", "pred": "SMS (Short Message Service) is limited to sending text-only messages of up to 160 characters, with longer messages split into multiple parts. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending pictures, video, audio, or any combination of text and media, with content size up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, or GIF. SMS is restricted to text-only communication between mobile phones via a service provider, while MMS supports multimedia content sharing.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is limited to sending text-only messages of up to 160 characters, with longer messages split into multiple parts. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending pictures, video, audio, or any combination of text and media, with content size up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, or GIF. SMS is restricted to text-only communication between mobile phones via a service provider, while MMS supports multimedia content sharing.", "cot": "[\"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is limited to sending text-only messages of up to 160 characters, with longer messages split into multiple parts. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending pictures, video, audio, or any combination of text and media, with content size up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, or GIF. SMS is restricted to text-only communication between mobile phones via a service provider, while MMS supports multimedia content sharing.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) only allows sending text messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending text along with pictures, videos, audio, or any combination of these media. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and are text-only, whereas MMS messages can carry up to 300KB of content in formats like WAV, JPEG, or GIF.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these, with content size up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these, with a content size up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is limited to sending text-only messages of up to 160 characters, which are automatically split into multiple parts if longer. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending pictures, video, audio, or any combination of these media, with a larger content size (up to 300KB) in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.\"]", "time_sec": 33.08, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.91, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "736", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text-only messages of up to 160 characters, while MMS allows you to send messages with pictures, sounds, videos, and text, with a larger content size of up to 300KB.", "pred": "SMS only allows sending text messages, while MMS allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these, with MMS supporting larger content sizes up to 300KB.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: SMS only allows sending text messages, while MMS allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these, with MMS supporting larger content sizes up to 300KB.", "cot": "[\"Answer: SMS only allows sending text messages, while MMS allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these, with MMS supporting larger content sizes up to 300KB.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is a text-only messaging service that allows sending messages of up to 160 characters, which are automatically split into multiple parts if longer, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending pictures, videos, audio, or any combination of these along with text, with content size up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, or GIF.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is limited to sending text-only messages of up to 160 characters, which are automatically split into multiple parts if longer, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending text along with pictures, video, audio, or any combination of these, with content size up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, or GIF.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and are split into multiple parts if longer, whereas MMS messages can carry larger content sizes (up to 300KB) including media files like JPEG, GIF, and WAV.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) only allows sending text messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these, with content size up to 300KB.\"]", "time_sec": 29.556, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "737", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "Based on the given passages, SMS stands for Short Message Service and allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send a message including pictures, videos, sounds, text, or any combination of the four. The content of an MMS message has a maximum size of 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.", "pred": "SMS (Short Message Service) is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these, with content size up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these, with content size up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.", "cot": "[\"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these, with content size up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is limited to sending text-only messages with a maximum of 160 characters per message, which may be split into multiple parts if longer. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending text along with pictures, videos, audio, or any combination of these media, with content sizes up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, or GIF.\", \"Answer: SMS only allows sending text messages, while MMS allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these, with content size up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, or GIF.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is limited to sending text-only messages of up to 160 characters, which are automatically split into multiple parts if longer. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending text along with pictures, videos, audio, or any combination of these, with content sizes up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, or GIF.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and are automatically split into multiple parts if longer, whereas MMS messages can carry content up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.\"]", "time_sec": 30.859, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "739", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "Sure! Here's my answer based on the given passages:\n\nThe main difference between SMS (Short Message Service) and MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is that SMS is limited to sending text-only messages, while MMS allows for sending multimedia content such as images, videos, and audio files, in addition to text.\n\nAccording to passage 1, SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts if they are longer. MMS messages, on the other hand, can carry a larger size of content, including pictures, videos, and audio files, with a maximum size of 300KB.\n\nPassage 2 explains that SMS is a premium service offered by mobile companies, while passage 3 highlights the differences between SMS and MMS, stating that SMS only allows for text, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n\nTherefore, the key differences between SMS and MMS are:\n\n* SMS is limited to text-only messages, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n* SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts, while MMS messages can carry a larger size of content.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "SMS only allows sending text messages (up to 160 characters per message, split into multiple parts if longer), while MMS allows sending multimedia content including pictures, videos, audio, and text (or any combination), with messages capable of carrying up to 300KB of content in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_sc_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: SMS only allows sending text messages (up to 160 characters per message, split into multiple parts if longer), while MMS allows sending multimedia content including pictures, videos, audio, and text (or any combination), with messages capable of carrying up to 300KB of content in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.", "cot": "[\"Answer: SMS only allows sending text messages (up to 160 characters per message, split into multiple parts if longer), while MMS allows sending multimedia content including pictures, videos, audio, and text (or any combination), with messages capable of carrying up to 300KB of content in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is a text-only messaging service that allows sending messages of up to 160 characters, which are automatically split into multiple parts if longer. It is restricted to text-only and is supported by most cell phones. MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that allows sending pictures, video, audio, or any combination of these with text. MMS supports larger content sizes (up to 300KB) and includes formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. Unlike SMS, MMS can include multimedia content beyond text.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is a text-only messaging service that allows sending messages of up to 160 characters, which are automatically split into multiple parts if longer. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS that enables sending pictures, videos, audio, or any combination of these with text. MMS supports larger content sizes (up to 300KB) and various file types like WAV, JPEG, and GIF, while SMS is restricted to text-only messages.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these four types of content.\", \"Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) only allows sending text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these four types of content. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and are automatically split into multiple parts if longer, whereas MMS messages can carry larger content sizes (up to 300KB) and support multimedia formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.\"]", "time_sec": 35.606, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code", "method": "sc", "num_rollout": 5, "temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
